	(259, 3, NULL, 'introduce me N Seoul Tower at Night', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-07 13:24:49'),
	(260, 3, NULL, 'tellme introduce top 10 place inseoul', 'Seoul Plaza refers to the square located in front of Seoul City Hall, which used to be widely used as a location for public rallies, protests, and events. In 2002 the roadway was completely transformed and grassed over, and the current lively Seoul Plaza with its artwork and culture was inaugurated in 2004. The plaza features a refreshing fountain in the summer and an outdoor ice rink in the winter.', '2025-11-07 19:23:17'),
	(261, 3, NULL, 'Namsan Seoul Tower', '**Namsan Seoul Tower** is a prominent landmark located at 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, Korea. The tower stands at 236.7 meters tall and is situated at the summit of Namsan Mountain, which is 262 meters high, offering an exceptional 360-degree panoramic view of Seoul from an elevation of 480 meters above sea level. \n\nThe tower is open 365 days a year, with operating hours from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM on weekdays and until 11:00 PM on weekends. The last entry is allowed 30 minutes before closing time. It is a popular destination for couples, featuring attractions like the "Locks of Love" and "Heart Chair." \n\nVisitors can enjoy various facilities at Namsan Seoul Tower, including an observation deck, restaurants, cafes, and attractions within the Lower Seoul Tower Plaza, such as Gallery K and the Bodyfriend Lounge.\n\nRegarding pets, they are not allowed in Namsan Seoul Tower. If you wish to visit the tower using the cable car, it operates from 10:00 AM to 11:00 PM, with round-trip fares of 15,000 KRW for adults and 11,500 KRW for children. \n\nFor more information or to plan your visit, you can find details on the official website or at the ticket counter.', '2025-11-07 19:26:59'),
	(262, 3, NULL, 'introduce Namsan Seoul Tower', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-07 19:27:15'),
	(263, 3, NULL, 'Namsan Seoul Tower', '**Question:** Can I visit Namsan Seoul Tower on national holidays or regular holidays?\n\n**Answer:** Yes, the Namsan Seoul Tower is open 365 days a year, including national and regular holidays.', '2025-11-07 19:28:42'),
	(264, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce Namsan Seoul Tower', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-07 19:29:03'),
	(265, 3, NULL, 'Namsan Seoul Tower', 'Sure! Here are answers to the questions based on the provided information about Namsan Seoul Tower:\n\n1. **Can I visit Namsan Seoul Tower on national holidays or regular holidays?**\n   - Yes, the Namsan Seoul Tower is open 365 days a year.\n\n2. **Can I visit Namsan Seoul Tower with my pet?**\n   - No, pets are not allowed at the Namsan Seoul Tower.\n\n3. **What are the operating hours of the Namsan Seoul Tower Cable Car and how much is it?**\n   - The Namsan Seoul Tower Cable Car operates from 10 am to 11 pm. The ticket prices are as follows:\n      - Round-trip fare: Adults 15,000 KRW / Children 11,500 KRW\n      - One-way fare: Adults 12,000 KRW / Children 9,000 KRW\n      - (Children are considered to be from 36 months to elementary school students.) \n\nIf you have any more questions or need further information, feel free to ask!', '2025-11-07 19:29:28'),
	(266, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-07 19:30:38'),
	(267, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce N Seoul Tower at Night ', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-07 19:30:48'),
	(268, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce National Assembly Building', 'The National Assembly Building houses Korea\'s legislative branch of government and it is located in Yeouido. The building represents the democracy and human rights of Korea. The National Assembly Library is located to the right of the main building, and the Assembly Members??Office Building is located to the left. Free tours of the National Assembly are available, but reservations are required. Visitors must reserve a tour date at least three days in advance of the desired visit date.', '2025-11-07 19:31:08'),
	(269, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce Changsin-dong\'s Cliff Village', '.se-contents .se-scrollbox{overflow-x: auto; -ms-overflow-style: none; scrollbar-width: none;}.se-contents .se-scrollbox::-webkit-scrollbar{display: none;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image .se-caption{max-width: 100% !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image, .se-contents .se-responsive.se-video{max-width: 100%; height: auto !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image > img, .se-contents .se-responsive.se-video > *{max-width: 100%; min-width: 10px; height: auto !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-video .se-video-wrapper{position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; display: block;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-video .se-video-wrapper > iframe{width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; position: absolute; left: 0px}Changsin-dong Cliff Village, located in Changsin 1, 2, and 3-dong in Dongdaemun-gu, Seoul, has undergone various transformations over the years. It was a quarry village in the 1960s, a wooden village in the 1970s, a sewing factory in the 1990s, and finally a sewing village in the 2000s. It is situated around the rocky cliffs once used as the nation\'s only quarry. Changsin-dong Cliff Village is divided into densely packed, dilapidated, aged homes built on cliffs and precipices and homes formed beneath rocky hills.*Please Note: When visiting, please refrain from making excessive noise, as actual residents live there.', '2025-11-07 19:31:44'),
	(270, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce King Taejo of the Joseon Dynasty moved the capital to Hanyang in 1394 and built Gyeongbokgung Palace, the official residence of the Joseon Dynasty. In addition, on both sides of the road in front of the palace??s main gate, the Street of Six Ministries, including Uijeongbu (State Council), was built. It was the best road in Hanyang. In 2009, that road opened again. Gwanghwamun Square and Cheonggye Plaza were built. The square is mostly ??a square that restores the history of Gwanghwamun,????a square that recreates the scenery of the Street of the Six Ministries,????an emblematic square of Korea,????an urban culture square where citizens mingle,????a square in the city center,??and ??a connection to the Cheonggyecheon Stream.??It functions as a space for history, culture, and relaxation. The focal point of this emblematic square in Korea is the statue of King Sejong the Great. The ??downtown square??around the statue of Admiral Yi Sun-sin is also a space appreciated by city dwellers. In addition, artificial ponds and fountains are installed to cool off people from the summer heat. Also, the Haechi statue and Grass Plaza, which are symbols of Seoul, were also created.', 'King Taejo of the Joseon Dynasty moved the capital to Hanyang in 1394 and built Gyeongbokgung Palace, the official residence of the Joseon Dynasty. In addition, on both sides of the road in front of the palace?셲 main gate, the Street of Six Ministries, including Uijeongbu (State Council), was built. It was the best road in Hanyang. In 2009, that road opened again. Gwanghwamun Square and Cheonggye Plaza were built. The square is mostly ?  square that restores the history of Gwanghwamun,???  square that recreates the scenery of the Street of the Six Ministries,??? n emblematic square of Korea,??? n urban culture square where citizens mingle,???  square in the city center,??and ?  connection to the Cheonggyecheon Stream.??It functions as a space for history, culture, and relaxation. The focal point of this emblematic square in Korea is the statue of King Sejong the Great. The ?쐂owntown square??around the statue of Admiral Yi Sun-sin is also a space appreciated by city dwellers. In addition, artificial ponds and fountains are installed to cool off people from the summer heat. Also, the Haechi statue and Grass Plaza, which are symbols of Seoul, were also created.', '2025-11-07 19:32:51'),
	(271, 3, NULL, 'let me intro duce Gwanghwamun Square', '**Gwanghwamun Square** is a prominent urban space located in Seoul, South Korea. Situated at **175 Sejong-daero, Jongno-gu**, this square is accessible 24 hours a day, year-round. It holds significant historical importance as it was established in front of Gyeongbokgung Palace, which was built in 1394 when King Taejo of the Joseon Dynasty moved the capital to Hanyang (now Seoul). \n\nThe square is designed to evoke the history of Gwanghwamun and recreate the scenery of the historical Street of Six Ministries. It serves as a central gathering place for citizens, blending history, culture, and relaxation. Notable features of Gwanghwamun Square include the statue of **King Sejong the Great**, a celebrated figure in Korean history, and the statue of **Admiral Yi Sun-sin**. The square also features artificial ponds and fountains, providing a refreshing escape from the summer heat. Additionally, the **Haechi statue** and **Grass Plaza** serve as symbols of the city, enhancing its cultural significance.', '2025-11-07 19:33:42'),
	(272, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce Gwanghwamun Square', 'Gwanghwamun Square is located on Sejong-ro in Jongno-gu and is vast in size. Gwanghwamun Square stretches out from Gwanghwamun Gate, towards Cheonggyecheon Stream, and is divided into 6 sections: ?쏳ecovering the History of Gwanghwamun Gate Plaza,???쏳eenacting Yukjo Street Plaza,???쏫orea Main Plaza,???쏞ivil Participation Urban Culture Plaza,???쏡owntown Plaza??and ?쏞heonggyecheon Stream Connector.?씲졖?      The focal point of the square is the statue of King Sejong the Great. During the day, the square is always busy with people but at night it is a tranquil and beautiful tourist attraction. Gwanghwamun Square, with Inwangsan Mountain just behind it, is not just a beautiful tourist locale. The square has over 600 years of history and it is a place where the spirit of the Korean nation can be felt.      For more information:    Gwanghwamun Square       The Story of King Sejong ??The Story of Admiral Yi   Sunshin', '2025-11-07 19:33:58'),
	(273, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce Gwanghwamun Square', 'Gwanghwamun Square is located on Sejong-ro in Jongno-gu and is vast in size. Gwanghwamun Square stretches out from Gwanghwamun Gate, towards Cheonggyecheon Stream, and is divided into 6 sections: ?쏳ecovering the History of Gwanghwamun Gate Plaza,???쏳eenacting Yukjo Street Plaza,???쏫orea Main Plaza,???쏞ivil Participation Urban Culture Plaza,???쏡owntown Plaza??and ?쏞heonggyecheon Stream Connector.?씲졖?      The focal point of the square is the statue of King Sejong the Great. During the day, the square is always busy with people but at night it is a tranquil and beautiful tourist attraction. Gwanghwamun Square, with Inwangsan Mountain just behind it, is not just a beautiful tourist locale. The square has over 600 years of history and it is a place where the spirit of the Korean nation can be felt.      For more information:    Gwanghwamun Square       The Story of King Sejong ??The Story of Admiral Yi   Sunshin', '2025-11-07 19:42:00'),
	(274, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce Seoul Sky', '.se-contents .se-scrollbox{overflow-x: auto; -ms-overflow-style: none; scrollbar-width: none;}.se-contents .se-scrollbox::-webkit-scrollbar{display: none;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image .se-caption{max-width: 100% !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image, .se-contents .se-responsive.se-video{max-width: 100%; height: auto !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image > img, .se-contents .se-responsive.se-video > *{max-width: 100%; min-width: 10px; height: auto !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-video .se-video-wrapper{position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; display: block;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-video .se-video-wrapper > iframe{width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; position: absolute; left: 0px}Located on the top floor of Lotte World Tower in Jamsil, Seoul Sky (5th highest in the world, 500 M) is the highest point in South Korea that offers a 360-degree view of Seoul?셲 dazzling beauty. From 500 meters in the sky, visitors can admire the city?셲 diverse charms as they change from day to night and throughout the four seasons. Moreover, Seoul Sky also features thrilling experiential attractions, a variety of exhibition content, a caf챕 where visitors can relax with a cup of coffee, and a range of tower-themed souvenirs, making it an ideal spot to create lasting experiences and memories.', '2025-11-07 19:42:51'),
	(275, 3, NULL, 'let me introduco Cheongwadae', 'Cheongwadae, also known as the Blue House, is the official residence of the President of South Korea and has been open to the public since June 2022. Located at 1, Cheongwadae-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, it has become a popular tourist destination. The main building includes the president\'s office, reception rooms, and conference rooms, while additional facilities consist of Chunchugwan (the State Guest House) and a beautiful rear garden.\n\nVisitors can explore the grounds, which typically takes about 1.5 to 2 hours. Cheongwadae is open from March to November from 09:00 to 18:00 (with last entry at 17:00) and from December to February from 09:00 to 17:30 (with last entry at 16:30). It is closed every Tuesday, and tours can be reserved through its official website. Please note that on rainy days, access to certain indoor areas may be limited, and tours may be suspended during natural disasters for safety reasons. \n\nCheongwadae has received positive reviews, with an aggregate rating of 4.0 based on 231 ratings. One visitor, Max Y, praised the site for its beauty and quick-moving lines, suggesting a hike to an observation deck for a stunning view of Seoul.', '2025-11-07 19:43:21'),
	(276, 3, NULL, 'let me introduco Cheongwadae', 'Cheongwadae, also known as the Blue House, is the official residence of the President of South Korea and has been open to the public since June 2022. Located at 1, Cheongwadae-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, it has become a popular tourist destination. The main building houses the president\'s office, reception rooms, and conference rooms, while additional facilities include the State Guest House and a beautiful rear garden.\n\nVisitors can explore the grounds, which include Nokjiwon and Sangchunjae, with tours typically lasting between 1.5 to 2 hours. Cheongwadae is open from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM from March to November, and from 9:00 AM to 5:30 PM from December to February, with specific last entry times. It is closed every Tuesday, and reservations for tours can be made on its official website.\n\nPlease note that on rainy days, access to certain indoor areas may be restricted, and tours may be suspended during natural disasters for safety reasons. Cheongwadae has received positive reviews, with an aggregate rating of 4.0 based on 231 ratings.', '2025-11-07 19:43:56'),
