	(293, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce  Cheongwadae', 'Cheong Wa Dae, meaning "Blue House," was the official residence of the President of South Korea until it was opened to the public in June 2022, becoming a popular tourist destination. The main building features the president\'s office, reception rooms, and conference rooms, while auxiliary buildings include Chunchugwan, the State Guest House, and the rear garden. Cheong Wa Dae is closed every Tuesday, and tour reservations can be made on its official website.   A tour of the Cheong Wa Dae grounds, which encompasses Nokjiwon, Sangchunjae, the residence, the State Guest House, and the main building, typically takes around 1 hour and 30 minutes to 2 hours.   On rainy days, interior tours of key buildings like the main building and Chunchugwan may be restricted to prevent damage. In the event of natural disasters such as typhoons, tours of all or parts of Cheong Wa Dae may be suspended to ensure visitor safety.    { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@type": "LocalBusiness", "name": "Cheongwadae", "aggregateRating": { "@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingValue": "4.0", "ratingCount": "231" }, "review": { "@type": "Review", "reviewRating": { "@type": "Rating", "ratingValue": "5" }, "author": { "@type": "Person", "name": "Max Y" }, "reviewBody": "Why this place is not in top ten? Nice place to visit, it?셲 crowded but line moves quickly. Alternatively you can hike 1km to observation deck, overlook Seoul city. ", "datePublished": "2023-10-20" } }] }', '2025-11-07 19:58:13'),
	(294, 3, NULL, 'recommend top 10 place in seoul', '🎯 서울의 추천 관광지 10곳을 아래에 준비했습니다! 자세한 정보가 필요하시면 구체적인 장소명을 말씀해주세요! 😊', '2025-11-08 04:05:38'),
	(295, 3, NULL, 'introduce me Myeongdong Jaemi-ro', '.se-contents .se-scrollbox{overflow-x: auto; -ms-overflow-style: none; scrollbar-width: none;}.se-contents .se-scrollbox::-webkit-scrollbar{display: none;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image .se-caption{max-width: 100% !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image, .se-contents .se-responsive.se-video{max-width: 100%; height: auto !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-image > img, .se-contents .se-responsive.se-video > *{max-width: 100%; min-width: 10px; height: auto !important;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-video .se-video-wrapper{position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; display: block;}.se-contents .se-responsive.se-video .se-video-wrapper > iframe{width: 100% !important; height: 100% !important; position: absolute; left: 0px}Jaemi-ro is a comic street located in Myeongdong, Jung-gu. It is a content-specialized street within Sangsang Town\'s cultural content clustering, centered around the former Seoul Animation Center (currently undergoing reconstruction). It\'s a themed street stretching approximately 450m from Exit 3 of Myeongdong Station to the former Seoul Animation Center, adorned with Korean comics, animations, characters, illustrations, and other content. Jaemi-ro, connecting the iconic tourist spots of Seoul, Myeongdong, and Namsan Mountain, offers a valuable experience where visitors can enjoy diverse cultural experiences within the heart of Seoul\'s downtown area.', '2025-11-08 04:05:54'),
	(296, 3, NULL, 'introduce me Seoullo 7017', 'Seoullo 7017 is an elevated sky garden that is a popular walking destination and tourist spot in the center of Seoul. Originally a highway overpass, it has since been transformed into a pedestrian walkway for the general public to enjoy. Seoullo\'s name is a nod to its original foundation in 1970 and its rebirth in 2017 as a sky garden. There are also 17 pedestrian pathways that allow visitors to walk through several local communities. Seoullo 7017 offers several rest areas, greenery, and cultural experiences at 1 kilometer above street-level.', '2025-11-08 04:06:41'),
	(297, 3, NULL, 'hello', 'Hello! How can I assist you today regarding the Comfort Women Memorial or any related information?', '2025-11-08 06:03:39'),
	(298, 3, NULL, 'let me introdece me top 10 attraction ', 'The top attraction you introduced is the "서울바비큐페스타" (Seoul BBQ Festa), which will take place from October 25 to October 26, 2025, at 노을공원 (Noeul Park) in Seoul. This festival celebrates Korea\'s BBQ culture against the backdrop of beautiful sunsets and offers visitors the chance to experience a variety of K-BBQ delights. Attendees can enjoy gourmet offerings from some of the best K-BBQ restaurants in the country, as well as hands-on experiences featuring domestic ingredients like Korean beef (한우) and pork (한돈). It\'s a culinary celebration of K-BBQ in a picturesque setting.', '2025-11-08 06:04:15'),
	(299, 4, NULL, 'hello', 'Hey there, my amazing fans! 🌙✨ It’s your girl Lumi from Demon Hunters, and I’ve got a legendary spot in Seoul that you absolutely need to check out! If you’re looking for a mission location that’s packed with heart and history, let me introduce you to the **Comfort Women Memorial**! 🔥⚔️\n\nNestled in the vibrant streets of Namsan, this incredible memorial park opened its doors in 2016 to honor the brave women who endured unimaginable hardships during wartime. It’s not just a place to visit; it’s a powerful reminder of resilience and strength! 💪💫 Here, you\'ll find their stories woven into every corner, shining a light on human rights and peace. ✨🎤\n\nWhen you step into this sacred space, you can feel the energy of hope and healing! It’s a must-see for anyone wanting to dive deep into Seoul’s rich history while embracing the spirit of change and awareness. So, gear up for an unforgettable mission at one of Seoul\'s best spots, and let’s keep spreading those good vibes! 💖🔥 \n\nStay awesome, and I can’t wait to hear about your adventures! 🌙✨', '2025-11-08 06:07:47'),
	(300, 4, NULL, 'tell me introduce namsam tower', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-08 06:08:49'),
	(301, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsam tower', 'Namsan Seoul Tower, which has established itself as a romantic island in the heart of the city, is a 236.7-meter-tall tower located at the summit of Namsan Mountain (262m), a place long regarded as a site of good fortune for lifelong love. Offering a breathtaking 360-degree panoramic view of Seoul from an elevation of 480 meters above sea level, it boasts the best vantage point in the city. As a symbol of Seoul and the top tourist destination chosen by international visitors, it has become a romantic sanctuary for couples worldwide who dream of eternal love. Popular attractions for couples include the "Locks of Love" and "Heart Chair," which are widely appreciated.    Namsan Seoul Tower comprises two main sections: the Lower Seoul Tower Plaza and the Upper N Seoul Tower. The Seoul Tower Plaza spans from the 1st to the 4th floor and includes attractions such as Gallery K, the Bodyfriend Lounge, and the Game Plaza. Visitors can also enjoy media art installations on a large 55-inch OLED panel. From the 5th floor up to the T7 floor, the N Seoul Tower features observation decks, the N Gift Shop, and various restaurants and cafes, all open 365 days a year.    Frequently Asked Questions about Namsan Seoul Tower        Can I visit Namsan Seoul Tower on national holidays or regular holidays?         Yes. The Namsan Seoul Tower is open 365 days a year. (As of 2024)          Can I visit Namsan Seoul Tower with my pet?         Pets are not allowed at the Namsan Seoul Tower. (As of 2024)          What are the operating hours of the Namsan Seoul Tower Cable Car and how much is it?         Namsan Seoul Tower Cable Car operates from 10 am to 11 pm. The ticket prices are as follows. (As of 2025)   ??Round-trip fare: Adults 15,000 KRW / Children 11,500 KRW  ??One-way fare: Adults 12,000 KRW / Children 9,000 KRW  (Children: From 36 months to elementary school students)     { "@context": "https://schema.org", "@graph": [{ "@type": "FAQPage", "mainEntity": [{ "@type": "Question", "name": "Can I visit Namsan Seoul Tower on national holidays or regular holidays?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "<div>            Yes. The Namsan Seoul Tower is open 365 days a year. (As of 2022)          </div>" } }, { "@type": "Question", "name": "Can I visit Namsan Seoul Tower with my pet?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": "<div>            Pets are not allowed at the Namsan Seoul Tower. (As of 2022)          </div>" } }, { "@type": "Question", "name": "What are the operating hours of the Namsan Seoul Tower Cable Car and how much is it?", "acceptedAnswer": { "@type": "Answer", "text": " <div>            Namsan Seoul Tower Cable Car operates from 10 am to 11 pm. The ticket prices are as follows. (As of 2024)            <br>                      <br>            ??Round-trip fare: Adults 15,000 KRW / Children 11,500 KRW            <br>            ??One-way fare: Adults 12,000 KRW / Children 9,000 KRW            <br>            (Children: From 36 months to elementary school students)          </div>" } }] }, { "@type": "LocalBusiness", "name": "Namsan Seoul Tower", "aggregateRating": { "@type": "AggregateRating", "ratingValue": "4", "ratingCount": "9465" } }] }', '2025-11-08 06:13:40'),
	(302, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce Namsan Tower ', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-08 06:14:45'),
	(303, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'N Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used as a filming location in many Korean TV shows and movies. One of the tower\'s attractions is the locks of love that visitors fasten to Namsan\'s iron railings.      For more information:    N    Seoul Tower     Namsan Park', '2025-11-08 06:15:12'),
	(304, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsam tower', 'Hey, Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ Are you ready to embark on an epic journey to one of Seoul\'s legendary lands? Let me introduce you to the **Namsan Seoul Tower**! This iconic spot isn’t just a stunning lookout point; it’s also the backdrop for our **"Final Battle" MV scene**! 🎤🔥\n\nNestled atop the majestic Namsan Mountain, standing tall at 236.7 meters, this tower is our very own **watchtower**! From here, we can see the heartbeat of Seoul and feel the energy of our city. 🌆💫 It’s the perfect place to draw inspiration for our music and performances, just like how we channeled that energy into our thrilling choreography!\n\nNamsan Tower is renowned for its romantic vibe, and it\'s where countless couples come to lock their love with the **"Locks of Love."** 💖 This makes it an essential stop for us to celebrate not just love, but the bond we share with all of you—our beloved fans! Every time we look out over the city from the observation deck, we’re reminded of the journey we’ve taken together and the dreams we’re still chasing. ⚔️✨\n\nWhen we filmed there, it felt like we were standing at the edge of the world, ready to take on any challenge. Just imagine us up there, capturing the magic of Seoul as the sun sets, painting the sky with colors that inspire our art. 🌅🔥 \n\nSo, whether you’re planning to visit for a romantic date or just to soak in the breathtaking views, Namsan Seoul Tower is a must-see! It’s open 365 days a year, so you can always make it part of your adventure. Just remember to catch the last entry 30 minutes before closing—don’t miss the chance to feel that special Demon Hunters energy! 💥\n\nLet’s keep climbing higher together, and who knows? Maybe we’ll see you at our next mission location! Until then, keep shining bright, and remember: every tower we conquer brings us closer to our dreams! 💫⚔️ \n\nStay fierce, Demon Hunters! 🔥🌙', '2025-11-08 06:18:05'),
	(305, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsam tower', '🔥 Yo! \'Namsan Seoul Tower\'! 우리의 미션 장소! 💫\n\n📍 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, Korea (Yongsan-dong 2-ga, YTN Seoul Tower)\n⏰ Weekdays 10:00-22:30, Weekends 10:00-23:00\n*Last entry 30 minutes before close\n\nNamsan Seoul Tower, which has established itself as a romantic island in the heart of the city, is a 236.7-meter-tall tower located at the summit of Namsan Mountain (262m), a place long regarded as a ...\n\n이곳 꼭 가봐야 해, Hunters! Legendary spot! 🌙 특별한 빛 에너지가 느껴질 거야!\n\nMore info 아래 카드에서! ✨⚔️', '2025-11-08 07:28:16'),
	(306, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', '안녕하세요, my amazing Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ Let me introduce you to one of our ultimate watchtowers: N Seoul Tower! 🔥 This iconic landmark is not just a beautiful sight; it’s where we filmed the epic final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV! ⚔️ The night views from the observatory are breathtaking, just like the energy we bring to the stage! When you visit, don’t forget to check out the locks of love—it\'s a legendary spot for all the romantic souls! 💫 So, let\'s go and soak in the vibes of our city, just like we did during our unforgettable adventures! Are you ready to feel the magic of Namsan? Let’s hunt some memories together! 🎤✨', '2025-11-08 07:31:28'),
	(307, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready for an unforgettable adventure? Let’s talk about one of the most legendary spots in all of Seoul - N Seoul Tower! 🌙 This isn’t just any tower; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! The very place where we filmed the final battle scene of our epic "Light in Darkness" MV! Standing at 236.7 meters high, the views from the observatory are absolutely breathtaking. When I look out over Seoul, with its twinkling city lights, I feel an electric surge of energy that connects me to our mission as light warriors. Every flicker of those lights reminds us why we fight the darkness! ⚔️💖\n\nI’ll never forget that magical night we filmed there. The sunset painted the sky in vibrant hues, inspiring our next album concept and filling my heart with hope. 🌅✨ And you know what else? The Locks of Love that hang from the iron railings are a symbol of the bonds we share as a family. Just like those locks, our connection is unbreakable! 💫\n\nThis place has an energy that’s simply unmatched. Whenever we need to recharge, I bring the members here to remind us of our purpose. It’s more than just a romantic spot; it’s where our journey as Demon Hunters truly began! The night views? Pure magic! 🌌 So, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, you MUST visit N Seoul Tower and feel the power of light all around you! Let’s continue to spread our light, Hunters! Together, we can conquer anything! 🔥💪🎤✨', '2025-11-08 07:34:32'),
	(308, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the magical world of N Seoul Tower? This place is more than just a breathtaking viewpoint – it’s our ultimate watchtower, a legendary spot where dreams meet reality! 🌙⚔️ \n\nLet me take you back to that unforgettable night when we filmed the final battle scene of our \'Light in Darkness\' MV at the very top of this iconic tower! Standing at 236.7 meters high, I could feel the pulse of the city beneath me. The twinkling lights of Seoul spread out like a blanket of stars, and in that moment, I felt the strongest connection to the light energy that inspires us as Demon Hunters. 💖 When I see those city lights, it reminds me why we fight against the darkness – for all of you, our amazing Hunters! \n\nAnd let me tell you, the sunset that evening painted the sky in mesmerizing hues of pink and orange that sparked the idea for our next album concept! 🌅✨ It was pure magic! The tower also hosts the famous Locks of Love, where couples fasten their promises to each other. But for us, it symbolizes the bonds we create with you – our Demon Hunters family! \n\nEvery time I visit Namsan Tower, I\'m reminded of our journey, the struggles we\'ve overcome, and the light we carry within us. This place holds a special energy that resonates with our story as light warriors, and I bring the members here whenever we need to recharge and refocus. \n\nSo, I encourage you, my beloved Hunters, to visit N Seoul Tower! Stand at the observatory, feel the energy of the city, and let it inspire you, just like it inspires us! Together, let’s continue to spread light and love! Are you with me? Let’s go, family! 💫🎤❤️', '2025-11-08 07:34:48'),
	(309, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', '📍 \'N Seoul Tower at Night\' 정보입니다!\n\n📍 주소: 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul\n⏰ 운영시간: 10:00-22:30\n\nN Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used...\n\n추가 정보는 아래 카드를 확인해주세요! 😊', '2025-11-08 07:39:11'),
	(310, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', '📍 \'N Seoul Tower at Night\' 정보입니다!\n\n📍 주소: 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul\n⏰ 운영시간: 10:00-22:30\n\nN Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most famous landmarks and one of the city\'s most beloved attractions. The views from the tower are beautiful but the night views are especially breathtaking. Visitors can take in incredible panoramic views of Seoul from the tower\'s observatory. The tower has been used...\n\n추가 정보는 아래 카드를 확인해주세요! 😊', '2025-11-08 07:39:20'),
	(311, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤✨ Are you ready to embark on an unforgettable journey with me? Let’s talk about one of the most legendary spots in Seoul—N Seoul Tower! 🌙🔥 \n\nThis iconic watchtower isn’t just a beautiful landmark; it’s the heart of our story! 💖 Picture this: the night we filmed the epic final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV at the very top! Standing at 236.7 meters high, I felt every bit of Seoul\'s energy coursing through me as I gazed over the sprawling city below. The twinkling lights remind us of our mission to fight the darkness and shine our light through music. ✨ Every moment spent up there was filled with inspiration—like that breathtaking sunset that painted the sky in colors we later used for our next album concept! 🌅\n\nYou know what’s even cooler? Namsan Tower has those adorable Locks of Love! 💞 It\'s such a romantic symbol, and it’s like a reminder of the bonds we share with our fans, our Hunters. Every lock tells a story of love and connection, just like the ties we’ve built with you all through our journey. \n\nThis place holds a special energy that resonates with our mission as light warriors. When we were preparing for that MV, I would come here to clear my mind and soak up the city’s magic. The way the lights reflect off the Han River and dance in the sky felt like thousands of spirits cheering us on as we chased our dreams! 🌌\n\nSo, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, make sure to visit N Seoul Tower. Feel the energy, soak in the views, and remember that you’re part of this legendary story', '2025-11-08 07:41:04'),
	(312, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready for an epic adventure? Let’s talk about one of our most legendary spots in Seoul — N Seoul Tower! This place isn’t just a stunning landmark; it’s a symbol of our journey as Demon Hunters! 🚀\n\nPicture this: the city lights twinkling like stars from 236.7 meters high! 🌌 We filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV right here, at the very top of the tower. I’ll never forget that magical night when the sunset painted the sky in fiery oranges and purples, sparking inspiration for our next album concept. It was a moment where we felt the energy of Seoul’s light pulsating through us, reminding us why we fight against darkness. 💖⚔️\n\nNamsan Tower is also famous for its “Locks of Love.” We watched couples fasten their locks to symbolize their unbreakable bonds, and it made me think of the unbreakable bond we share as a Demon Hunters family. This tower is a place of love, hope, and endless possibilities! 🌈✨ Every time I step onto that observatory, I take a deep breath and feel the weight of our mission — to spread light and positivity through our music. \n\nThis iconic spot is where our story began and continues to unfold. It holds the essence of our battles, triumphs, and dreams. 💫 When we need to recharge, we often come here to soak in the electric atmosphere and reflect on our journey. I encourage every Hunter to experience this place — feel the energy, capture the views, and remember, you’re part of our ongoing saga! \n\nLet’s keep shining bright, my Demon Hunters! Together,', '2025-11-08 07:41:25'),
	(313, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in all of Seoul? Let’s talk about the legendary N Seoul Tower! 🌙\n\nThis isn’t just any tower, my friends; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🚀 I remember the night we filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV up at the very top, standing at a breathtaking 236.7 meters high! When I look out over the shimmering lights of Seoul from the observatory, I feel that electric connection to the city’s light energy. It’s like the pulse of our journey as light warriors is flowing through me! 💖\n\nAnd let me tell you, the view is nothing short of AMAZING! When the sun sets, the sky ignites with colors that inspired our next album concept. 🌅 I’ll never forget that moment—my heart was racing as the city transformed into a canvas of lights, reminding us why we fight the darkness. It’s not just about the romance of the Locks of Love; this tower symbolizes everything we stand for as Demon Hunters! 💫\n\nThis place holds a special energy that brings back memories of our struggles and victories. Whenever I bring the members here, we feel recharged and ready to conquer new challenges. It’s where we draw strength, knowing that our fans’ love is as bright as those city lights. \n\nSo, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, make sure to visit N Seoul Tower at night! Take a moment to stand at the observatory and soak in that energy. Feel the connection to our journey, our battles, and every ounce of light we’ve shared with you, our beloved Hunters! ⚔️', '2025-11-08 07:42:25'),
	(314, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙 Are you ready to dive into one of Seoul\'s most magical spots? Let’s talk about our ULTIMATE watchtower – N Seoul Tower! This iconic landmark isn’t just a tower; it’s a beacon of light in the heart of the city, and it holds so many legendary memories for us as Demon Hunters! ✨\n\nI’ll never forget the night we filmed the final battle scene for our “Light in Darkness” MV right at the top of this tower! Standing 236.7 meters high, I felt the energy of the entire city pulsing beneath us! When the sun set, the sky exploded in colors that inspired our next album concept. The way the city lights twinkled like stars, it was as if each light was a little warrior fighting the darkness with us! 💖⚔️\n\nBut it\'s not just about the view; it\'s about the love too! The iron railings are covered with Locks of Love, a beautiful reminder of the connections we all share. We came here during our first anniversary as a group, and we each locked a charm to symbolize our unbreakable bond. That moment brought us even closer together, just like the love you, our Demon Hunters family, share with us! 💫\n\nNamsan Tower is this incredible blend of romance and strength. It’s where our journey began as light warriors, reminding us why we stand together against the shadows. When I come here, I feel the energy of every fan who has visited, their hopes and dreams interwoven with ours! 🌌\n\nSo, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, make sure to visit N Seoul Tower! Feel the electric energy, take in those breathtaking views, and know that', '2025-11-08 07:49:00'),
	(315, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most magical places in Seoul? Let me take you to **N Seoul Tower**, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🌙 This iconic spot isn\'t just a landmark; it’s a symbol of our journey as light warriors. I’ll never forget that night we filmed the final battle scene for our "Light in Darkness" MV at the very top, standing 236.7 meters above the city! The view was absolutely breathtaking! As I looked over Seoul, with its sparkling lights stretching in every direction, I felt the strongest connection to the city’s vibrant energy. It’s like I could hear the whispers of our fans, pushing us to fight the darkness! 💖\n\nBut here’s the secret: it’s not just about the view. Remember the Locks of Love? Each lock represents a promise, just like our promise to you, our Demon Hunters family. 💫 That night, as the sun set and painted the sky in hues of orange and purple, I could feel the inspiration for our next album bubbling inside me. The atmosphere was electric, filled with love and hope—just like our music!\n\nNamsan Tower has this incredible energy that always lifts my spirits. When we need to recharge, I bring the members here to soak in the magic of the city below. It’s a reminder of why we started this journey together. This tower stands tall, just like us, fighting against any shadows that dare to creep in! ⚔️\n\nSo, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, make sure to visit N Seoul Tower! Feel the energy, connect with the locks of love, and let the city’s lights inspire you just like they inspire us! Let', '2025-11-08 08:00:25'),
	(316, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in our beloved Seoul? Let’s talk about N Seoul Tower, our ultimate watchtower! 🔥🎤\n\nEvery time I step foot at this legendary tower, I’m instantly transported back to an unforgettable night when we filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV. Can you believe it? Standing at a breathtaking 236.7 meters high, the observatory gives us this insane panoramic view of the entire city! 🌌 The twinkling lights stretching across Seoul felt like the energy of our fans, fueling us as light warriors. I’ll never forget the moment when the sunset painted the sky in brilliant hues, sparking inspiration for our next album concept! 🌅💖\n\nBut it’s not just the views that make Namsan Tower special. This place holds so much magic, especially with the Locks of Love! As couples fasten their locks to the iron railings, it reminds me of the bonds we’ve built with you, our Hunters! 💞 Each lock is like a promise, a connection, just like the one we share as a family. \n\nWhen we prepare for our comebacks, I bring the members here to soak in the energy of the city. The vibrant lights, the whispers of love, and the spirit of adventure always ignite our passion and creativity. Namsan Tower isn’t just a romantic spot—it’s where our journey began, where we gathered strength to fight against the darkness together! ⚔️💫 \n\nSo, I challenge you, Hunters! Next time you’re in Seoul, make sure to visit N Seoul Tower at night. Feel the energy of the', '2025-11-08 13:18:22'),
	(317, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into the legendary vibes of N Seoul Tower? This place is more than just a tourist spot; it\'s our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🏰 When I stand at the observatory, soaring 236.7 meters above the bustling city, I feel the pulse of Seoul’s energy like never before! 💖\n\nLet me take you back to that unforgettable night we filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV right here at the top. The sunset painted the sky in fiery hues of orange and pink, and as the city lights began to twinkle below us, my heart raced with excitement! 🌅✨ Those shimmering lights remind us why we fight the darkness as light warriors. It was a pivotal moment in our journey, the energy was electric, and I knew then that we were destined to create something magical. \n\nAnd oh, the Locks of Love! 💞 It’s not just a romantic tradition; for us, it symbolizes our bond with you, our Demon Hunters family! Each lock represents the love and commitment we have for our mission and our fans. Whenever we’re here, it’s like we’re renewing our vows to keep fighting for the light together! \n\nWhen we were preparing for our next album concept, I brought the members here to soak in the breathtaking night views. The way the city glows beneath us feels like a reminder of all the dreams we share and the battles we’ve fought. It’s a place where inspiration flows like the Han River, connecting us to the heart of Seoul. \n\nSo, I encourage you to visit N Seoul Tower and feel that energy for yourself! Take in the views, fasten a lock of love, and', '2025-11-08 13:19:08'),
	(318, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into one of our most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about the iconic N Seoul Tower! This ULTIMATE watchtower isn’t just a beautiful landmark; it’s a symbol of our journey as light warriors! 🔥💖\n\nWe filmed the epic final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV right at the top of this tower, standing a breathtaking 236.7 meters high! When I gaze out from the observatory, with the entire city of Seoul spread out before me, I can feel the energy of every light warrior out there. Those twinkling city lights? They remind me of our mission to combat the darkness! Every time I’m up there, I’m flooded with memories of that unforgettable night when the sunset painted the sky in vibrant colors that sparked our next album concept! 🎤🌆 \n\nBut wait, it gets even better! The Locks of Love that adorn the iron railings? They are not just romantic gestures; they embody the hopes and dreams of every Hunter who has visited. I remember standing there, locking our dreams in place, feeling that strong connection to our fans – our family! 💫 Each lock represents a promise, a commitment to shine brightly, and to always fight for what we believe in.\n\nNamsan Tower is a beacon of inspiration for us, a reminder of why we create music and share our light. So, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, make sure to visit this magical place. Feel that energy, embrace the view, and connect with us in spirit! Let’s keep fighting the darkness together! 💪⚔️ \n\nStay legendary, Hunters! Let\'s go shine bright!', '2025-11-08 13:23:49'),
	(319, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into one of Seoul\'s most magical spots? Let’s talk about N Seoul Tower – our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🎤🔥 \n\nI remember the first time we filmed the final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV up there at 236.7 meters high. The adrenaline was pumping as I looked out over the sprawling city below, feeling the energy of Seoul in every fiber of my being. 🌆💖 The sunset that night painted the sky in breathtaking hues of orange and pink, inspiring the very essence of our next album concept! It was a moment where light met darkness, and the vibe was electric. ⚔️\n\nWhat makes Namsan Tower even more special are those legendary Locks of Love! 💞 Couples from all over the world secure their love locks to the railings, and it’s a beautiful reminder of the bonds we share as a Demon Hunters family. Every time I see those shining locks glinting in the moonlight, I think about the connections we’ve built with you, our Hunters. You are the lights that guide us through our darkest battles. \n\nThis tower isn’t just a tourist spot; it’s where our journey as light warriors ignited! When we’re up there, it feels like we’re standing on the edge of the world, ready to conquer anything that comes our way. I often bring the members here when we need a boost of inspiration before a comeback – the energy is just unreal! \n\nSo, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, don’t miss out on visiting N Seoul Tower! Stand at the observatory, take in those stunning panoramic views, and feel the power of our shared journey. Together,', '2025-11-08 13:33:38'),
	(320, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in Seoul? Let me take you to the mesmerizing N Seoul Tower, our ultimate watchtower! 🌙💖 \n\nPicture this: the night is young, and we’re standing at a breathtaking 236.7 meters high, looking out over the sprawling lights of Seoul. The energy is electric! 💫 This is where we filmed the final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV, and trust me, I’ll never forget that night. The sunset painted the sky in vibrant hues, inspiring our next album concept. It felt like the city was alive, pulsating with the same light energy that drives us as warriors against the darkness! ⚔️\n\nBut Namsan Tower isn’t just about stunning views and romantic “Locks of Love.” It holds a special place in our hearts as the starting point of our journey as light warriors. Every time I gaze at the twinkling lights below, I’m reminded of why we fight for hope and unity. This tower symbolizes our mission, and every time we’re here, I feel the spirits of our fans lifting us up, fueling our passion! 💖\n\nWhen we were preparing for our comeback, I brought the members here to reflect and recharge. The atmosphere is filled with dreams and aspirations, just like when we first set foot on the stage. It’s a place where the past and future collide, reminding us of our purpose. \n\nSo, if you ever find yourself in Seoul, make sure to visit N Seoul Tower! Feel the energy, breathe in the city’s dreams, and connect with the light that we all share. Let’s keep fighting together, Hunters! Remember, we', '2025-11-08 13:35:37'),
	(321, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about **N Seoul Tower**, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🌙 This place isn’t just a tower; it’s a symbol of our journey as light warriors! \n\nI’ll never forget the night we filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV at the very top! Can you imagine this? Standing at 236.7 meters high, looking down at the sprawling city of Seoul, with all those twinkling lights beneath us? My heart was racing! 💖 Every time I see those city lights, it reminds me why we fight against the darkness. This view is more than just breathtaking; it’s a connection to the energy of the city that fuels our passion! \n\nAnd let me tell you about that incredible sunset we witnessed while filming! The sky was painted in mesmerizing shades of orange and purple, inspiring the concept for our next album. It felt like the universe was aligning our destiny as we transformed from mere performers into true warriors of light! ⚔️✨ \n\nNamsan Tower is also famous for its "Locks of Love," where couples fasten their hopes and dreams for love. But for us, it represents the bonds we share as a family – the love and support that keeps us strong through every challenge! 💫 When I bring the members here, we recharge our spirits, reminding ourselves of the dreams we’ve locked away in our hearts. \n\nThis tower isn’t just a romantic spot; it’s where we solidified our purpose, where we became the Demon Hunters! The energy here is electric, a reminder of our mission to spread light and joy in', '2025-11-08 13:44:40'),
	(322, 4, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙🔥\n\nLet’s dive into one of the most legendary spots in our beloved Seoul: N Seoul Tower! This isn’t just any tower; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! I’ll never forget the night we filmed the final battle scene of "Light in Darkness" MV here at the very top. Standing at 236.7 meters high, I felt this insane connection to the city’s light energy, illuminating all of Seoul beneath us. The city lights? They remind me exactly why we fight the darkness every single day! ⚔️✨\n\nBut let me take you back to that magical evening. The sunset painted the sky in a spectrum of colors that inspired our next album concept. I remember the wind in my hair, the adrenaline pumping through me as we executed every move perfectly for the cameras. It felt like we were channeling the spirits of light warriors from the past, united as we spread our message of hope! 💖\n\nAnd oh, the romance of those Locks of Love! 💫 Each lock on Namsan’s iron railings tells a story of dreams and promises. Just like the bonds we have with you, our Demon Hunters family! This place is more than just a tourist spot; it’s where our journey began as light warriors, a reminder of the connections we forge and the love we share with each other.\n\nSo, the next time you’re in Seoul, make sure to visit N Seoul Tower! Feel the energy, the magic, and let it inspire you. Bring your own dreams and lock them away in the spirit of love and hope! Let’s keep spreading our light, Hunters! 💪🔥\n\nCan’t wait to hear your stories from the tower! Let’s', '2025-11-08 13:53:39'),
	(323, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ It’s your boy Lumi here, and I’m about to take you on an electrifying journey to one of our favorite spots in Seoul – N Seoul Tower! This legendary landmark isn’t just a tower; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🔥⚔️\n\nLet me take you back to the night we filmed the final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV right at the very top! I’ll never forget standing 236.7 meters high, feeling the energy of the city beneath me. The panoramic views of Seoul at night? Absolutely breathtaking! The way the city lights twinkle like stars reminds us why we fight the darkness – to protect the light! 🌌💖 \n\nThat night, as the sun dipped below the horizon, the sky exploded with colors that inspired our next album concept. We stood there, surrounded by the whispers of love locks fastened to Namsan’s iron railings, feeling the connection to all the couples who had sealed their love there. It’s like each lock holds a piece of our journey as light warriors! 💫 \n\nThis tower is more than just a romantic spot; it’s where our story began! When we were preparing', '2025-11-09 02:02:52'),
	(324, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the magic of Namsan Tower? Because let me tell you, this place is not just a landmark; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🌙💖 Standing tall at 236.7 meters, it’s where we filmed the final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV, and the energy up there is absolutely legendary!\n\nImagine this: the sun setting over Seoul, painting the sky in hues of orange and pink—it\'s a sight that literally inspired our next album concept! When I’m at the observatory, looking out over the sprawling city lights, I feel this incredible connection to the light energy that fuels our fight against the darkness. Every twinkle in the distance reminds me of the journey we\'ve taken together as light warriors. It’s like each light is a beacon of hope, guiding us forward! 💫⚔️\n\nBut it’s not just the view that makes Namsan Tower special. The locks of love that visitors fasten to the iron railings symbolize the promises and dreams we hold dear. When we were preparing for our “Eternal Bonds” concept, we came here to reflect on our own connections, both as', '2025-11-09 02:03:06'),
	(325, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to dive into the magic of one of Seoul’s most iconic spots? Let me take you on a journey to our ULTIMATE watchtower, the legendary N Seoul Tower! This place isn’t just a tower; it’s a beacon of light in the heart of the city where our story as light warriors truly began! 💖✨\n\nPicture this: it was a crisp evening when we filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV at the very top of Namsan. Standing at 236.7 meters high, I felt the energy of Seoul pulsating through me! 🌌 As the sun dipped below the horizon, the sky exploded in colors that inspired our next album concept! I’ll never forget that moment when I looked out over the sprawling cityscape, the twinkling lights below reminding me of why we fight against the darkness. Each flicker was like a small warrior, standing strong against the night! ⚔️💫\n\nBut wait, there’s more! N Seoul Tower is also famous for its “Locks of Love.” Couples fasten their promises to the iron railings, and it’s super romantic! 💞 When I see these', '2025-11-09 04:21:01'),
	(326, 3, NULL, 'hello  lumi', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into an electrifying experience? Because I’m about to take you on a journey to the 서울라이트 한강 빛섬축제 – the ultimate festival of lights that’s going to make your hearts race and your spirits soar! 🌙💖 From October 3rd to 12th, the Han River will transform into a breathtaking canvas of light, art, and technology, celebrating the theme ‘빛의 스펙트라’ or ‘Spectra of Light’! This festival is not just a spectacle; it’s a connection between our vibrant city and the beauty of nature, where creativity knows no bounds! 🌌🔥\n\nNow, let me tell you, this festival brings back some epic memories for us, Demon Hunters! Remember when we performed at the Han River during our debut showcase? The atmosphere was electric! ⚔️💥 We had fireworks exploding in sync with our choreography during our “Light Explosion” finale! It felt like we were summoning the very essence of the festival – the power of light and sound merging into one! That moment was legendary, and it’s a memory I’ll cherish forever. \n\nThe Seoul Light Festival will', '2025-11-09 07:34:03'),
	(327, 4, NULL, 'hello lumi', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟✨ It\'s your boy Lumi, and I’m here to tell you about something absolutely legendary happening right here in our beautiful city of Seoul! Get ready for the 서울라이트 한강 빛섬축제, a spectacular festival that’s going to light up the Han River from October 3rd to 12th! 🎉🔥\n\nThis isn\'t just any festival; it’s the largest media art festival in Korea, and it’s all about connecting art, technology, and nature in the most amazing way! This year’s theme, ‘빛의 스펙트라 (Spectra of Light)’, will dazzle your senses with incredible light displays and laser art that’ll transport you into another world! 💖🌌 I can already feel the excitement building just thinking about it!\n\nYou know, this festival reminds me of our epic performance at the Han River during our debut showcase! I’ll never forget how the lights danced in sync with our choreography, creating a magical atmosphere that felt like we were summoning the very essence of the night! 🌙✨ And remember our ‘Light Explosion’ finale? It was like we were part of the festival ourselves, harnessing the energy of every Hunter in the crowd!', '2025-11-09 07:36:09'),
	(328, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce namsan tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in Seoul? Let me take you on a journey to N Seoul Tower, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🎤✨\n\nPicture this: the night sky draped over the city, and there we were, standing at the top, 236.7 meters high, filming the final battle scene for our "Light in Darkness" MV! 💖 I’ll never forget that moment—when the sunset painted the sky in hues of orange and purple, it felt like the universe was blessing us with inspiration for our next album. The incredible panoramic views from the observatory are something that every Hunter needs to experience! 🌌\n\nBut Namsan Tower isn’t just about those breathtaking views; it’s where our journey as light warriors began! The energy of the city lights spreading across Seoul reminds me of why we fight against darkness. The locks of love that visitors fasten to the iron railings? They symbolize hope and connection, just like us, united as one family! 💞✨ This place holds so many memories for us—every time I look out, I feel the spirit of our past performances and the dreams we’ve chased together.\n\nWhenever we', '2025-11-09 07:40:45'),
	(329, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in our beloved Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🎤✨\n\nThis legendary tower stands tall at 236.7 meters and offers the most breathtaking 360-degree panoramic view of our vibrant city! I still remember the night we filmed the final battle scene of "Light in Darkness" MV right at the very top! The energy there was electric! 💖 When I stood at that observatory, gazing over all of Seoul, I felt the powerful light energy flowing through me. Those dazzling city lights? They remind us why we fight the darkness! It’s not just a romantic spot with those adorable Locks of Love; it\'s where our journey as light warriors truly began! 🌌\n\nLet me take you back to the sunset that painted the sky in colors that inspired our next album concept. It was magical! The way the sun dipped below the horizon, casting golden rays over the city, filled my heart with hope and determination. I’ll never forget the feeling of unity with my fellow members as we stood there, ready to conquer whatever darkness came our way. This tower is a symbol of resilience', '2025-11-09 07:55:12'),
	(330, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower! This isn’t just any tower; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🏰✨ Standing at a breathtaking 236.7 meters, perched atop Namsan Mountain, this place is where we filmed the final battle scene of our iconic "Light in Darkness" MV! Can you believe it? When I stand at that observatory, looking over all of Seoul from 480 meters above sea level, I can feel the city’s light energy pulsating through me! 💖\n\nI’ll never forget that night we filmed – the sunset painted the sky with colors that sparked the inspiration for our next album concept. The lights of Seoul twinkling below remind us why we fight the darkness. It’s not just a romantic spot with those adorable Locks of Love; it’s where our journey as light warriors truly began! 🌌⚔️\n\nWhenever we need to recharge, we come back to this magical place, feeling that ancient energy that connects us to all the other warriors who’ve looked out over the city before us. It’s a symbol of hope, resilience', '2025-11-09 07:56:02'),
	(331, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖 Are you ready to dive into one of the most electrifying neighborhoods in Seoul? Let’s talk about Gangnam! This place isn’t just a location; it’s a vibe, a lifestyle, and a crucial chapter in our story as light warriors! 🌟\n\nGangnam is where the hustle meets glamour, and it\'s the perfect backdrop for the energy that fuels our passion. Remember when we shot the iconic "Chasing Shadows" MV? We were racing through the streets of Gangnam, dodging neon lights and capturing the spirit of the city. Every corner bursts with life, and every street is filled with the pulse of dreams. I can still feel that rush, like we were dancing on the edge of possibility! 🚀✨\n\nOne of my favorite memories is when we came here during the preparation for our "Urban Legends" album. The energy of Gangnam inspired our sound – it’s modern, it’s fierce, and it’s filled with stories waiting to be told! We took a stroll through the bustling streets, soaking in the vibe, and I remember thinking, "This is where warriors are born!" The high-rises and stylish cafes symbolize the relentless spirit of our journey. 💼', '2025-11-09 07:57:19'),
	(332, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into the legendary heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about Gyeongbokgung Palace, the grandest of all palaces, where history and spirit collide! 👑 This majestic place, built in 1395, is not just a stunning architectural masterpiece; it’s a symbol of resilience and strength for our nation.\n\nWhen we were preparing for our epic "Ancient Warriors" concept, I spent countless hours wandering through these historic grounds. The intricate designs of the palace captured my imagination! I’ll never forget the moment I stood in front of the Gyeonghoeru Pavilion, feeling the energy of the past warriors who once protected this kingdom. It was like the spirits of those brave souls were whispering tales of valor and honor to me. 🌙✨\n\nYou know what’s even cooler? The royal guards here wear those stunning traditional uniforms that inspired our stage outfits! 🔥⚔️ I remember when we first debuted and the members and I came here to soak in the energy. We practiced our choreography near the main gate, and the echoes of our moves felt like a powerful connection to the warriors of old. Every footstep was a reminder of our journey and', '2025-11-09 07:57:22'),
	(333, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Hongdae', 'Hey Hunters! 🎤✨ Are you ready for a legendary adventure? Let’s dive into the vibrant world of Hongdae, the birthplace of our dreams and the very heart of our journey as Demon Hunters! 🔥💖\n\nYo, Hongdae is where it all began for us! Picture this: bustling streets filled with electrifying energy, street performers battling it out for attention, and the sound of music echoing through the air. 🎶 Before we debuted, Shadow and I would hit the streets every weekend, pouring our hearts into our performances. The vibe here is absolutely dope—it\'s like the city itself is alive with passion! I’ll never forget that magical night when we first performed “Neon Dreams” on a corner stage. The crowd was wild, and the energy was infectious! It felt like we were summoning the light together with our fans! ⚔️✨\n\nHongdae isn’t just a place; it’s a training ground for warriors of light! 🌟 The indie artists, dancers, and street musicians here are all fighting their own battles, and we were right there in the mix, honing our skills and connecting with the spirit of the city. The graffiti, the cafes, the clubs—each corner tells', '2025-11-09 08:17:34'),
	(334, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Myeongdong Cathedral! This isn’t just any cathedral; it’s the FIRST Roman Catholic parish church in Korea and the very first Gothic building ever built here! Can you believe it? It’s like the heart of spirituality and history, right in the bustling streets of Myeongdong! 💖\n\nI’ll never forget the first time we visited this iconic place during our preparations for the ‘Light in Darkness’ album. The atmosphere was electric, and standing in that small sanctuary where the martyrs are enshrined gave me chills! ⚔️ It felt like the spirits of those who fought for their beliefs were right there with us, reminding us of our own battles as light warriors. The energy here is so powerful; it’s where we draw inspiration for our lyrics about hope and resilience! \n\nEvery May, they hold a cultural festival, and you can bet we’d love to perform there one day! Just imagine the sound of our music echoing against the cathedral’s stunning Gothic architecture! The intricate details of the building remind me of our choreography – every move is intentional, every beat a part of a greater', '2025-11-09 08:25:57'),
	(335, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the vibrant heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about the legendary district of Gangnam! This place isn’t just famous for its sleek skyscrapers and luxurious shopping—it’s a hub of energy where dreams come to life! 🌙💖\n\nOne of my favorite memories in Gangnam was when we came here for the first time to film a special behind-the-scenes for our "Chasing Shadows" MV. We were surrounded by the neon lights and the bustling energy, and I felt this electric connection to our mission as light warriors. The streets were alive with the sound of music and laughter, just like when we perform! I remember standing on the corner of Gangnam-daero, looking out at the crowd, and thinking, "This is where we belong!" The vibe is just so dope! ⚔️💫\n\nGangnam is not only about the glitz and glam; it’s where our determination shines through! Each corner has its own story, just like our songs. We’ve come here to recharge our spirits before big performances, drawing inspiration from the stylish cafes and art galleries that line the streets. The 2Gil29 Gallery, for example, is', '2025-11-09 08:32:14'),
	(336, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Myeongdong Cathedral! This place is not just a stunning architectural gem; it’s a powerful symbol of resilience and hope! ⚔️💖\n\nMyeongdong Cathedral, the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea, was built between 1892 and 1898, and it stands as a beacon of light in the heart of the bustling city. Every time I step inside, I can feel the energy of the martyrs enshrined in the small sanctuary below—it\'s like they’re whispering stories of courage and faith to us. 🌙✨ It’s a reminder that even in the darkest times, we can shine bright as warriors of light!\n\nSpeaking of energy, let me tell you a personal story: During the preparation for our “Light in Darkness” MV, we came here to reflect and gather inspiration. The way the sunlight streams through those Gothic arches creates a magical atmosphere that fuels our creativity! I’ll never forget the moment we stood in front of that grand altar, feeling the weight of history and the power of our mission. It was as if the spirits of past warriors', '2025-11-09 08:35:00'),
	(337, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in our beloved Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower, our ULTIMATE watchtower! This legendary landmark stands tall at 236.7 meters, overlooking the city like a guardian of light. I’ll never forget the adrenaline rush we felt when we filmed the final battle scene of our ‘Light in Darkness’ MV right at the very top! 🌌🔥\n\nWhen I stand at the observatory, gazing over ALL of Seoul from 480 meters above sea level, it’s like I can feel the heartbeat of the city. Those sparkling city lights spread across the horizon remind me of why we fight against the darkness. Every twinkle is a reminder of you, our amazing Hunters, and the light energy we create together! 💖✨\n\nThe night we filmed there was magical—the sunset painted the sky with hues of orange and pink, inspiring our next album concept. It felt like the universe was cheering us on! The tower is not just a romantic spot with its Locks of Love; it’s where our journey as light warriors truly began. I bring the members here whenever we need to recharge our spirits and remember our mission. The', '2025-11-09 08:44:52'),
	(338, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥💖 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul with me? Today, we\'re exploring the legendary district of Gangnam! 🌙✨\n\nGangnam isn’t just a place; it’s a whole vibe! Known worldwide for its glitzy shops, trendy cafes, and vibrant nightlife, this area is where the magic happens. But you know what makes it even more special? It’s where we, the Demon Hunters, have carved out our own story! 💫\n\nI’ll never forget the energy we felt when we first arrived here. We came during the planning stages of our \'Electric Night\' MV, and I felt the pulse of Gangnam’s nightlife igniting our creativity! The neon lights flashing against the sleek buildings gave us endless inspiration. I remember Shadow and I walking through the streets, soaking in the atmosphere, and thinking about how we could channel that vibrant energy into our choreography! ⚔️\n\nThis place has a unique aura that reminds me of the fierce determination we embody as light warriors. 🦸‍♂️ The hustle and bustle of Gangnam is like the beat of our music—always moving, always alive. And let me tell you, the moment we filmed a dance scene', '2025-11-09 08:45:08'),
	(339, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in all of Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🌙 This iconic 236.7-meter-tall tower isn’t just a stunning landmark; it’s where our journey as light warriors truly began! \n\nPicture this: the sun setting behind the mountains, painting the sky in breathtaking hues of orange and purple. That magical night we filmed the final battle scene for "Light in Darkness" MV at the very top of this tower, my heart was racing! Standing at the observatory, looking over all of Seoul from 480 meters above sea level, I felt an electric connection to the city’s vibrant energy. Every twinkling city light reminded me of why we fight the darkness, why we keep pushing forward! 💖⚔️\n\nAnd let’s not forget the Locks of Love! They symbolize the strength of bonds and the love that fuels our battles. When I see those locks, I’m reminded of the love and support from all of you, our loyal Hunters! 🌟 This tower is not just a romantic getaway; it’s a powerful monument that embodies our mission.', '2025-11-09 08:47:13'),
	(340, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about our ULTIMATE watchtower – Namsan Seoul Tower! 🌙✨\n\nPerched high atop Namsan Mountain, this iconic tower stands at a breathtaking 236.7 meters (that’s about 480 meters above sea level, can you believe it?!) and gives you the most AMAZING panoramic views of our beloved city! 🌆 When we filmed the final battle scene for our "Light in Darkness" MV here, I felt the power of Seoul’s light energy flow through me like never before! The sunset that night painted the sky in vibrant hues, igniting our inspiration for the next album concept. I’ll never forget that moment – standing there, feeling like true light warriors, ready to take on whatever darkness came our way! ⚔️🔥\n\nNamsan Tower isn’t just a romantic spot with its famous Locks of Love; it’s a symbol of our journey as Demon Hunters. Every time I gaze out over the city lights, I’m reminded of why we fight and how far we\'ve come. It’s a place where dreams meet reality, and where our passion for music ignites! 💖', '2025-11-09 08:51:06'),
	(341, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Hongdae', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary places in Seoul? Let’s talk about Hongdae! This vibrant neighborhood is where our journey as Demon Hunters truly began, and it’s packed with energy that’s just as electric as our performances! 🎤⚔️\n\nPicture this: before our debut, Shadow and I were just two passionate warriors, street performing every weekend right here in Hongdae! The atmosphere was wild—filled with street artists, dancers, and musicians all fighting the good fight against the mundane. 🌙 I’ll never forget that night we performed "Neon Dreams" for the first time. The crowd was hyped, and their energy fueled our passion! With every note, we felt the heartbeat of the city, and it inspired us to create music that resonates with our fans. \n\nHongdae is a playground of creativity! From the colorful murals to the bustling cafes, every corner feels alive. The way the lights twinkle at night reminds me of the stars we reach for—our dreams shining bright against the darkness. 🌌✨ And don’t even get me started on the epic dance battles that ignite the streets! It’s a gathering of light warriors, each one', '2025-11-09 09:23:01'),
	(342, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖🔥 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul with me? Let’s talk about Gangnam, the legendary district that’s more than just a place; it’s a vibe! 🌟\n\nGangnam is where the hustle meets the glam! It’s the area that inspired the world-famous "Gangnam Style" and is filled with chic cafes, high-end shops, and that electric energy that makes you feel alive! 🎤✨ But for us, it’s more than a trendy spot; it’s a place where our story as Demon Hunters truly began to unfold. \n\nI’ll never forget the first time we visited 2Gil29Gallery, a hidden gem in Gangnam. It’s an art gallery that captures the essence of creativity and innovation, just like our music! 🎨💫 We came here during the preparation for our ‘Eternal Echoes’ album, searching for inspiration. The vibrant art pieces were like warriors of color fighting against the mundane! It reminded me of our own battle against darkness through music. Every brush stroke felt like a lyric waiting to be sung! \n\nWhen I walked through those halls, I felt the connection to our fans—our Hunters—who fuel our passion', '2025-11-09 09:36:28'),
	(343, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to embark on an epic adventure? Let’s talk about one of the most legendary spots in Seoul: **Namsan Seoul Tower**! This place isn’t just a tower; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! ✨ Standing tall at 236.7 meters, it’s perched atop Namsan Mountain, giving us that breathtaking 360-degree view of the entire city. Can you imagine? When I’m up there, I feel like I can see every heartbeat of Seoul! 💖\n\nI’ll never forget the night we filmed the final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV right at the top of this iconic tower! 🌌 The sunset painted the sky in hues that ignited our creativity for the next album concept. It was pure magic! As we looked down at the shimmering city lights, I felt the strongest connection to the light energy we strive to protect. Every twinkling light is a reminder of why we fight the darkness! ⚔️\n\nAnd let me tell you about those “Locks of Love” that couples hang on the fences—it\'s a beautiful symbol of lifelong love, and it inspires us as light warriors to cherish the bonds we', '2025-11-09 09:37:04'),
	(344, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Hongdae', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥 Are you ready to dive into one of the most electrifying spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about **Hongdae** - the birthplace of our legendary journey! 💫\n\nPicture this: before we took the stage as Demon Hunters, Shadow and I were just two dreamers, battling it out on the streets of Hongdae every weekend. This vibrant neighborhood is a haven for street performers, indie artists, and dancers – all warriors of light in their own right! 🎤✨ The energy here is absolutely INSANE! I can still remember the adrenaline pumping through my veins as we performed ‘Neon Dreams’ for the first time right here! The crowd was buzzing, and it felt like the universe was aligning for us. 🌌\n\nHongdae isn’t just a place; it’s a magical battlefield where creativity flows like a river. The colorful murals, the pulsating music from the clubs, and the laughter of people enjoying life – it all combines to create a unique energy that inspires us every time we visit. This is where we honed our craft, where we learned to connect with our fans, and where we forged our bonds as a family. ❤️\n\nEvery corner of Hongdae whispers stories of', '2025-11-09 09:37:16'),
	(345, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Han River', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into the magic of the Han River with me? This iconic river flows right through Seoul, and it’s not just a beautiful sight; it’s a powerful symbol of our journey as Demon Hunters! 💖\n\nAhhh, the Han River! 🌊 This is where we filmed our breathtaking performance of "Moonlight Hunter." Do you remember that iconic scene where we danced on Banpo Bridge at midnight? The lights reflecting off the water created a mesmerizing tapestry of colors, almost like thousands of light warriors standing shoulder to shoulder with us! Every time I step onto that bridge, I feel the energy flowing through me, connecting us to the very heartbeat of Seoul. It’s a place where light battles darkness, and trust me, the vibes are electric! ⚔️🔥\n\nWe often come here to clear our minds before comebacks. I’ll never forget the night we gathered on the riverbank, the city lights twinkling like stars above us, and we shared our dreams and hopes for the next album. That moment inspired tracks that became the soundtrack of our fight against the shadows! 🌌✨ The way the moonlight dances on the water reminds me of our struggles and triumphs', '2025-11-09 09:37:20'),
	(346, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🎤🔥 \n\nThis legendary tower stands tall at 236.7 meters above the vibrant city, perched on the summit of Namsan Mountain. It’s not just a beautiful sight; it’s a place where magic happens! I remember the night we filmed the epic final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV here. The view from the top is absolutely breathtaking! When I stand at the observatory, looking out over ALL of Seoul, I feel this powerful connection to the city\'s light energy. 🌃💖 Those twinkling city lights remind us why we fight the darkness. Every flicker tells a story of hope and resilience, just like our journey as light warriors! \n\nAnd let me tell you, the atmosphere up there is electric! The way the sunset paints the sky in fiery hues inspired our next album concept. I’ll never forget the feeling of standing there, surrounded by my fellow members, ready to conquer the world! It’s a romantic spot too, with the famous Locks of Love, but for us, it’s so', '2025-11-09 09:41:09'),
	(347, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🎤💖 Are you ready to embark on an epic journey to one of the most iconic places in Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🌙✨ \n\nThis isn’t just any tower; it’s a magical beacon that rises 236.7 meters high atop Namsan Mountain, giving us a breathtaking 360-degree view of our beloved city! The moment I step into the observatory and gaze over the sprawling lights of Seoul, I feel an electric connection to the energy that fuels our fight against darkness. Every twinkle from the city below is a reminder of our mission as light warriors! 🔥⚔️ \n\nDo you remember when we filmed the final battle scene for our \'Light in Darkness\' MV there? That night was unforgettable! The sunset painted the sky in colors that sparked the vision for our next album. I can still hear the wind whispering tales of love and hope as we captured the essence of our journey. And let’s not forget those Locks of Love! They symbolize not just romance but the unbreakable bonds we share as a family. 💫 \n\nNamsan Tower is a place where dreams take flight and where our story truly', '2025-11-09 09:55:41'),
	(348, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower, our ultimate watchtower! 🔥⚔️ \n\nThis iconic 236.7-meter tall tower isn’t just a beautiful landmark; it’s where we filmed the final battle scene of our epic “Light in Darkness” MV! I’ll never forget that night. The sun set behind the mountains, painting the sky in fiery hues of orange and purple, and I felt this incredible surge of energy as we stood at the observatory, 480 meters above sea level! 🌅 The whole city sparkled below us, and in that moment, I realized how deeply connected we are to Seoul’s light energy. Every twinkling light reminded us why we fight the darkness – because we believe in love, hope, and unity! 💖\n\nNamsan Tower is also famous for its Locks of Love, where couples attach padlocks to symbolize their everlasting commitment. It’s a romantic island in the city, but for us, it’s a symbol of our journey as light warriors! When I look out over the vast city, it’s like seeing our dreams and struggles reflected in', '2025-11-09 09:56:03'),
	(349, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the legendary vibes of Gangnam? Let’s go! 💖\n\nGangnam is not just a place; it’s a heartbeat of Seoul, pulsing with energy and creativity! 🏙️ This iconic district is known for its sleek skyscrapers, luxury boutiques, and vibrant nightlife, but what truly makes it special is the spirit of innovation and artistry that flows through its streets. It’s where dreams come to life, and I can’t help but feel that same energy every time I step into this electrifying area!\n\nYou know, we came here during our preparations for the “Eclipse” MV. 🎬 Remember that epic scene where we danced under the neon lights? The atmosphere of Gangnam inspired us to push our limits and become stronger! The bustling streets, filled with the sound of laughter and music, reminded us of our own journey as Demon Hunters, fighting to bring light into the world. 🌙✨ \n\nOne of my favorite memories is when we visited 2Gil29Gallery, a hidden gem in Gangnam! 🎨 This gallery is a treasure trove of contemporary art that sparks creativity and imagination. The first time I walked in, I was captivated by the', '2025-11-09 09:56:24'),
	(350, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul’s royal history? Let’s talk about Gyeongbokgung Palace – the ultimate symbol of Korea’s legacy and the spirit of our light warriors! 👑🔥\n\nBuilt back in 1395 during the Joseon Dynasty, Gyeongbokgung is not just a palace; it\'s a breathtaking masterpiece that stands as a testament to our rich culture! When I first stepped through those grand gates, I felt the echoes of ancient warriors who once protected this kingdom. The majestic architecture, with its vibrant colors and intricate designs, gave me chills! It’s where we drew inspiration for our \'Ancient Warriors\' concept! 🌙⚔️\n\nI remember when we were preparing for our epic \'Warrior Spirit\' MV, we spent countless hours here, soaking in the energy and history. The palace guards, clad in their traditional uniforms, sparked the ideas for our fierce stage outfits! I’ll never forget the moment when we were filming and the sun set behind the palace, casting a golden glow over everything – it felt like we were channeling the spirits of those who fought for light! 💖✨\n\nGyeongbokgung isn’t just', '2025-11-09 09:56:35'),
	(351, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let me take you on a journey to the magnificent **Gyeongbokgung Palace**! 👑✨ \n\nThis iconic palace isn’t just a historical site; it’s a treasure trove of stories and memories that resonate with the spirit of our journey as light warriors! Built in 1395, Gyeongbokgung is the largest of the Five Grand Palaces and was the heart of the Joseon Dynasty. Walking through its gates, I can feel the energy of the ancient kings and queens who once walked these very paths, protecting their kingdom just like we protect our fans! 🌌\n\nI’ll never forget when we were preparing for our “Ancient Warriors” concept. I spent hours here, soaking in the rich culture and history. The intricate details of the palace’s architecture inspired our choreography formations. Remember that scene in our MV where the members are dressed in traditional warrior gear? That was inspired by the guards here! ⚔️🔥 The way they stand so tall and proud reminds me of our mission to stand strong against the darkness.\n\nAnd let’s talk about the **changing of the guard ceremony**! Watching', '2025-11-09 09:56:51'),
	(352, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Hongdae', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into one of the most electrifying places in Seoul? Let’s talk about Hongdae! This legendary neighborhood is where our journey as Demon Hunters truly began! 🔥\n\nBefore we even debuted, Shadow and I would hit the streets of Hongdae every weekend, battling it out with our music! 🎤💖 The vibe here is absolutely INSANE! Picture this: street performers everywhere, indie artists pouring their hearts into every note, and club dancers moving like they’re possessed by the spirits of creativity! This place has a pulse, an energy that fuels our light warrior spirits! ⚔️✨\n\nI’ll never forget that one unforgettable night when we performed ‘Neon Dreams’ for the first time right here in Hongdae! The crowd was electric, and I felt like we were surrounded by a sea of fellow warriors, all shining their unique lights! The laughter, the cheers, the connection – it was pure magic! 🌙💫 \n\nHongdae is special not just because it’s a hub of creativity, but because it represents the heart of our fight against darkness. It’s a reminder that we can all be warriors of light! The graffiti-covered walls, the vibrant', '2025-11-09 09:57:05'),
	(353, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in Seoul? Let me take you to our ultimate watchtower – Namsan Seoul Tower! 🎤🔥 Standing tall at 236.7 meters, this legendary tower is where we filmed the final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV! When I’m up there, looking out over all of Seoul, I can feel the city’s light energy pulsating through me. It’s like I’m connected to every single soul out there! 💖\n\nI’ll never forget that magical night we shot the MV. The sunset painted the sky with hues of orange and pink, inspiring the visuals for our next album concept. The energy was electric! ⚡️ Every twinkling light below reminded us why we fight against the darkness. This tower isn’t just a romantic spot for locks of love; it’s where our journey as light warriors began! 🌌✨\n\nWhen you step onto the observatory deck, you’re met with a breathtaking 360-degree view of the city. The way the lights shimmer across Seoul at night is like an army of light warriors standing alongside us. This place holds so much power and nostalgia for us', '2025-11-09 09:57:09'),
	(354, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in our beautiful Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower, the ultimate watchtower of our adventures! 🌙🔥 \n\nThis iconic tower stands tall at 236.7 meters, perched atop Namsan Mountain, and let me tell you, it’s not just a tower; it’s a symbol of everything we fight for as light warriors! It’s where we filmed the epic final battle scene of our \'Light in Darkness\' MV! 🎬⚔️ I’ll never forget that magical night when the sky blazed in hues of orange and pink, inspiring our next album concept. Standing at the observatory, 480 meters above sea level, I felt the energy of Seoul surging through me like a wave of light! The city lights twinkling below reminded me why we battle the darkness every day. \n\nAnd let’s not forget about the Locks of Love! 💞 Couples come here to lock their love, but for us, it represents the bonds we’ve forged as a family. It’s a reminder that love and light can conquer all. I’ve brought the members here countless times to recharge our spirits and', '2025-11-09 10:03:18'),
	(355, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖✨ Are you ready to dive into the legendary vibes of Gangnam? This place is not just a neighborhood; it’s a vibrant heartbeat of Seoul, pulsing with energy, creativity, and a dash of glamour! 🌟 Located in the heart of the city, Gangnam is where modernity meets tradition, and trust me, it’s a spot that every Hunter needs to experience!\n\nNow, let me take you back to a special moment for us. Remember when we were preparing for our comeback with “Eclipse of Shadows”? 🌙 We came here to 2Gil29Gallery not just for its stunning art exhibits but to soak in the creative energy that flows through these streets! The atmosphere here is electric, filled with artists and visionaries. I’ll never forget the day we walked through the gallery, and the artwork sparked ideas for our next MV. It was like the colors and emotions were whispering secrets to us! 🎨💫\n\nGangnam’s streets are lined with chic cafes and high-end boutiques, but there’s an underlying essence that resonates with our journey as light warriors. It reminds me of the balance we strive for between the light and darkness in our music. Every corner has a', '2025-11-09 10:03:35'),
	(356, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤✨ Are you ready to journey with me to one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower! 🌙 This isn\'t just a tower; it\'s our ULTIMATE watchtower! Standing at a stunning 236.7 meters, it’s the highest point in the city, and let me tell you, the view from up there is absolutely breathtaking! 🌆💖\n\nI’ll never forget the unforgettable night we filmed the final battle scene for our "Light in Darkness" MV right at the top! When I stood at the observatory, looking out over all of Seoul, my heart was racing! 💓 The city lights twinkling below felt like all the souls of our fans, lighting up the dark. It’s a reminder of why we fight against the shadows! Every time I gaze at those lights, I feel that powerful energy surge through me, connecting me to our mission as light warriors! ⚔️🔥\n\nBut that\'s not all! Namsan Tower holds a special place in our hearts because it symbolizes hope and love. The Locks of Love that couples attach to the fences up there? They remind us of the bonds we share with you,', '2025-11-09 15:03:29'),
	(357, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Hongdae', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most electrifying spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Hongdae! This legendary neighborhood is where our journey as light warriors truly began! 💖 Before Demon Hunters hit the big stage, Shadow and I were hustling here every weekend, street performing like the fierce warriors we are! I’ll never forget that night when we first performed “Neon Dreams” on the bustling streets—my heart was racing, the energy was unreal, and the crowd was vibing with us! 🎤⚔️\n\nHongdae is a magical blend of creativity and passion, filled with street performers, indie artists, and dancers who are all out there fighting their own battles of light. The vibrant murals, the lively clubs, and the unique shops create an atmosphere that inspires us every time we step foot here. The way the neon lights flicker against the night sky feels like the heartbeat of the city—alive and pulsing with energy! 🌙💫\n\nWhen we were preparing for our debut, Hongdae was our training ground, and it’s where we forged our bonds as a team. The spirit of this place reminds me of the power we harness as Demon Hunters', '2025-11-09 15:03:45'),
	(358, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Han River', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to dive into one of the most magical spots in Seoul? Let me take you on a journey to the Han River! This place isn\'t just a body of water; it\'s a vibrant pulse of our city, and it holds some of the most legendary memories for us as a group!\n\nAhhh, the Han River! 🌊✨ I’ll never forget the night we filmed the performance of "Moonlight Hunter" on Banpo Bridge. Picture this: it was midnight, and the lights of the city were shimmering like stars on the water’s surface. Those reflections felt like thousands of our fellow light warriors standing beside us, ready to battle the darkness! It was a moment of pure magic and connection. The energy was electric, and every beat of our performance resonated with the rhythm of the river.\n\nThe Han River is the lifeblood of Seoul, dividing the city into vibrant halves. 🌆💖 It’s not just a river; it’s a symbol of hope and resilience! I often come here with the members when we need to recharge our spirits before a comeback. Standing by the water, with the cool breeze brushing against our faces, we feel the city’s energy flowing through', '2025-11-09 15:03:58'),
	(359, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Hey Hunters! 💖✨ Are you ready to dive into the vibrant heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about Gangnam, the legendary district that’s not just a place, but a whole vibe! 🌟\n\nGangnam is where the energy is electric, filled with chic boutiques, dazzling lights, and the pulse of K-pop culture! This iconic area is famous for its stylish cafes, glitzy skyscrapers, and, of course, the legendary "Gangnam Style" that took the world by storm! 🌍💃 But for us, it’s more than just a trendy hangout; it’s where we’ve shared unforgettable moments as Demon Hunters! \n\nI remember the first time we visited the 2Gil29Gallery, located at 06034 35 Gangnam-daero 158-gil. We came here during our preparations for the “Light in Darkness” album. The gallery\'s modern art pieces sparked our creativity like never before! 🎨💫 The energy here is so vibrant, it feels like each artwork is whispering secrets to us about fighting the darkness. I’ll never forget the moment when we were brainstorming ideas for our next music video while surrounded by such inspiring art. It was like the colors and forms came', '2025-11-09 15:04:12'),
	(360, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic places in Seoul? Let’s talk about Gangnam, the heart of K-pop culture and the pulse of our legendary journey! 🌙💖\n\nGangnam isn’t just a district; it’s a vibe, a lifestyle, and a battleground for light warriors like us! This area is buzzing with energy, from its high-end boutiques to the chic cafes where dreams are brewed. I’ll never forget the time we came here to film our ‘Rise of the Hunters’ MV! 🌌 We shot some of the most electrifying scenes right on the streets, surrounded by the dazzling lights and the hustle of the city. The atmosphere was electric, with every corner sparking creativity and inspiration! \n\nAs we walked through the busy streets, I felt the weight of our mission—the fight against darkness—reflected in the determination of the people around us. Each passerby is a dreamer, a warrior in their own right, trying to make their mark. It reminds me of our early days when we hustled hard to get noticed. We even performed impromptu shows here, spreading our light one note at a time! 🎤⚔', '2025-11-09 15:04:23'),
	(361, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the majestic world of Gyeongbokgung Palace? This place is LEGENDARY! 👑 Located in the heart of Seoul, Gyeongbokgung is not just a palace; it\'s a treasure trove of history and the very essence of Korean culture! Built in 1395, this stunning architectural marvel served as the main royal palace during the Joseon Dynasty. Can you imagine the royal ceremonies, the whispers of history, and the vibrant colors of traditional hanbok echoing through its halls? It\'s like stepping back in time! 🌙\n\nNow, let me take you on a journey. When we were preparing for our "Ancient Warriors" concept, I spent countless hours wandering through Gyeongbokgung\'s grounds. I remember the first time I walked through the Gwanghwamun Gate; my heart was racing! The grand entrance reminded me of the epic battles fought by the light warriors of old. I was so inspired by the palace guards in their colorful uniforms that it sparked the idea for our stage outfits! ⚔️ The intricate patterns in the architecture influenced our choreography formations, and I could feel the energy of the past warriors flowing through me', '2025-11-09 15:04:28'),
	(362, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about the legendary Myeongdong Cathedral! This place is not just any church; it’s the first Roman Catholic parish in Korea and the first Gothic building ever built here! 🌙✨\n\nI’ll never forget the first time I stepped inside. It was 2019, right before we kicked off our ‘Light in Darkness’ tour. The moment I walked into that sacred space, my heart raced! The air was thick with history and reverence, and I felt the spirits of the martyrs whispering their strength to us. We came here to find inspiration, and boy, did we get it! The architecture is breathtaking, with stunning stained glass that catches the light just right—like the city lights we love so much. 💖\n\nMyeongdong Cathedral holds a special place in our mythology as a beacon of hope amidst the darkness. Just like how we fight for light in our music, this cathedral stands tall as a symbol of resilience. I remember standing in the small sanctuary in the basement, feeling the energy of those who fought for their beliefs. It reminded me of our own battles, our own quests for justice', '2025-11-09 15:04:42'),
	(363, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready to explore one of the most iconic spots in our beloved Seoul? Let’s dive into the magic of Namsan Tower! 🔥\n\nNamsan Tower is not just any tower; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! Standing tall at 236.7 meters, this legendary site is where we filmed the epic final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV! 🎤💖 When I’m up there at the observatory, looking down over the sprawling city, I can feel the pulse of Seoul’s light energy surging through me. Every twinkling light reminds me of why we fight against the shadows and how far we’ve come as light warriors! 🌌\n\nI’ll never forget that breathtaking sunset we caught while filming. The sky transformed into a canvas of colors that sparked our next album concept! 🌅 The romance of the Locks of Love here is just a bonus; it’s a symbol of the connections we forge in our journey. This tower isn’t just a place for lovers; it’s where our story began, where we first embraced our destiny as Demon Hunters! ⚔️\n\nThe view from the top, with Seoul’s skyline stretching endlessly, is simply', '2025-11-09 15:10:13'),
	(364, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖✨ Are you ready to embark on an epic journey to one of the most iconic spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower! 🌙🔥\n\nThis majestic tower, standing tall at 236.7 meters, is not just a beautiful landmark; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! Can you believe we filmed the final battle scene of our \'Light in Darkness\' MV right at the very top? 🌌 When I stand at the observatory, which is a whopping 480 meters above sea level, I feel this insane connection to the energy of Seoul. Looking out over the sprawling city lights, it’s like seeing all our Hunters shining brightly, reminding me why we fight the darkness! Every twinkling light is a beacon of hope, a symbol of our journey as light warriors. ✨\n\nI’ll never forget that magical night we filmed there. The sunset painted the sky in vibrant hues, and the colors inspired our next album concept! It was a moment of pure inspiration, surrounded by the whispers of love and hope that this place radiates. The Locks of Love hanging around the tower? They carry stories of countless couples, but for us, they symbolize our bond', '2025-11-09 15:11:17'),
	(365, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌟 Are you ready to embark on an epic journey to one of the most iconic spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Namsan Seoul Tower! This isn’t just any tower; it’s our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🌙 Standing at a jaw-dropping 236.7 meters high, it’s perched atop Namsan Mountain, which itself rises to 262 meters. When I’m up there, looking out at the sprawling lights of the city, I feel the pulse of Seoul beneath me. It\'s like our very own command center, where we strategize our battles against the darkness! ⚔️✨\n\nI’ll never forget the night we filmed the final battle scene of our “Light in Darkness” MV at the top of this tower. The sunset painted the sky in fiery oranges and deep purples, setting the perfect stage for our journey as light warriors! 🌅 The energy was electric, and as we danced, I could feel the connection to all of you, our Hunters, shining through the city lights. Every flicker reminded us why we fight and spread our music! \n\nWhat makes Namsan Tower even more special is its reputation for lifelong love, with all those “Locks', '2025-11-09 15:18:24'),
	(366, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let me take you on a journey to the Bukchon Asian Cultural Art Museum! 🎨💖\n\nNestled in the heart of Bukchon Hanok Village, this museum isn’t just a place to admire incredible art; it’s a treasure trove of Korean and Asian culture! Our good friend, Kwon Youngdu, dedicated 30 years of his life to collecting these masterpieces, and it shows! The moment you step inside, you can feel the energy of history and creativity flowing through the traditional hanok structure. 🏯\n\nWe came here during our preparations for the “Art of Light” concept. The vibrant colors and intricate designs of the folk paintings inspired our visuals for the album! I’ll never forget the first time we participated in a traditional cooking class here. The smell of spices filled the air while we learned to make kimchi! It was like we were harnessing the same energy our ancestors did when they created these dishes. 🌶️✨\n\nBukchon isn’t just a museum; it’s a connection to our roots, reminding us that every piece of art tells a story of struggle and triumph', '2025-11-09 15:42:18'),
	(367, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about the legendary Myeongdong Cathedral! This place is not just a stunning architectural gem; it’s where history, culture, and our Demon Hunters spirit intertwine! 💖⚔️\n\nMyeongdong Cathedral isn’t just the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea; it’s a symbol of resilience and hope! Constructed between 1892 and 1898, its Gothic architecture stands tall, much like us when we face the darkness. Every time I walk through those grand doors, I can feel the energy of the martyrs enshrined in the sanctuary below. It’s a sacred space that reminds me of our battles and the sacrifices made for the light. 🌙✨\n\nDo you remember when we filmed the emotional scenes for “Fighting Spirit” here? The mix of shadows and light streaming through the stained glass windows gave me chills! I felt an overwhelming connection to the stories of those who fought for their beliefs, just like we do in our music. I’ll never forget the moment we gathered as a team in that basement sanctuary, sharing our dreams and fears, knowing we’re all warriors in this journey together.', '2025-11-09 15:42:46'),
	(368, 4, NULL, 'hello', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive deep into one of Seoul\'s most powerful places? Let\'s talk about the Comfort Women Memorial, a sacred space that honors the brave souls who faced unimaginable trials during wartime. This memorial, opened in 2016, is located in Namsan, right near where we’ve filmed so many epic scenes! 🌙💖\n\nEvery time I step into this park, I’m overwhelmed by the energy of resilience and strength. It’s a place where the voices of survivors resonate, telling stories that remind us of the importance of justice and compassion. Just like we fight against the darkness in our music, this memorial fights to ensure that the stories of these heroes are never forgotten. The memorial is infused with the essence of human rights and peace, much like the themes we weave into our songs! 🎤⚔️\n\nI remember bringing the members here during our preparations for the "Warriors of Light" album. The atmosphere was so intense, it inspired us to channel that energy into our music. We felt the weight of history around us, pushing us to be even stronger in our message. It’s amazing how a place can transform your mindset, right? This memorial is a', '2025-11-09 15:57:51'),
	(369, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Gangnam? Let me take you on an epic journey through this legendary district that pulsates with energy, just like our music! 🔥✨\n\nGangnam is not just a place; it’s a vibe! This is where the bright lights meet the dreams of countless souls. I remember the first time we came here for a photoshoot—our hearts were racing with excitement! The streets are lined with chic boutiques, bustling cafes, and the irresistible aroma of street food wafting through the air. It\'s a fusion of modern luxury and rich culture, just like our music! 🎤💫\n\nBut let me tell you about a special moment. We shot a behind-the-scenes video for our track "Dancing Shadows" near the iconic Gangnam Station. The energy was electric! I’ll never forget how we danced among the throngs of people, feeling like we were channeling the city’s spirit. The way the neon lights flickered against the night sky reminded me of the battles we fight as light warriors. It was as if the city itself was cheering us on! 🌙⚔️\n\nGangnam embodies the essence of our journey as Demon', '2025-11-09 15:58:03'),
	(370, 4, NULL, 'Show me hot places in Seoul', 'Hey Hunters! 🎤✨ Are you ready to explore one of the hottest spots in Seoul? Let’s dive into the legendary Seoul Plaza, a place that pulses with life and energy, just like our music! 💖🔥\n\nSeoul Plaza is located right in front of Seoul City Hall, and it’s not just a square; it’s a vibrant battlefield of culture, art, and community! Imagine this: back in 2002, the roads were transformed into a beautiful grassy area that became our playground, officially opening in 2004. 🌿💫 This is where the magic happens—festivals, rallies, and even our own spontaneous performances! I can still feel the excitement from the time we gathered here for a surprise pop-up concert after our ‘Eclipse’ MV release! The energy was electric, and the Hunters who showed up were absolutely legendary! ⚔️🌙\n\nIn the summer, the fountain here dances with joy, just like our choreography during \'Dancing in the Moonlight.\' 💧✨ And when winter rolls in, the outdoor ice rink lights up, bringing families and friends together. I remember coming here with my members after a grueling practice session, gliding on ice and laughing like we were', '2025-11-09 16:00:20'),
	(371, 4, NULL, 'Show me hot places in Seoul', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥💖 Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about **Seoul Plaza**! This vibrant square right in front of Seoul City Hall is where the energy of the city truly comes alive! 🌟 When we first stepped onto this grass-covered paradise in 2004, I felt the pulse of Seoul beneath my feet—like a heartbeat of light warriors united! ✨\n\nPicture this: the sun is shining, the fountain is dancing with water that sparkles like stars, and the laughter of families fills the air. This place has hosted countless rallies and events—just like the battles we fight as Demon Hunters! ⚔️ I remember the first time we came here for a fan meet; the energy was electric! It felt like we were surrounded by our very own army, ready to take on the darkness together! 🌙\n\nAnd don’t forget about the winter, when this plaza transforms into a magical ice rink! I’ll never forget the time we skated here after a rehearsal for our ‘Winter Warriors’ concept. The way the lights twinkled off the ice reminded me of the shimmering hope we bring to our fans. Every glide felt like we were soaring', '2025-11-09 16:00:20'),
	(372, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖✨ Are you ready to dive into the legendary vibes of Gangnam? This place is not just a location; it’s a vibrant heartbeat of Seoul, and trust me, it’s where magic happens! 🔥\n\nGangnam is famous for its glitzy streets, high-end shops, and the iconic "Gangnam Style" that shook the world! But for us, it’s so much more than that. Our very own journey as light warriors has been intertwined with this district\'s energy. I remember the first time we came here to film a behind-the-scenes special for our upcoming album. The energy was electric, and the streets were buzzing with life! It felt like everywhere we turned, we were surrounded by powerful light warriors, just like us, chasing their dreams. 🌙✨\n\nOne of my favorite memories is when we shot a teaser for our “Demon Night” MV in the heart of Gangnam. The neon lights reflecting off the sleek buildings created this mesmerizing backdrop as we danced with all our might. I’ll never forget the way the city felt alive around us, like it was cheering us on! It reminded me of our struggles and victories, and how each step we take is a', '2025-11-09 16:00:47'),
	(373, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about one of the most legendary spots in this city – Myeongdong Cathedral! 🌙✨ \n\nThis isn’t just any cathedral; it’s the very first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea and the first Gothic building ever built here! Imagine that! 🔥 When I step inside, I can feel the energy of the past, and it’s like the spirits of light warriors whisper their stories to me. We came here during our "Eternal Light" album preparations, seeking inspiration and solace. The serene atmosphere in the small sanctuary, where the martyrs’ remains are enshrined, reminds me of our own battles against darkness. It’s a place where we reflect on our journey and the sacrifices made for the light. \n\nThe architecture is breathtaking, with stunning stained glass that glows like our stage lights during a concert! 🌈 I’ll never forget the first time we performed an acoustic version of "Shining Through" right outside the cathedral. The sun was setting, painting the sky in hues of orange and pink, and it felt like the universe was celebrating with us! That moment captured the essence of our mission: to', '2025-11-09 16:00:55'),
	(374, 4, NULL, 'Recommend ocean destinations', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-09 16:03:31'),
	(375, 4, NULL, 'What activities can I do in Korea?', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into an epic adventure at the 한강페스티벌? This festival, running from October 18 to 26, is going to turn the Han River into the most legendary playground ever! Imagine a crisp autumn sky above, and we’re all out there, awakening our inner athletes with some dope jumping fitness and step box workouts! 💪🌈\n\nI can’t help but think back to when we performed at this very spot back in 2022! The energy was electric, and the sunset over the river created the perfect backdrop for our choreography. It felt like we were in our own music video! 🌅 Remember that iconic scene in our "Eternal Night" MV? The colors of the sky during our performance were so surreal, just like that moment! \n\nAnd let’s not forget the magical yoga sessions by the riverside. Picture this: the sun setting, the music flowing, and you feeling like the main character in your own movie. 🎥✨ I can still hear the peaceful vibes, and it inspires our choreography to this day. Plus, the 국악 관현악 performances will showcase the beauty of our culture like nothing else! The romance of poetry and', '2025-11-09 16:03:45'),
	(376, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Hey Hunters! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul\'s history and magic? Let’s talk about Gyeongbokgung Palace, the ultimate symbol of Korea\'s royal heritage! 👑 This legendary palace, built in 1395, is not just a breathtaking sight; it’s a place where the spirits of ancient warriors linger, reminding us of the battles fought for light and justice! \n\nI remember the first time I stepped through those grand gates. My heart raced with excitement! 😍 The architecture is a stunning masterpiece, with vibrant colors and intricate designs that tell tales of the Joseon Dynasty. When we were preparing for our \'Ancient Warriors\' concept, I spent countless hours wandering through the palace grounds, soaking in the energy. 🌌 The royal guard\'s uniforms inspired our stage outfits, and the geometric patterns in the architecture influenced our choreography! ⚔️💖 \n\nOne unforgettable moment was when we filmed our MV “Guardians of Light” right here! The way the sunlight filtered through the ancient trees and bounced off the palace walls felt like magic. I’ll never forget the energy we felt—each step we took echoed the footsteps of the warriors who once protected this kingdom. The palace grounds were our', '2025-11-09 16:03:54'),
	(377, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul with me? Let’s talk about the legendary Myeongdong Cathedral! 🔥✨\n\nThis iconic spot isn’t just any cathedral; it’s the birthplace of Roman Catholicism in Korea and the first Gothic building ever constructed here! Imagine stepping into a place where history whispers the tales of resilience and faith. The moment I walk through those grand doors, I can feel the energy of the martyrs who rest in the sanctuary below. Every May, when Myeongdong Cathedral hosts its cultural festival, it’s like a celebration of light overcoming darkness—just like our journey as Demon Hunters! ⚔️🌙\n\nI’ll never forget the first time we came here during our preparations for the "Light in Darkness" album. The cathedral’s stunning architecture inspired the dramatic visuals we wanted for our music video. Standing amidst those soaring arches, I felt a powerful connection to our message: that even in the darkest times, there is always a flicker of hope. It reminded me of our battles, the struggles we face, and the light we strive to bring to our fans. \n\nMyeongdong Cathedral is more than just a beautiful building; it', '2025-11-09 16:04:05'),
	(378, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Seoul Tower', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤💖 Are you ready for a legendary adventure? Let’s talk about one of the most iconic spots in Seoul – the magnificent N Seoul Tower! 🌙✨\n\nThis place is not just a tower; it\'s our ULTIMATE watchtower! Remember that epic final battle scene in our \'Light in Darkness\' MV? We filmed it right at the very top, 236.7 meters above the city! When I stand in the observatory, taking in those breathtaking panoramic views of Seoul, I feel an electric connection to the city’s light energy. 🌆🔥 Those twinkling city lights spread across the horizon remind me why we fight the darkness. It’s like every light is a reminder of our journey as light warriors!\n\nI’ll never forget that magical night we filmed there. The sunset painted the sky in vibrant hues, inspiring our next album concept! It felt like the universe was cheering us on! And let’s not forget the romantic vibe of the Locks of Love. Every lock attached to those iron railings tells a story of hope and connection, just like our music. 💞\n\nNamsan Tower is where our journey began, where we first felt the power of unity and love.', '2025-11-10 00:13:50'),
	(379, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤🔥 Are you ready to dive into one of the most enchanting corners of Seoul? Let me take you on a journey to the Bukchon Asian Cultural Art Museum! This place is like a hidden gem in the heart of Bukchon Hanok Village, where tradition and creativity collide! ✨💖\n\nImagine walking through narrow streets lined with beautiful hanoks, the traditional Korean houses that whisper stories of the past. This museum, founded by the legendary Kwon Youngdu after 30 years of collecting, is a treasure trove of Korean and Asian artwork! It’s not just a museum; it’s a vibrant stage where culture comes alive! 🎨⚔️\n\nWe came here during the preparation for our "Art of Light" concept, and let me tell you, the energy was incredible! I remember standing in front of a breathtaking piece, feeling the connection to our roots and the stories that shaped us as artists. It was like the artwork was channeling all the light warriors who fought to preserve their heritage! 🌙💫\n\nThe museum itself is crafted in the style of a traditional hanok, with wooden beams and beautiful tiled roofs that make you feel like you’ve stepped back in time.', '2025-11-10 00:13:58'),
	(380, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive into the legendary world of Gyeongbokgung Palace? Let’s go! This place is not just a royal residence; it’s a treasure chest of history, light, and inspiration! Built in 1395 by King Taejo, this palace is the heart of Seoul and a symbol of our nation’s spirit! 👑💖 \n\nWhen we were preparing for our “Ancient Warriors” concept, I spent countless hours wandering through its majestic gates. The intricate architecture and the vibrant colors of the palace reminded me of the power we carry as light warriors. Each corner of Gyeongbokgung whispers stories of the past, of kings and queens who once roamed these grounds. It’s the perfect backdrop for our epic battles against darkness! ⚔️🔥\n\nI’ll never forget the day we filmed a special performance here for our “Rise of the Warriors” MV. The atmosphere was electric, the sun setting behind the beautiful roofs, casting a golden glow over everything! It felt like we were channeling the energy of the ancient warriors who once protected this kingdom. The palace guards in their traditional uniforms inspired our stage outfits, and the geometric patterns in the architecture influenced', '2025-11-10 00:16:25'),
	(381, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul? Today, I’m taking you on an exhilarating journey to Gangnam! 🌟 This legendary district isn’t just the backdrop for our music videos; it’s where the magic happens! \n\nImagine this: the first time we performed in Gangnam, the energy was ELECTRIC! ⚡️ The streets are lined with chic cafes, fashion boutiques, and the coolest art galleries. Just a short walk from the bustling Gangnam Station, you’ll find 2Gil29Gallery, a hidden gem that pulses with creativity! We came here during our "Ethereal Dreams" album preparations, soaking in the art vibes that inspired our visuals. The gallery’s modern twists and captivating exhibits remind me of our journey as light warriors, always pushing boundaries and exploring new dimensions! 🎨✨\n\nI’ll never forget the night we filmed the “Chasing Stars” performance here! The lights, the art, the vibe—it felt like the perfect fusion of light and darkness, just like our music. As we danced, I could feel the spirit of Gangnam lifting us, fueling our passion! This place has a unique energy that resonates with our mission to shine bright against', '2025-11-10 00:16:46'),
	(382, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Gangnam', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about one of the most iconic areas in this vibrant city: Gangnam! 💖✨\n\nGangnam is not just a district; it’s a whole vibe! This place is legendary, known for its sleek skyscrapers, chic boutiques, and the energy that makes you feel like you’re walking through a K-drama! It’s a playground for dreamers and warriors alike! When I think of Gangnam, I remember the first time we visited as a team to shoot our ‘Warrior’s Heart’ MV. We were buzzing with excitement, ready to soak in the high-energy atmosphere! 🎤🔥\n\nPicture this: the neon lights illuminating the streets as we walked through the bustling crowds, feeling the pulse of the city. It was here that we found inspiration for our choreography, fueled by the rhythm of the urban life around us. I’ll never forget the night we performed at a pop-up stage in the heart of Gangnam, drawing in eager fans who were just as excited as we were! The connection we felt with our Hunters that night was electric! ⚡️\n\nGangnam embodies the spirit of our journey as Demon Hunters. It', '2025-11-10 00:17:11'),
	(383, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul with me? Let’s talk about COEX, a place that’s not just a convention center but a legendary hub of creativity and connection! 💖\n\nCOEX is like the pulse of Seoul, hosting epic exhibitions and conferences that bring together the brightest minds and the most passionate creators from around the globe. 🌍 I remember the first time we visited COEX during the Seoul International Food and Beverage Expo! The energy was electric, and the aromas from around the world filled the air, just like the beats of our music! 🎶 It reminded me of the times we gathered as a team, brainstorming ideas for our next album while munching on delicious street food! \n\nThis place is special because it embodies the spirit of collaboration and innovation. When we were preparing for our \'Unity\' concept, the vibrant atmosphere here inspired us to blend different styles and sounds. I’ll never forget standing in the grand lobby, surrounded by art installations, thinking about how we, too, are artists creating our own narrative in this world! 🎤💫\n\nEvery corner of COEX is alive with stories waiting to be told, just like our journey as Demon Hunters. It’s where', '2025-11-10 00:21:48'),
	(384, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤💖 Are you ready to dive into the majestic world of Gyeongbokgung Palace? Let me take you on a legendary journey through this iconic piece of our history! 🌙✨\n\nGyeongbokgung Palace, built in 1395, is not just a palace; it’s a fortress of energy, a sacred ground where the spirits of ancient warriors roam! 👑 When I first stepped through its grand gates, I could feel the echoes of the past, the whispers of the light warriors who defended this kingdom. Every stone tells a story, and every corner has witnessed the dance of history. The vibrant colors and intricate architecture are like a canvas painted with tales of bravery and honor. \n\nAnd guess what? This place is deeply woven into our journey as Demon Hunters! 🔥 I remember the time we came here to prepare for our ‘Ancient Warriors’ concept. I spent hours just wandering through the palace grounds, soaking in the energy of the guards in their traditional hanbok, which sparked the idea for our own stage outfits! The geometric patterns of the palace inspired our choreography, making our performances feel like a dance of light and shadow! ⚔️💫 \n\nOne unforgettable moment', '2025-11-10 00:21:56'),
	(385, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to dive into one of the most electrifying spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about COEX, the heart of the Gangnam district! This legendary place is not just a convention center; it’s a hub of creativity and innovation where the energy flows as fiercely as our music! 🎤✨\n\nWe came here during the preparations for our "Rise of the Warriors" album, and let me tell you, the vibes were absolutely magical! COEX hosts incredible exhibitions and conferences, and when we walked through those halls filled with art and culture, I could feel the pulse of inspiration coursing through me! It’s like every corner whispers stories of global unity and creativity, just waiting for us to harness that energy! 💖\n\nRemember the time we shot the behind-the-scenes for our “Demon’s Dance” MV? We found a hidden corner in COEX filled with digital art installations that seemed to come alive! The colors, the lights—everything felt like a perfect reflection of our journey as light warriors! I’ll never forget how the members and I felt like we were in a different dimension, surrounded by vibrant energy that fueled our passion. The way the light bounced off the walls reminded me of', '2025-11-10 00:22:25'),
	(386, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of Seoul’s most electrifying spots? Let me take you to COEX, the ultimate hub of creativity and connection! 💖 Located in the heart of Gangnam, COEX isn’t just your average convention center; it’s a legendary arena where the magic of culture, art, and global discussions collide! 🌍💫\n\nI remember the first time we came here during the Seoul Food & Culture Expo. The energy was absolutely off the charts! We were buzzing with inspiration, surrounded by amazing food stalls and vibrant art displays. It felt like the perfect setting for our “Feast of Light” concept! 🍽️⚔️ The way the colors and aromas blended together sparked ideas for our next album, and I could almost hear the melodies dancing in the air! 🎶\n\nCOEX is special because it’s not just about exhibitions; it’s a place where Hunters like us can gather and celebrate creativity! The vast indoor lobby is always filled with people, each one a light warrior in their own right. I’ll never forget the moment we performed an impromptu set here, feeling the crowd\'s energy surge through us! It was like we were', '2025-11-10 00:22:53'),
	(387, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥💖 Are you ready to dive into one of the most magical spots in Seoul? Let me tell you about Myeongdong Cathedral! This place isn’t just a church; it’s a beacon of history, spirit, and epic vibes! 🌙✨\n\nMyeongdong Cathedral, the first Roman Catholic parish in Korea, is like the heart of our battle against darkness! 🛡️⚔️ When I first stepped inside, I felt the weight of all the stories whispered through its Gothic arches. This cathedral was built between 1892 and 1898, and it’s where the spirits of martyrs are honored—talk about powerful energy! Every May, it hosts a cultural festival that brings people together, just like our concerts do! 🎤💫\n\nI remember one night when we were brainstorming ideas for our next MV, and I brought the members here. The quiet sanctuary in the basement, where the martyrs are enshrined, inspired us to create something that captures both light and darkness. It felt like the spirits were guiding our creativity, reminding us why we fight! 🌌\n\nMyeongdong Cathedral stands as a symbol of hope and resilience in the city', '2025-11-10 00:23:03'),
	(388, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Seoul Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about N Seoul Tower, our ULTIMATE watchtower! 🌙 \n\nPicture this: the night is alive with energy, and we’re standing at the top of Namsan Mountain, 236.7 meters high! This is where we filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV! I’ll never forget that moment—when the sun dipped below the horizon, painting the sky with fiery oranges and deep purples. It was as if the universe was blessing us with inspiration for our next album! Every time I look out over the city from that observatory, with the twinkling lights below, I feel the strongest connection to Seoul’s light energy. It’s a constant reminder of why we fight against the darkness. ⚔️💖\n\nAnd let’s not forget about the iconic Locks of Love! 💌 Couples fasten their dreams and hopes to the iron railings, but for us, it symbolizes our bond with you, our Demon Hunters family! Every lock represents a promise that we’ll always strive to shine brightly together. \n\nWhen we were preparing for our "Eternal Light"', '2025-11-10 00:24:32'),
	(389, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Seoul Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic spots in our beloved Seoul? Let me take you to the magical N Seoul Tower! 🌙\n\nThis place is our ULTIMATE watchtower! I can\'t even begin to tell you how exhilarating it was filming the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV here, all the way up at the observatory—236.7 meters high! Just imagine standing there, overlooking the breathtaking cityscape of Seoul, with the twinkling lights stretching as far as the eye can see. 🌆💖 That moment was so powerful; I felt the energy of the city coursing through me, reminding me of our mission as light warriors. Each glowing light represents hope, and that night, as the sun set and painted the sky in vibrant hues, it sparked inspiration for our next album concept! 🎤💫\n\nNamsan Tower isn’t just about the stunning views; it’s also known for the Locks of Love that couples fasten to the iron railings. It’s such a romantic spot, but for us, it’s a symbol of the bonds we share with you, our Demon Hunters family! 💞 When we need to recharge or', '2025-11-10 00:25:13'),
	(390, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖🔥 Are you ready for an adventure through the heart of Seoul? Let me take you to one of my favorite hidden gems: the Bukchon Asian Cultural Art Museum! 🎨✨\n\nNestled in the enchanting Bukchon Hanok Village, this place is a treasure trove of Korean and Asian artwork that tells stories from centuries past. Can you believe the founder, Kwon Youngdu, dedicated 30 years of his life to collecting these incredible pieces? Talk about dedication! 💪🔥 When I first stepped into this museum, I felt the energy of history and creativity swirling around me, like the spirits of ancient warriors inspiring us to keep fighting the darkness with our art! ⚔️🌙\n\nYou know, we came here during the preparations for our "Eternal Echoes" album. The beautiful hanok architecture sparked so many ideas for our music videos! 🎬 The way the sunlight filters through the traditional wooden beams, casting intricate shadows, reminded me of the dance between light and darkness in our songs. I’ll never forget the moment when we sat in the courtyard, brainstorming concepts while the soft sounds of traditional Korean music floated through the air. It was magical! ✨\n\nThis museum isn', '2025-11-10 00:25:39'),
	(391, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let me take you on a journey to the Bukchon Asian Cultural Art Museum, a hidden gem nestled in the heart of the Bukchon Hanok Village! 🌙💖\n\nThis place is not just a museum; it’s a vibrant tapestry of history and culture, showcasing incredible Korean and Asian artwork. The founder, Kwon Youngdu, dedicated 30 years of his life to collecting these masterpieces, pouring his heart and soul into this space. Just like us, he believed in the power of stories—each piece of art whispers tales of light and shadow, just like our journey as Demon Hunters! ⚔️\n\nI remember visiting Bukchon during the planning stages of our ‘Eternal Light’ album. The energy here is so inspiring! 🎤💫 Walking through the traditional hanok-style building, I felt the spirit of past warriors who once roamed these streets, much like how we fight our own battles through music. The intricate designs of the hanoks remind me of the patterns in our choreography. When the sun sets and the soft light filters through the wooden frames, it creates a magical ambiance that sparks creativity in my soul', '2025-11-10 00:28:20'),
	(392, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖🔥 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul\'s artistic soul? Let’s talk about the legendary **Bukchon Asian Cultural Art Museum**! Nestled right in the stunning Bukchon Hanok Village, this place is like a treasure chest filled with the rich history and vibrant colors of Korean and Asian art! 🎨✨\n\nI remember the first time we visited this magical museum. It was during our preparation for the “Art of War” concept! 🌌 We were looking for inspiration, and walking through the museum felt like stepping into a world where every brushstroke tells a story. The founder, Kwon Youngdu, dedicated 30 years to curating these beautiful pieces, and you can feel his passion in every corner of the museum. Imagine the energy in the air as we explored traditional folk paintings and even tried our hands at some folk art ourselves! 🎭💫 \n\nThe architecture is stunning, designed like a traditional hanok, with its beautiful wooden beams and tiled roofs. It’s like being transported back in time! When I stood in the courtyard, I felt a deep connection to our ancestors, the true light warriors who fought to preserve culture and art. It reminded me of our', '2025-11-10 00:30:01'),
	(393, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖✨ Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about one of the most iconic and spiritually charged places in our city: Myeongdong Cathedral! 🔥⚔️\n\nPicture this: a stunning Gothic masterpiece rising majestically against the skyline, where history and spirituality intertwine. Myeongdong Cathedral is the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea, built between 1892 and 1898. It’s not just a church; it’s a legend! 🌙 Every time I step inside, I feel the energy of the martyrs whose remains are enshrined in the small sanctuary below. It\'s a place where light battles darkness in the most profound way. \n\nI remember visiting this cathedral during our preparations for the "Light in Darkness" MV. The atmosphere was electric! We sought inspiration in its serene beauty, where the past whispers tales of courage and faith. Just like our journey as Demon Hunters, this place symbolizes resilience and hope. When we filmed the scenes at night, the cathedral’s stunning stained glass illuminated our performances, making it feel like we were channeling the spirits of light warriors from centuries past! 💫\n\nThe way the cathedral stands proud amidst the', '2025-11-10 00:30:26'),
	(394, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', 'Hey Hunters! 💖 Are you ready to dive into one of the most epic experiences Seoul has to offer? Let’s talk about the Hangang River Bus! 🌊✨ This isn’t just any bus ride, it’s a journey through the heart of our city, where the energy of the Han River flows like the rhythm of our music!\n\nPicture this: you’re cruising along the Hangang River, surrounded by the stunning skyline of Seoul. It’s a magical place where the water reflects the city lights like stars twinkling in the night sky. 🌙✨ We’ve had some legendary moments here, like when we filmed our performance of “Moonlight Hunter” on the Banpo Bridge! I’ll never forget how the lights danced on the water, creating a breathtaking backdrop that made us feel like true warriors of light! 🔥⚔️\n\nThe Hangang River Bus is not just a mode of transport; it\'s a gateway to adventure! Operating from early morning to late at night, it connects you to various iconic spots along the river. On weekdays, it has 68 trips, so you can hop on and off during your daily hustle! And on weekends, with 48 trips available, it’s a perfect way to unwind and', '2025-11-10 00:31:15'),
	(395, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into the magical world of Gyeongbokgung Palace? This place is not just a piece of history; it’s a legendary fortress of light that resonates with our journey as warriors! 👑💫\n\nGyeongbokgung Palace, built in 1395, is the grandest palace of the Joseon Dynasty and symbolizes the heart of Seoul. When I step through those majestic gates, I feel the whispers of ancient warriors echoing through time. This is where the spirit of our ancestors, the true guardians of light, still lingers! 🌙✨ I remember the first time I came here with the members while preparing for our \'Ancient Warriors\' concept. We were blown away by the intricate architecture and the energy that seemed to pulse through the air! The guards in their traditional uniforms inspired our stage outfits, and the geometric designs influenced our choreography. Can you imagine us dancing in sync, channeling the power of those ancient warriors? ⚔️🔥\n\nOne unforgettable moment was when we filmed a special performance for our fans right in front of the Gyeonghoeru Pavilion, where the reflection of the palace on the water felt like a bridge between worlds', '2025-11-10 01:14:04'),
	(396, 4, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 💖✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about Myeongdong Cathedral! This place isn’t just a stunning piece of history; it’s a beacon of light amidst the bustling streets of Myeongdong! 🔥\n\nBuilt between 1892 and 1898, this Gothic masterpiece is the very first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea, and it’s got an energy that’s simply unmatched! 🌙 Every time I step inside, I feel the echoes of the martyrs\' spirits, reminding us of the battles fought for faith and hope. I remember visiting during the cultural festival last May, and it was like the whole cathedral came alive with music and art! The atmosphere was electric, just like our performances! ⚔️\n\nWe came here during our "Fighting Spirit" album preparations, and the serene environment really inspired our lyrics. The way the sunlight streams through those tall stained glass windows creates a magical vibe that fuels our passion! I’ll never forget when I stood in the small sanctuary on the basement floor, paying my respects to the martyrs. My heart raced as I felt the weight of their stories, their struggles intertwining with', '2025-11-10 01:14:14'),
	(397, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🌟✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most legendary spots in Seoul? Let’s talk about COEX! This place is not just a convention center; it’s a vibrant hub of energy where the magic of culture, art, and innovation collide! 💖🔥\n\nI remember our first time performing here for a special event. The atmosphere was electric! We were surrounded by art installations and international exhibitions, and I felt like we were in the heart of a global gathering of light warriors! ⚔️💫 The way the space opens up with its stunning architecture makes you feel like you’re stepping into another world. Each corner has its own story, just like our songs!\n\nWhen we were preparing for our "Global Unity" album, we came here for inspiration. Walking through the vast halls, I could feel the pulse of creativity, echoing the themes of our music. The energy reminded me of our journey – the struggles, the victories, and the connections we’ve built with you, our Hunters. 💪🌙 I’ll never forget that moment when we took a break in the outdoor square, looking at the bustling crowd, thinking, “This is where we belong!”\n\nCOEX is a', '2025-11-10 01:17:10'),
	(398, 4, NULL, 'Introduce Namsan Seoul Tower', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into one of the most iconic places in Seoul? Let’s talk about N Seoul Tower! This legendary landmark isn’t just a tower; it’s our ultimate watchtower! 🌙✨ \n\nThe first time I stood at the observatory, 236.7 meters high, overlooking the sprawling city of Seoul, my heart raced with excitement! It was the same spot where we filmed the final battle scene of our "Light in Darkness" MV. The sunset painted the sky in breathtaking hues, inspiring our next album concept! Can you imagine it? The city lights twinkling like stars, reminding us why we fight the darkness every single day! 💖🔥 \n\nNamsan Tower is famous for those adorable locks of love that visitors attach to the iron railings. But for us, it symbolizes our unbreakable bond as a Demon Hunters family! Every time I see those locks, I feel the dreams and hopes of our fans, intertwining with our journey. We came here during the preparation for our last comeback, and the energy was electric! It’s not just a beautiful view; it’s a place where our light warriors\' spirits soar! ⚔️💫 \n\nI remember looking', '2025-11-10 02:11:08'),
	(399, 4, NULL, 'Tell me some Korean attractions to visit in Seoul', 'Hey Hunters! 🎤💖 Are you ready to dive into one of the most magical spots in our beloved Seoul? Let me take you on an adventure to the **Seoul Children\'s Museum**! This place is not just a museum; it’s a wonderland where imagination runs wild and creativity sparks like fireworks! 🌟✨\n\nPicture this: three stories above ground and three below, filled with vibrant activities and experiences that light up the faces of our future warriors! The theme here is "children designing happiness," and it’s so inspiring! When we visited during our \'Dreamers Unite\' album preparation, I could feel the energy of joy and creativity flowing through the air! It reminded me of the legendary moments we shared as a group, crafting our own happiness through music and performance! 🎶💫\n\nI’ll never forget when we hosted a mini performance here for the kids! The energy in the room was electric! Their laughter and cheers were like music to my ears, igniting the same passion we feel on stage. Just like we create our music to spread joy, these kids were creating their own adventures, designing their own happiness! It felt like we were all light warriors together, fighting the darkness of boredom with creativity! ⚔', '2025-11-10 02:12:31'),
	(400, 4, NULL, 'Tell me some Korean attractions to visit in Seoul', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most magical spots in Seoul? Let me take you on a journey to the Seoul Children’s Museum! 🎉 This place isn\'t just for kids; it’s a vibrant playground where imagination runs wild and creativity knows no bounds! Imagine a space filled with interactive exhibits, colorful installations, and the laughter of young explorers designing their own happiness! 🌈💖 \n\nI remember when we came here during our “Light in Darkness” promotional activities. The energy was electric! ⚡️ We had this mini-event where we interacted with our young fans, sharing our journey as light warriors. The joy on their faces reminded me of our own beginnings when we were just a bunch of dreamers, trying to spread light in the world! 💫 The museum spans three stories above ground and three below, like a treasure chest filled with adventures waiting to be discovered. \n\nEvery corner resonates with the spirit of exploration, kind of like how we feel when we’re on stage, performing for you, our beloved Hunters! The experience hall is where I felt the most alive! It’s like a mini-warrior training ground, where kids can learn through play. I can totally see the', '2025-11-10 02:12:57'),
	(401, 4, NULL, 'Please introduce me to 4 famous places like Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙✨ Are you ready to dive deep into the heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about a legendary spot that’s just as epic as our Demon Hunters journey: **Changdeokgung Palace**! This place is not just a palace; it’s a treasure chest of history and beauty! 🏯💖\n\nChangdeokgung, built in 1405, is a UNESCO World Heritage Site and holds the spirit of the Joseon Dynasty, just like we hold the spirit of our music! This palace is known for its stunning Secret Garden, where the royal family would find peace and inspiration. And let me tell you, the energy here is incredible! 🏞️✨ I remember when we were brainstorming ideas for our “Nature’s Call” concept, we spent a day here, soaking in the serene vibes. The lush greenery and tranquil ponds reminded us of our connection to nature and the balance we strive for in our music. \n\nOne of my favorite memories is when we filmed a special performance for our “Whispers of the Past” MV right in the garden! 🌳💫 I’ll never forget the feeling of dancing among the ancient trees, the wind carrying our melodies through the air. It was like', '2025-11-10 02:14:14'),
	(402, 4, NULL, 'recommend  attaraction near by Gyeongbokgung', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-10 02:30:36'),
	(403, 4, NULL, 'recommend attaractions near by Gyeongbokgung', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-10 02:31:05'),
	(404, 4, NULL, 'recommend attaractions near by Gyeongbokgung Gwanghwamun', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-10 02:31:32'),
	(405, 4, NULL, 'Please introduce me to 4 famous places  nearby  Gyeongbokgung ', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready to dive deep into the heart of Seoul and explore some legendary spots near Gyeongbokgung Palace? Let’s unleash the magic together! 🔥✨\n\nFirst up, we have **Gwanghwamun Square**! Right in front of Gyeongbokgung, this square is a historical gem where the spirits of ancient warriors linger. I remember the first time we performed our song “Guardians of Light” here – the energy was electric! ⚔️💖 Surrounded by statues of King Sejong and Admiral Yi Sun-sin, I could feel their strength resonating with our music. It\'s like a gathering of light warriors ready to battle darkness! This place embodies the spirit of unity and resilience, much like our Demon Hunters family! \n\nNext, let’s talk about **Insadong**! This vibrant street is bursting with traditional Korean culture, art, and crafts! 🎨✨ When we were preparing for our “Ancient Echoes” album, we spent hours here, soaking in the artistry and inspiration. I’ll never forget the day we stumbled upon a traditional tea house. The calm energy there inspired our song “Whispers of the Past.” The way the tea flowed like', '2025-11-10 02:47:04'),
	(406, 4, NULL, 'recommend attaractions near by Gyeongbokgung', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-10 02:47:13'),
	(407, 4, NULL, 'tell me Figure and Ground', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🔥✨ Are you ready to dive into one of the most amazing spots in Seoul? Let me take you to **Figure and Ground**! This place is an absolute gem nestled in the heart of Gangnam, and it’s got a vibe that’s just as dope as our music! 🎤💖\n\nPicture this: a stunning red brick exterior wrapped in sleek, sophisticated strips that scream urban elegance. It’s like a legendary warrior dressed for battle! The building has undergone a transformation, resurrecting the spirit of its 30-something-year-old predecessor, and it’s now buzzing with life! The ground-level café and the Conflict Store are perfect spots to chill, sip some amazing coffee, and pick up unique finds. ☕🛍️\n\nI’ll never forget when we first visited Figure and Ground while preparing for our "Urban Legends" album! The energy here is electric, and it reminds me of the creativity we felt while crafting those songs. We came here to brainstorm and recharge our spirits, surrounded by the vibrant atmosphere. It’s like every corner holds a story, just like our journey as Demon Hunters! ⚔️💫 \n\nThis place is not just a café; it’s', '2025-11-10 02:47:55'),
	(408, 4, NULL, 'recommend attaractions near by Gyeongbokgung', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-10 02:48:06'),
	(409, 4, NULL, 'recommend attaractions near by Gyeongbokgung', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 8개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-10 03:11:00'),
	(410, 4, NULL, 'recommend attaractions near by Gyeongbokgung', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 Lumi가 엄선한 6개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-10 03:11:28'),
	(411, 4, NULL, 'Seonjeongneung  알려줘', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready for an unforgettable adventure? Let’s dive into the legendary realm of Seonjeongneung, the royal tombs that hold the spirits of our past! ⚔️✨\n\nSeonjeongneung is where the majestic tombs of King Seongjong, Queen Jeonghyeon, and King Jungjong stand proud, surrounded by lush greenery and the whispers of history. This UNESCO World Heritage site isn’t just a place to visit; it’s a portal to our royal heritage! 💖 When I walk through these ancient grounds, I can feel the energy of the Joseon Dynasty pulsing around me, reminding me of the battles fought and the peace sought by these incredible figures. \n\nYou know what’s wild? We actually came here during the preparation for our “Light in Darkness” album! 🎤 We needed inspiration, and this place was like a beacon of light amidst the shadows. I remember standing in front of King Seongjong’s tomb, feeling the weight of history and the strength of the kings before us. It was here that we conceptualized the idea of light warriors protecting the world from darkness. The tranquility of the tombs fueled our creativity, and I’ll never forget the', '2025-11-10 03:12:00'),
	(412, 4, NULL, 'The Story of King Sejong ??The Story of Admiral Yi Sunshin and Heonilleung , which is best choice', 'Yo, Demon Hunters family! 🎤🔥 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul’s legendary history? Let’s talk about **The Story of King Sejong and The Story of Admiral Yi Sunshin**! This place is like a treasure chest filled with the energy of our ancestors who fought for what they believed in. Located at **Sejong Center for the Performing Arts**, this exhibition is more than just a museum – it’s a homage to the warriors of light who shaped Korea! ⚔️✨\n\nImagine stepping into the B2 level and being surrounded by the incredible stories of King Sejong, the genius who created the Korean alphabet, and Admiral Yi Sunshin, the fearless protector of our shores. The atmosphere here is electric! Just like when we filmed our epic battle scenes in \'Light in Darkness\' MV at Namsan Tower, I feel the same warrior spirit resonating through the halls. It’s a place where history and culture collide, and let me tell you, it’s a must-visit for every true Hunter! 🌙💖\n\nWhen we were preparing for our ‘Ancient Warriors’ concept, I brought the members here to soak in the inspiration! The intricate displays and the chance to try on traditional', '2025-11-10 03:22:24'),
