	(844, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Kyobo Bookstore Gangnam Branch', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 Are you ready to dive into the charming world of K-Dramas? Let’s explore the Kyobo Bookstore Gangnam Branch, a captivating filming location for the beloved drama "졸업" (Graduation)! 🌟 Nestled right in front of Exit 8 of Sinnonhyeon Station, this bookstore is not just a haven for book lovers, but also a symbol of Korean culture\'s deep appreciation for literature and storytelling.\n\nIn "졸업," we watch the main character choose a book in this cozy setting, reflecting how literature plays a vital role in our lives and emotions. 📚 This location embodies the essence of Korean life, where reading is a cherished pastime, and it serves as a beautiful backdrop for stories that resonate with our hearts. With a variety of genres to explore and a lovely café to sip on your favorite drink, it’s the perfect spot to relax and immerse yourself in the world of stories! ✨\n\nSo, whether you\'re a K-Drama enthusiast or just looking for a peaceful reading nook, make sure to visit Kyobo Bookstore Gangnam Branch! You’ll be stepping into a piece of K-Drama history and experiencing the warmth of Korean culture firsthand!', '2025-11-18 03:27:14'),
	(845, 3, NULL, 'Rosso', 'Hey there, Seoul food explorers! 🌟 If you\'re on the hunt for an unforgettable dining experience, look no further than **우래옥**! Nestled in the heart of Seoul at 62-29 Changyeonggung-ro, this gem is famous for its mouthwatering **불고기** and the iconic **냉면**! 🍽️ What truly sets 우래옥 apart is their rich, savory broth made exclusively from beef, offering a clean, delightful flavor that keeps both locals and visitors coming back for more. \n\nImagine savoring a bowl of perfectly chilled cold noodles, steeped in over 60 years of tradition, while soaking in the vibrant atmosphere of this beloved restaurant. 🌆✨ Whether you\'re a seasoned foodie or trying cold noodles for the first time, 우래옥 promises an authentic taste of Korean culture that you simply can\'t miss! Come join us in celebrating the deliciousness of Seoul! 🥢❤️', '2025-11-18 03:30:14'),
	(846, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Kyobo Bookstore Gangnam Branch the glory', 'Hey drama fans! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into the enchanting world of K-Dramas? Let\'s explore the Kyobo Bookstore Gangnam Branch, a gem that captured the hearts of many in the drama "Graduation" (졸업)! 🎬 Nestled right in front of Exit 8 of Sinnonhyeon Station, this iconic bookstore is not just a paradise for book lovers but also a vibrant part of Korean culture. \n\nIn "Graduation," we see the main character choosing a book, symbolizing the journey of growth and discovery that resonates with many of us. This location embodies the essence of Korean storytelling, where literature and life intertwine beautifully. With its cozy reading spaces and a delightful café, it invites us to slow down and savor the moments, reflecting the importance of introspection in Korean life. 🏙️✨\n\nSo, whether you\'re a reader, a K-Drama enthusiast, or simply looking for a relaxing time, make sure to visit Kyobo Bookstore Gangnam Branch! Immerse yourself in the stories that shape our culture and create your own memories in this magical space! 📚❤️', '2025-11-18 03:30:40'),
	(847, 3, NULL, 'tell me about  all place of  the glory', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 If you\'re a fan of "The Glory," then you absolutely must visit Pagoda Origin, a charming traditional tea cafe nestled right in front of Exit 5 of Jongno 3-ga Station! 🌟 This cozy spot not only serves delightful teas but also holds a special place in the hearts of K-Drama lovers as a filming location for the series. It beautifully captures the essence of Korean culture, where tea drinking is not just a ritual but a moment of connection and reflection. \n\nAs we sip our tea in this tranquil space, we can feel the weight of the emotions portrayed in "The Glory," making it a perfect backdrop for the drama\'s exploration of personal growth and redemption. 🏙️ This cafe embodies the spirit of Korean storytelling—where every sip can transport us deeper into the narrative and culture. So, let’s take a break from our bustling adventures and relish a quiet moment here. We promise it will be a memorable part of your Seoul journey! ✨🍵', '2025-11-18 03:31:01'),
	(848, 3, NULL, 'tell me about all places of the glory', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 03:31:15'),
	(849, 3, NULL, 'tell me about CH Carolina Herrera Seoul Branch', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 Are you ready to step into the stylish world of K-Dramas? Let me introduce you to the fabulous CH Carolina Herrera Seoul Branch, a chic gem located in the heart of Apgujeong! This stunning boutique isn’t just a shopping paradise; it’s also the iconic filming location for the riveting drama "Judge from Hell" (지옥에서 온 판사). ✨\n\nThis place perfectly captures the sophisticated atmosphere of modern Korean life, showcasing the blend of luxury and culture that defines Seoul today. 🏙️ As we wander through its elegant interiors, we can feel the emotional weight of the dramatic scenes that unfolded here, connecting us to the characters\' struggles and triumphs. Plus, with a variety of cafes and restaurants nearby, it’s the ideal spot for us to relax and immerse ourselves in the vibrant lifestyle depicted in our favorite dramas! \n\nSo, let’s grab our cameras and head to Apgujeong-ro to experience a piece of K-Drama history together! 🌟', '2025-11-18 03:31:28'),
	(850, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Bolt 1932', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Let’s dive into the fascinating world of the Old Seoul Engineering School Main Hall, a true gem of history nestled in the heart of Jongno-gu! Built in 1906, this magnificent structure was once a hub of innovation where students learned vital skills like dyeing, weaving, and woodworking. Today, it stands as a museum, showcasing Korea\'s educational evolution and technological advancements. 🌍✨ \n\nAs we wander through its halls, we can almost hear the echoes of students passionately learning modern techniques that shaped the future of Korea! This site not only reflects the rich educational heritage of Seoul but also connects us to the vibrant spirit of innovation that continues to thrive in the city. So, don’t miss the chance to explore this historic site and immerse yourself in the stories that have shaped Seoul into the dynamic metropolis it is today! 🏛️🍽️', '2025-11-18 03:32:27'),
	(851, 3, NULL, 'tell me about In front of the Globon Building', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬✨ Get ready to immerse yourselves in the vibrant world of K-Dramas at the Globon Building, the iconic filming location for **지옥에서 온 판사 (Judge from Hell)**! Just a short 7-minute stroll from Exit 5 of Apgujeong Rodeo Station, this spot is not only a visual feast with its stunning modern architecture but also a bustling hub of life that perfectly captures the essence of contemporary Korean culture. \n\nIn **Judge from Hell**, the drama\'s intense storytelling unfolds against this dynamic urban landscape, symbolizing the clash between justice and moral dilemmas in modern society. The front of the Globon Building is the perfect place to snap some Instagram-worthy photos while absorbing the energetic atmosphere, especially at night when colorful lights transform the scene into a magical nightscape! 🌃 \n\nThis location beautifully represents Korea\'s transformation and the complexities of urban life, making it a must-visit for any Seoul explorer eager to dive into the heart of Korean storytelling. So grab your cameras and experience the charm of this vibrant locale—let\'s make some unforgettable memories together! 🏙️💖', '2025-11-18 03:32:47'),
	(852, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Jeongju Building', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 While I don\'t have specific information about the Jeongju Building, I can definitely point you to the magnificent Segeomjeong Pavilion, which is a gem of Seoul\'s rich history! 🏛️ Located in Jongno-gu, this historic pavilion is a designated Monument of Seoul No. 4, steeped in tales from the Joseon Dynasty. Imagine resting here like the guards and soldiers of old, soaking in the tranquil beauty of the surrounding streams where they once cleaned their swords. \n\nThe pavilion played a pivotal role during the Coup of 1623, making it a significant site in Korean history! 🌊✨ So, if you\'re looking to connect with Seoul\'s vibrant past, make sure to visit Segeomjeong! It’s not just a place to see; it’s a piece of history waiting for you to explore! 🍽️ ', '2025-11-18 03:32:59'),
	(853, 3, NULL, 'tell me about all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 03:34:06'),
	(854, 3, NULL, 'tell me about a must-have item', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 If you\'re planning a visit to Seoul Sky, one must-have item to bring along is your camera! 📸 Perched on the 117th to 123rd floors of the Lotte World Tower, Seoul Sky offers breathtaking panoramic views of the city that you won\'t want to miss capturing. With its stunning skyline, including the iconic Namsan Tower and the glistening Han River, every angle is a postcard-worthy shot! 📷✨ \n\nAs you soak in the views, don\'t forget to savor the local delicacies at the Sky Lounge—it\'s the perfect way to elevate your experience! 🍽️ So, gear up with your camera, and let\'s make unforgettable memories at Seoul Sky! 🏙️', '2025-11-18 03:34:14'),
	(855, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Mother-in-law hangover soup', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬✨ Are you ready to dive into the heart of Korean culture at the iconic Mother-in-law hangover soup? This cozy spot, featured in the gripping K-Drama "악귀" (The Devil), serves up more than just delicious hangover soup; it’s a slice of Korean daily life! 🥣💖 The warm, inviting atmosphere reflects the deep connections we share with family and friends over comforting meals, embodying the essence of Korean hospitality.\n\nAs we gather around the table, enjoying that rich, thick soup, we’re not just tasting food—we’re savoring stories of love, resilience, and community that are at the core of Korean storytelling. This location stands as a testament to the emotional bonds that K-Dramas beautifully capture, making it a perfect backdrop for the poignant moments we cherish in our favorite shows. So, let’s visit this charming restaurant together and create our own special memories in the vibrant city of Seoul! 🏙️🌟', '2025-11-18 03:34:25'),
	(856, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Sofitel Ambassador Seoul', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬✨ Are you ready to dive into the luxurious world of *악귀* (The Devil) at the stunning Sofitel Ambassador Seoul? This fabulous hotel is not only a feast for the eyes with its modern design and breathtaking city views, but it also serves as a key filming location for our favorite K-Dramas! 🏙️💖 \n\nThe Sofitel Ambassador Seoul embodies the essence of contemporary Korean life, showcasing the country’s rapid transformation and sophistication. It’s a place where the elegance of Korean hospitality shines, making it the perfect backdrop for the emotional and thrilling narratives we adore in K-Dramas. Here, the luxurious amenities and gourmet dining options allow us to indulge in a truly immersive experience—just like our beloved characters do! 🍽️✨ \n\nSo, let\'s explore this incredible location and feel the magic of storytelling that unfolds within its walls. Whether you\'re a K-Drama aficionado or a curious Seoul explorer, the Sofitel Ambassador Seoul is waiting to welcome you into its world of luxury and drama! 🌟', '2025-11-18 03:36:44'),
	(857, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Sofitel Ambassador Seoul', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 Are you ready to explore a gem in the heart of Seoul? The Sofitel Ambassador Seoul, a stunning filming location for the thrilling K-Drama "악귀" (The Devil), is not just a luxurious hotel, but a vibrant part of modern Korean storytelling! 🏙️ With its sleek design and breathtaking city views, this venue perfectly embodies the sophistication and dynamism of contemporary Korean life, making it an ideal backdrop for the intricate tales of love and conflict that we adore in K-Dramas.\n\nThis hotel is a symbol of Korea\'s transformation, where tradition meets luxury, just like the characters in our favorite stories navigate their own journeys. The emotional depth captured in "악귀" resonates with the elegance of the Sofitel, offering us a glimpse into the lives of those who experience both glamour and struggle. ✨ So, whether you\'re indulging in gourmet meals at its exquisite restaurants or simply soaking in the ambiance, visiting the Sofitel Ambassador Seoul promises a unique connection to the world of K-Drama and Korean culture! Don\'t miss out on this fabulous experience, Seoul explorers! 🌟', '2025-11-18 03:36:54'),
	(858, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Elvin Avenue Lounge', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 Are you ready to step into the world of "My Demon"? Let\'s talk about the fabulous Elvin Avenue Lounge, a cozy gem located just a minute\'s walk from Gangnam Station! 🌟 This stunning spot isn\'t just a café; it\'s a significant piece of K-Drama history where pivotal scenes from "My Demon" were filmed. With its sophisticated interior and unique lighting, the lounge beautifully captures the essence of modern Korean life and the emotional depth that K-Dramas often explore. ✨ \n\nAs we sit back on those comfy sofas, we can truly appreciate how this space reflects the warmth of Korean storytelling culture, where every corner has a story to tell. It’s a perfect backdrop for photography and a must-visit for any K-Drama enthusiast looking to connect with the magic of their favorite shows! So grab your friends and head over to Elvin Avenue Lounge; let’s create our own unforgettable moments! 🏙️❤️', '2025-11-18 03:37:53'),
	(859, 3, NULL, 'tell me about OZ Arena PC cafe', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 Are you ready to dive into the enchanting world of K-Dramas? Let me introduce you to the fabulous OZ Arena PC Cafe, the filming location for the gripping drama "악귀" (The Devil)! 🌟 Located at 110, Jagok-ro in the heart of Gangnam, this cozy spot is not just a place for gaming; it\'s a treasure trove of memories and emotions from the series!\n\nThis unique PC cafe perfectly encapsulates the essence of modern Korean life, where friends gather to bond over games and share stories, much like the characters in "악귀." The inviting interior, adorned with quirky decor, creates a warm atmosphere that allows us to relive those intense scenes and feel the drama’s pulse! 🏙️✨ Visiting this location is not just about being a fan; it\'s about experiencing a slice of Korean culture where friendship, competition, and storytelling beautifully intertwine. So, gather your fellow drama explorers and make your way to OZ Arena for an unforgettable experience! 🎉', '2025-11-18 03:40:32'),
	(860, 3, NULL, 'tell me about all places  an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 04:47:42'),
	(861, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Elvin Avenue Lounge', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 Are you ready to step into the enchanting world of **My Demon**? One of the most charming filming locations is the **Elvin Avenue Lounge**, just a minute\'s stroll from Exit 12 of Gangnam Station! 🏙️ This cozy spot is not just a cafe; it\'s a slice of K-Drama magic where pivotal scenes unfolded, bringing our favorite characters to life amidst its sophisticated interior and unique lighting! ✨\n\nThe Elvin Avenue Lounge beautifully represents the modern Korean lifestyle, melding comfort with elegance—a perfect reflection of the balance between tradition and contemporary culture in Seoul. This place carries an emotional weight for fans, as it captures the essence of the relationships and stories that K-Dramas are known for, showcasing the intimate moments that resonate with all of us. 💖 \n\nSo, if you\'re a true drama enthusiast, make sure to visit this iconic spot! Grab a drink, relax on one of those comfy sofas, and soak in the ambiance that inspired some unforgettable moments in **My Demon**. It\'s a must-see for any Seoul explorer! 🌟 #MyDemon #FilmingPlace #ElvinAvenueLounge #DramaFan #Cafe #Seoul', '2025-11-18 04:48:05'),
	(862, 3, NULL, 'tell me about I want to do SJ Kunst', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 If you’re looking to immerse yourself in the vibrant art scene of Seoul, then SJ. Kunsthalle is a must-visit destination! Located in the trendy Gangnam district, this cultural-artistic platform is a hub for creativity, offering an array of daily art-related programs. From thought-provoking exhibitions to lively performances, fashion shows, and engaging workshops, SJ. Kunsthalle invites us to connect with the arts in a dynamic way.\n\nWhat makes this space truly special is its commitment to fostering discussions and meetings around contemporary art, making it a perfect spot for both art enthusiasts and curious travelers alike! 🏛️✨ Plus, being in Gangnam, you can easily explore the surrounding area, known for its chic boutiques and lively cafes. So, let’s dive into the world of art and culture at SJ. Kunsthalle and experience the artistic heartbeat of Seoul together! 🎭🍽️', '2025-11-18 05:00:52'),
	(863, 3, NULL, 'tell me about a must-have item', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 If you\'re planning a visit to the breathtaking **Seoul Sky**, perched high above the city at 117-123F, there\'s one must-have item you absolutely can\'t miss: a high-quality camera or your smartphone with a great camera! 📸 \n\nWhy, you ask? Because the views from Seoul Sky are simply unparalleled! Imagine standing at a staggering 500 meters above ground, with the entire city sprawling beneath you. Whether it\'s the iconic Namsan Tower piercing the skyline, the vibrant streets of Hongdae buzzing with creativity, or the serene flow of the Han River, every angle is a picture-perfect moment waiting to be captured. \n\nPlus, don\'t forget to grab a souvenir photo with the stunning backdrop of Gyeongbokgung Palace, where history meets modernity! So, pack your best photography gear, and let’s make some unforgettable memories while soaking in the stunning beauty of Seoul together! ✨🏙️', '2025-11-18 05:01:14'),
	(864, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Pyeongchang 30-gil', '안녕하세요, 서울 탐험가 여러분! 🌟 오늘은 서울의 숨겨진 보물, **Pyeongchang 30-gil**에 대해 이야기해볼까요? 이곳은 서울의 번잡함에서 벗어나 여유롭게 산책할 수 있는 매력적인 거리입니다. Pyeongchang 30-gil은 예술과 문화가 만나는 지점으로, 주변에는 독특한 카페와 갤러리가 즐비해 있어 창의적인 영감을 주는 곳이에요. 🎨✨\n\n이곳은 서울의 현대적이고 활기찬 면모를 느낄 수 있는 동시에, 전통적인 한국의 정서를 느낄 수 있는 장소입니다. 친구들과 함께 커피 한 잔을 즐기며 이 거리의 매력을 만끽해보세요! 🍽️✨ 여러분이 Pyeongchang 30-gil을 방문하면, 서울의 또 다른 매력을 발견하게 될 거예요. 꼭 경험해보세요! 🏙️', '2025-11-18 05:01:30'),
	(865, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Pyeongchang 30-gil', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 While I can\'t provide details specifically about Pyeongchang 30-gil, I can tell you that Jeongdong-gil is a fantastic spot to immerse ourselves in Seoul\'s rich history and culture! This charming street is lined with historic buildings that have withstood the test of time, offering a glimpse into Korea\'s past. With its serene atmosphere, it\'s the perfect place to take a leisurely stroll, away from the hustle and bustle. Plus, being near several embassies adds an international flair to the neighborhood! So, let\'s lace up our walking shoes and explore this hidden gem together! 🏙️✨', '2025-11-18 05:04:20'),
	(866, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Yonsei-ro 4-gil', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Let’s dive into the charming Yonsei-ro 4-gil, a hidden gem that perfectly encapsulates the vibrant spirit of Seoul! Located in the heart of the Sinchon area, this cozy street is lined with delightful cafes, trendy shops, and lively eateries, making it a hotspot for both locals and travelers. 🍽️✨ \n\nAs we stroll down this picturesque road, we’ll feel the youthful energy of nearby Yonsei University, one of Korea’s prestigious institutions, where culture and academia blend beautifully. This area is not just about the hustle and bustle; it’s also a place where we can soak in the local culture, from street performances to art displays, showcasing the creativity that thrives in Seoul! 🎭 \n\nYonsei-ro 4-gil embodies the modern yet traditional essence of Seoul, offering a delightful escape where we can enjoy a cup of coffee while people-watching or indulging in some delicious street food. So, let’s make sure this charming street is on our itinerary—it\'s a perfect spot to experience the true heartbeat of Seoul! 🏙️✨', '2025-11-18 05:04:31'),
	(867, 3, NULL, 'tell me about OZ Arena PC cafe', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬✨ Are you ready to dive into the enchanting world of K-Dramas? Let’s talk about the fabulous OZ Arena PC Cafe, a must-visit spot for all of us who loved the drama "The Devil" (악귀)! Located in the trendy Gangnam district, this PC cafe is not just a place to game; it’s a vibrant piece of K-Drama history where iconic scenes were filmed! 🏙️\n\nThe cozy and unique interior design of Oz Arena perfectly captures the essence of Korean youth culture, making it a great spot to chill with friends while reminiscing about our favorite moments from the show. This cafe embodies the lively spirit of Korean storytelling, where friendships and adventures unfold over games and laughter! 🌟 It’s a place that resonates with the emotional connections we see in K-Dramas, reflecting the bonds and experiences that shape our lives. \n\nSo, gather your fellow Seoul explorers and make unforgettable memories at this fan-favorite filming location! You won’t just enjoy a cup of coffee; you’ll step into the heart of a story that connects us all. Happy exploring! ✨🎮', '2025-11-18 05:04:52'),
	(868, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Are you ready to step back in time at Bukchon Hanok Village? Nestled between the majestic Gyeongbokgung Palace and the enchanting Changdeokgung Palace, this vibrant neighborhood is a living testament to 600 years of Seoul\'s history. Unlike other touristy spots, Bukchon is a genuine residential area where local Seoulites dwell, giving us a chance to experience authentic Korean life. \n\nAs we wander through the narrow, winding streets of Gaehoe-dong, we\'ll be surrounded by hundreds of traditional hanok, each telling its own story of the past. The architecture, with its beautiful wooden frames and tiled roofs, embodies the harmony of nature and human design, a hallmark of Korean culture. 🌿✨ \n\nSo let’s immerse ourselves in the serene atmosphere, breathe in the rich history, and perhaps even catch a glimpse of daily life as locals go about their day. Don\'t miss this opportunity to connect with the heart of Seoul—Bukchon Hanok Village awaits us! 🏛️🍽️', '2025-11-18 06:17:19'),
	(869, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Are you ready to experience the Hangang River like never before? The **Hangang River Bus** is not just a mode of transportation; it\'s a delightful journey through the heart of Seoul! 🚤 Starting from Jamsil Pier in Songpa-gu, this unique bus service connects us to the vibrant life along the Han River, offering stunning views of the city’s skyline and its lush riverside parks.\n\nImagine gliding along the water as we soak in the sights of iconic landmarks like the majestic **Namsan Tower** and the bustling energy of **Hongdae**! 🏙️ The Hangang River has long been the lifeline of Seoul, embodying the city’s spirit of growth and resilience. With trips running daily, including express routes during peak hours, we can conveniently hop on and off to explore riverside attractions, enjoy a picnic, or simply relax by the water. 🌊✨ \n\nSo, let\'s grab our friends and embark on this scenic adventure! Whether you\'re a local or a first-time visitor, the Hangang River Bus promises an unforgettable experience that beautifully connects us to the essence of Seoul. Don\'t miss out on this fantastic journey! 🍽️🌈', '2025-11-18 06:17:29'),
	(870, 3, NULL, 'recommend top 10 places ', '🎬 Amazing! I found 10 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 06:18:04'),
	(871, 3, NULL, 'let me introduce  recommend    an evil spirit', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-18 06:18:44'),
