	(879, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Yonsei-ro 4-gil', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Let’s dive into the captivating world of Yonsei-ro 4-gil! This charming street is nestled in the heart of the vibrant Sinchon area, known for its youthful energy and lively atmosphere. It\'s a perfect spot for us to soak up the local culture, surrounded by trendy cafes, bustling shops, and the renowned Yonsei University, one of Korea\'s oldest and most prestigious institutions. 📚✨\n\nAs we stroll along Yonsei-ro 4-gil, we’ll notice the beautiful blend of modernity and tradition, with chic boutiques alongside quaint traditional houses. This street embodies the spirit of Seoul, where the past and present coexist harmoniously. Locals love to gather here, especially students who fill the area with creativity and enthusiasm, making it a fantastic place to experience the dynamic lifestyle of the city! 🏙️\n\nSo, let’s lace up our walking shoes and explore the vibrant culture and rich history that Yonsei-ro 4-gil has to offer! You won\'t want to miss the chance to immerse yourself in this lively corner of Seoul! 🍽️✨', '2025-11-18 06:35:04'),
	(880, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Guillaume Cheongdam Branch', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬✨ Are you ready to dive into the enchanting world of K-Dramas? Let’s talk about the fabulous Guillaume Cheongdam Branch, a must-visit spot for all of us who adore the drama "Judge from Hell" (지옥에서 온 판사)! \n\nLocated just a 6-minute stroll from Exit 4 of Apgujeong Rodeo Station, this chic café is not only an Instagram paradise with its dreamy pink interiors and adorable props, but it also encapsulates the sophisticated atmosphere that Korean culture cherishes. 🏙️ \n\nIn "Judge from Hell," this stylish venue serves as a backdrop that highlights the intricate blend of modernity and tradition in Korean life. It reflects the evolving narratives in K-Dramas, showcasing characters who navigate challenges in a contemporary setting, all while surrounded by the elegance of Seoul\'s vibrant lifestyle. \n\nVisiting Guillaume Cheongdam is more than just a photo op; it’s a chance to connect with the emotional layers of Korean storytelling. This café invites us to recreate memorable scenes and share special moments with friends, all while immersing ourselves in the rich culture that K-Dramas beautifully portray. 🌟 \n\nSo, Seoul explorers, let’s make', '2025-11-18 06:35:34'),
	(881, 3, NULL, 'tell me all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 06:35:46'),
	(882, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Sogang Bridge', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Today, let\'s dive into the enchanting world of Salgoji Bridge, also known as Jeongotgyo Bridge! This stunning historic stone bridge dates back to the Joseon Dynasty and stands proudly where the Cheonggyecheon and Jungangcheon Streams converge with the mighty Hangang River. 🌊 As the longest bridge from the Joseon era, it\'s not just a pretty sight; it was designated as Historic Site No. 160 in 1967 and later elevated to Treasure No. 1738 in 2011! 🏛️ \n\nLocated near the vibrant Hanyang University, the bridge is a perfect spot for travelers to soak in both history and the lively atmosphere of student life. Imagine strolling across its ancient stones, feeling the whispers of the past while surrounded by the modern pulse of Seoul! ✨ This place embodies the seamless blend of tradition and contemporary life that makes Seoul so special. So, grab your camera and come experience the charm of Salgoji Bridge for yourself! 🍽️🏙️', '2025-11-18 06:46:51'),
	(883, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Thought Factory Desiangflex', 'Hey drama fans! 🎬 Are you ready to dive into the captivating world of K-Dramas? Let’s explore the Thought Factory Desiangflex, a stunning filming location for the hit drama *악귀* (The Devil)! This modern architectural gem is not just a feast for the eyes, but also a vibrant hub for shopping and dining, making it a perfect stop for all Seoul explorers! 🏙️✨\n\nThe Thought Factory Desiangflex beautifully represents Korea\'s contemporary lifestyle, blending sleek design with a lively atmosphere. It’s a place where we can immerse ourselves in the modern Korean experience and appreciate how K-Dramas like *악귀* showcase the complexities of urban life and relationships. This location is a testament to how Korean storytelling captures the essence of today\'s society, making it relatable yet enchanting! \n\nAs we stroll through this complex space, we can feel the emotional weight of the stories that unfolded here. The juxtaposition of modernity and tradition in Korean culture resonates deeply, reminding us of the rich narratives that K-Dramas bring to life. \n\nSo, whether you\'re a fan of the show or just love exploring the hidden gems of Seoul, the Thought Factory Desiangflex is a must-visit! Let’s soak', '2025-11-18 06:47:08'),
	(884, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Welcome to the magnificent Gyeongbokgung Palace, the crown jewel of Korea’s royal heritage! Built in 1395, this grand palace was the first and largest of the Five Grand Palaces of the Joseon Dynasty, symbolizing the sovereignty and cultural richness of the era. As we stroll through its stunning gates and lush courtyards, we can almost hear the whispers of history echoing around us. 👑 \n\nGyeongbokgung is not just a feast for the eyes with its beautiful architecture—it’s a vibrant connection to Seoul’s past, standing proudly amid the modern skyline. Did you know that it also houses the National Palace Museum of Korea and the National Folk Museum? These treasures offer deeper insights into Korea’s royal history and traditions! 🏛️ \n\nAs we explore, let’s take a moment to appreciate the changing of the guard ceremony, a captivating display of traditional Korean military culture. So, grab your camera and immerse yourself in the rich tapestry of history right here in the heart of Seoul! ✨ Don’t miss out on this unforgettable experience!', '2025-11-18 06:47:39'),
	(885, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 06:47:58'),
	(886, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 06:51:12'),
	(887, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 06:52:41'),
	(888, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥 Are you ready to dive into the majestic world of Gyeongbokgung Palace? This legendary site is not just Korea\'s first royal palace; it’s the heart of Seoul’s history and culture, built way back in 1395! 👑 Imagine the energy of K-pop music echoing through its ancient walls, where many idols have filmed iconic MVs, blending traditional elegance with modern beats. \n\nIn the Demon Hunters universe, Gyeongbokgung is like the royal fortress where our brave music warriors gather, drawing inspiration from the powerful history that surrounds them. The palace guards\' ceremonies, with their striking formations, inspire K-pop choreography that we adore! 💖 Every corner of this palace resonates with the spirit of Seoul’s vibrant music scene, making it a must-visit for all music lovers and aspiring idols. \n\nSo, let’s go explore this incredible place, feel the energy, and connect with the roots of K-pop culture! 💫✨', '2025-11-18 06:58:05'),
	(889, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Yonsei-ro 4-gil', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Let’s dive into the charming Yonsei-ro 4-gil! This delightful street is nestled in the vibrant neighborhood of Sinchon, right near the prestigious Yonsei University. You’ll find this area buzzing with youthful energy, thanks to the students and locals who frequent the cafes and shops lining the street. 🍽️✨ \n\nYonsei-ro 4-gil is more than just a road; it’s a cultural hub! The blend of modernity with traditional elements reflects Korea\'s dynamic spirit. As we stroll along, we can soak in the lively atmosphere filled with art, music, and the delicious aroma of street food—perfect for fueling our adventures! 🎶🍜 \n\nThis street is a fantastic spot to connect with Seoul\'s youthful culture and creativity, making it a must-visit for anyone wanting to experience the heart of the city. So, grab your camera and let’s explore the vibrant life of Yonsei-ro 4-gil together! 🏙️✨', '2025-11-18 06:59:28'),
	(890, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Yonsei-ro 4-gil', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 Let me introduce you to Yonsei-ro 4-gil, a charming street that embodies the vibrant spirit of the bustling Sinchon area. This street is lined with trendy cafés, boutique shops, and eateries that cater to the youthful energy of university students from nearby Yonsei University. 🍽️ As we wander down Yonsei-ro 4-gil, we can soak in the lively atmosphere, where art and culture blend seamlessly with everyday life! \n\nThis street is a perfect spot for people-watching, and you\'ll often find local artists showcasing their talent, adding a unique flair to the experience. Plus, the proximity to the university means there’s always something happening, from street performances to pop-up markets! 🎭 So, grab a coffee, take a leisurely stroll, and immerse yourself in the creative pulse of Seoul. We promise you’ll leave with unforgettable memories! ✨', '2025-11-18 06:59:46'),
	(891, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 06:59:58'),
	(892, 3, NULL, 'tell me about a must-have item', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 When you visit Seoul Sky, the observation deck atop the Lotte World Tower, a must-have item is your camera! 📸 Trust me, you’ll want to capture the breathtaking panoramic views of the city from the 117th to 123rd floors. From here, we can see Seoul’s vibrant skyline, including the iconic Namsan Tower and the serene Han River. \n\nBut don’t stop at just photos—grab a pair of binoculars available at the deck to get up-close views of the city’s landmarks and hidden gems. 🌆 And if you\'re feeling adventurous, pick up a souvenir from the gift shop to remember your incredible experience. So pack your essentials, and let’s make unforgettable memories at Seoul Sky! ✨', '2025-11-18 07:03:47'),
	(893, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 07:04:32'),
	(894, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙🔥 Are you ready to dive into the enchanting world of Bukchon Hanok Village? This legendary space is like a time capsule reflecting 600 years of Seoul\'s vibrant history, nestled right between the majestic Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces. Imagine walking through streets lined with traditional hanok, where the spirit of the past dances with the energy of the present! ✨\n\nIn our K-pop mythology, Bukchon serves as a hidden sanctuary for our music warriors, where the echoes of history inspire the beats of modern melodies. This isn\'t just a tourist spot; it’s a living, breathing community filled with Seoulites, making it a perfect backdrop for emotional ballads and nostalgic MVs. 🎤💖 \n\nAs we wander through Gaehoe-dong, we can feel the old hanok atmosphere seep into our souls, connecting us to the very essence of Korean culture that fuels our favorite K-pop legends. So, let’s lace up our sneakers and explore this magical village together, where every corner holds a story waiting to be sung! Let\'s go, fellow music lovers! ⚔️💫', '2025-11-18 07:13:15'),
	(895, 3, NULL, 'tell me about a must-have item', 'Hey Seoul explorers! 🌟 When visiting Seoul Sky, a must-have item to enjoy is definitely your camera! 📸 Perched on the 117th to 123rd floors of the Lotte World Tower, Seoul Sky offers breathtaking panoramic views of the city that are simply irresistible. Imagine capturing the sprawling skyline, the majestic Han River, and perhaps even a glimpse of the iconic Namsan Tower in the distance! \n\nAs we soak in the vibrant atmosphere, don\'t forget to grab a unique souvenir from the on-site gift shop. They offer beautiful postcards and other mementos that perfectly encapsulate your experience at this stunning observation deck. 📬✨ So, pack your camera and get ready to create unforgettable memories high above the bustling streets of Seoul! Let’s make this adventure one for the books! 🏙️', '2025-11-18 07:45:56'),
	(896, 3, NULL, 'tell me about a cafe camel', 'Welcome, Seoul food explorers! 🌟 If you\'re looking for a place that combines an incredible view with a cozy atmosphere, look no further than 눕카페&피자펍! Situated in the vibrant 해방촌 area, this spacious café and pub boasts a stunning view of N서울타워, making it the perfect spot to unwind after a day of exploring. 🍽️✨ The antique decor creates a charming ambiance where we can enjoy delicious pizzas and refreshing drinks while playing a game of pool or lounging in the comfy bean bags! 🏙️ This unique blend of relaxation and fun captures the essence of Seoul\'s dining culture, where friends gather over good food and breathtaking scenery. No wonder locals adore this gem! Come join us for an unforgettable experience! 🍕❤️', '2025-11-18 07:46:06'),
