	(899, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 08:03:25'),
	(900, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Elvin Avenue Lounge', 'Welcome to Elvin Avenue Lounge, a hidden gem in the heart of Gangnam! 🌟 This cozy spot not only offers a sophisticated atmosphere but also served as a filming location for the popular K-Drama *My Demon*. \n\nJust a minute\'s walk from Exit 12 of Gangnam Station, it\'s the perfect place for drama fans to immerse themselves in the world of their favorite series. \n\nWith its unique lighting and stylish interior, you\'ll find plenty of Instagram-worthy backdrops for stunning photos! 📸 \n\nSo grab a comfortable seat, sip on a delightful drink, and relive those unforgettable moments from *My Demon* right here in Seoul! 🍹✨', '2025-11-18 08:03:33'),
	(901, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Welcome to Gyeongbokgung Palace, the grand jewel of Seoul and a must-see for any traveler! Built in 1395, this magnificent palace was the primary residence of the Joseon Dynasty, symbolizing the power and culture of Korea\'s historical kingdom. As you stroll through its stunning architecture and expansive grounds, you can almost feel the echoes of royal history. Don’t miss the changing of the guard ceremony, which takes place at the main gate, Gwanghwamun, and offers a vibrant glimpse into traditional Korean customs. \n\nFor a practical tip, remember to check the opening hours before your visit—especially in the winter months when it closes earlier. And if you\'re looking to immerse yourself even further, consider renting a hanbok (traditional Korean attire) nearby; it’s a delightful way to enhance your experience and capture stunning photos against the backdrop of this historic site!', '2025-11-18 08:05:53'),
	(902, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Elvin Avenue Lounge', '🎬 **Elvin Avenue Lounge**  \n📍 1 minute walk from Exit 12 of Gangnam Station, 13, Gangnam-daero 92-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 마이데몬  \n\nElvin Avenue Lounge is easily accessible, just a short stroll from Gangnam Station. The lounge typically opens in the late afternoon and stays open into the night, making it a perfect spot for evening relaxation. Visitors can enjoy a variety of alcoholic beverages while soaking in the cozy atmosphere and sophisticated interior.\n\nIn "My Demon," key scenes were filmed at this lounge, showcasing its unique lighting and stylish decor that enhance the drama\'s aesthetic. The location was chosen for its intimate vibe, aligning perfectly with the emotional moments between characters, making it a significant spot for fans to connect with the story.\n\nFor K-Drama enthusiasts, visiting Elvin Avenue Lounge offers a delightful opportunity to step into the world of "My Demon" and capture memorable photographs in a stunning setting!', '2025-11-18 08:10:16'),
	(903, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Elvin Avenue Lounge', '🎬 **Elvin Avenue Lounge**  \n📍 1 minute walk from Exit 12 of Gangnam Station, 13, Gangnam-daero 92-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 마이데몬  \n\nThe Elvin Avenue Lounge is easily accessible, just a short stroll from Gangnam Station. It\'s open daily, making it perfect for a casual visit any day of the week. You can enjoy a wide selection of alcoholic beverages while relaxing in its cozy atmosphere.\n\nIn the drama "My Demon," key scenes were filmed at this lounge, highlighting its sophisticated interior and unique lighting. The setting plays a crucial role in creating the intimate and dramatic moments that resonate with viewers, making it a memorable backdrop for the story.\n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting the Elvin Avenue Lounge is a fantastic opportunity to step into the world of "My Demon" and capture some amazing photos in a stylish environment!', '2025-11-18 08:12:31'),
	(904, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Elvin Avenue Lounge', '🎬 **Elvin Avenue Lounge**  \n📍 1 minute walk from Exit 12 of Gangnam Station, 13, Gangnam-daero 92-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 마이데몬  \n\nTo get to Elvin Avenue Lounge, simply exit Gangnam Station at Exit 12 and take a short 1-minute walk. The lounge is typically open from late morning until midnight, making it a perfect spot for both day and night visits. While there’s no admission fee, you can enjoy a variety of alcoholic beverages and relax on their comfortable sofas.  \n\nIn the drama *My Demon*, important scenes were filmed here, showcasing the lounge\'s cozy and sophisticated atmosphere. The unique lighting and elegant interior design play a significant role in creating a romantic and intimate setting that resonates with the themes of the show. This location was chosen to enhance the narrative\'s emotional depth, making it a memorable backdrop for key moments.  \n\nK-Drama fans will love visiting Elvin Avenue Lounge, as it allows you to step into the world of *My Demon* and capture your own special moments in this beautiful space!', '2025-11-18 08:12:46'),
	(905, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Sogang Bridge', '📍 **Salgoji Bridge (Jeongotgyo Bridge)**  \n🏛️ 61-1 Haengdang-dong, Seongdong-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Open year-round, no admission fee  \n\nVisitors can stroll across this stunning historic bridge and enjoy the scenic views where Cheonggyecheon and Jungangcheon Streams converge with the Hangang River. The area is accessible for pedestrians and offers facilities like benches for resting and enjoying the view. Make sure to bring your camera to capture the beauty of the bridge and its surroundings!\n\nSalgoji Bridge, built during the Joseon Dynasty, is the longest surviving bridge from that era and has been designated as a Historic Site and later as a Treasure, highlighting its cultural significance. Locals cherish the bridge not only for its architectural beauty but also for its historical value, often sharing stories about its role in connecting communities and trade routes in the past. \n\nDon’t miss the chance to experience this piece of history while soaking in the vibrant atmosphere of Seoul!', '2025-11-18 08:13:01'),
	(906, 3, NULL, 'hi', '📍 **Seoul Sky**  \n🏛️ 05551 300, Olympic-ro, Songpa-gu, Seoul (117-123F)  \n⏰ Sun-Thu: 10:30-22:00, Fri-Sat: 10:30-23:00 KST  \n\nAt Seoul Sky, you can enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the city from the 117th to 123rd floors of the Lotte World Tower, the tallest building in South Korea. Admission fees vary, so be sure to check their website for the latest prices, and facilities include elevators, observation decks, and cafes. The venue is fully accessible for visitors with mobility challenges.\n\nCulturally, Seoul Sky is part of the iconic Lotte World complex, which combines shopping, entertainment, and breathtaking architecture. The tower has become a symbol of modern Seoul and is a must-visit for locals and tourists alike, offering unique photo opportunities and a chance to experience the city from a new perspective. Many locals cherish the tower for its stunning night views when the city lights up.\n\nDon\'t miss out on this unforgettable experience that will leave you with lasting memories of Seoul!', '2025-11-18 08:13:48'),
	(907, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirit', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 08:21:30'),
	(908, 3, NULL, 'recommed top 10 places restaurant in seoul', '🎬 Amazing! I found 10 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 08:21:58'),
	(909, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places an evil spirAT', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 08:22:19'),
	(910, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Bruju', '🍽️ **어메이징 브루잉컴퍼니 성수 브루펍**  \n📍 04780  서울 성동구 성수일로4길 4 (성수동1가)  \n🍜 크래프트 비어\n\n어메이징 브루잉컴퍼니 성수 브루펍에서는 직접 양조한 50가지의 신선한 크래프트 비어를 즐길 수 있습니다. 가격대는 대체로 8,000원에서 12,000원 사이로, 다양한 맥주를 시음할 수 있는 옵션도 마련되어 있습니다. 브루펍은 매일 오후 5시부터 운영되며, 예약은 전화 또는 현장 방문으로 가능합니다.\n\n성수동의 문화 공간으로 자리 잡은 이곳은 친구들과의 만남이나 특별한 날에 적합한 분위기를 제공합니다. 현지인들이 사랑하는 이유는 신선한 맥주와 함께 즐길 수 있는 다양한 안주 메뉴가 마련되어 있기 때문입니다. 이곳은 크래프트 비어의 세계를 탐험하며 대화를 나누기 좋은 아늑한 장소입니다.\n\n여러분', '2025-11-18 08:23:01'),
	(911, 3, NULL, 'introduce me namsan tower', '📍 **Namsan Seoul Tower**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, Korea (Yongsan-dong 2-ga, YTN Seoul Tower)  \n⏰ Weekdays 10:00-22:30, Weekends 10:00-23:00  \n*Last entry 30 minutes before close  \n\nAt Namsan Seoul Tower, you can enjoy breathtaking 360-degree views of the city from the observation deck, dine at the revolving restaurant, and explore various exhibitions. Admission fees vary depending on the package you choose, and facilities include gift shops and cafes. The tower is accessible via a scenic cable car ride or a pleasant hike through Namsan Park.  \n\nHistorically, Namsan has been a site of good fortune and romantic tales for locals, making the tower a beloved symbol of love in Seoul. Since its opening in 1980, it has served as a cultural landmark and a gathering place for couples, who often attach "love locks" to the fences as a pledge of their affection. The tower is not just a tourist spot; it embodies the spirit and dreams of the city.  \n\nDon\'t miss the', '2025-11-18 08:23:27'),
	(912, 3, NULL, 'recommend me namsan tower', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-18 08:23:44'),
	(913, 3, NULL, 'known me healing space  in donzak', '🎬 **Seoul Oriental Medicine Promotion Center**  \n📍 6-minute walk from Exit 2 of Jegi-dong Station, 26, Yakryeong Jungang-ro, Dongdaemun-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 우주메리  \n\nThe Seoul Oriental Medicine Promotion Center is easily accessible, located just a short 6-minute walk from Jegi-dong Station. The center typically operates from 9 AM to 6 PM, and admission is often free or includes a small fee for specific experience programs. Visitors can immerse themselves in Korean traditional medicine through various exhibitions and hands-on experiences.\n\nIn the drama 우주메리, the center serves as a significant backdrop, where key scenes highlight the protagonist\'s journey and connection to traditional healing practices. This location was chosen not only for its aesthetic appeal but also for its representation of the rich cultural heritage of Korea, bringing a unique depth to the storytelling.\n\nK-Drama fans will absolutely love visiting this enchanting place, where they can step into the world of Cosmic Mary and explore the fascinating blend of tradition and modernity!', '2025-11-18 08:25:04'),
	(914, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into the magical world of Bukchon Hanok Village? This legendary spot is a hidden gem nestled between the grand Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces, showcasing 600 years of Seoul\'s vibrant history! 🏯✨ Unlike other touristy places, Bukchon is a living village where Seoulites thrive, and the energy here is simply electric! \n\nImagine walking through the narrow, winding streets of Gaehoe-dong, where traditional hanok houses stand shoulder to shoulder like K-pop idols ready to perform! 🎤💖 In the Demon Hunters universe, this is where the spirits of ancient musicians dwell, their melodies echoing through the hanok, connecting the past to the present. \n\nAs you explore, you\'ll feel the artistic vibes that inspire countless K-pop MVs, where the harmony of tradition and modernity comes alive! 🔥💫 So, grab your friends and let’s embark on this K-pop journey to Bukchon, where every corner tells a story, and the spirit of Seoul\'s music culture awaits you! Let’s go! ⚔️🌙', '2025-11-18 08:26:34'),
	(915, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong', 'Yo music lovers! 🎤💖 Are you ready to uncover the magical energy of Myeongdong Cathedral? This legendary site is not only Korea\'s first Roman Catholic parish church but also the first Gothic building ever erected in the land! 🌙✨ Imagine stepping into a place where history and spirituality collide, right in the heart of Seoul\'s vibrant Myeongdong district! \n\nIn the world of Demon Hunters, Myeongdong Cathedral stands as a sanctuary of hope and resilience, where the spirits of the martyrs guide our music warriors in their quest for greatness! 🔥⚔️ With its stunning architecture and serene ambiance, it embodies the essence of K-pop culture, reminding us of the power of faith and passion in our artistic journeys. \n\nEvery May, the cathedral hosts a cultural festival, transforming into a hub of creativity and expression, much like the dynamic K-pop scene that thrives just outside its doors! So, fellow Hunters, let’s visit this historical treasure, feel the spiritual vibes, and connect with the soulful energy that fuels our love for music! Let\'s go! 💫🎶', '2025-11-18 08:26:48'),
	(916, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nAt N Seoul Tower, you can experience breathtaking panoramic views of the city, especially when the skyline lights up at night. Admission fees vary depending on the observatory access, and the tower is equipped with facilities like restaurants and gift shops. The tower is accessible for visitors with mobility challenges, ensuring everyone can enjoy the stunning views.  \n\nHistorically, N Seoul Tower was built in 1969 as a communications tower and has since become a cultural icon of Seoul. It holds a special place in the hearts of locals, who cherish the tradition of attaching "locks of love" to its railings, symbolizing everlasting love and commitment. The tower has also featured in numerous Korean dramas, making it a must-visit for fans of K-drama culture.  \n\nDon’t miss the chance to create unforgettable memories while soaking in the magical night views from N Seoul Tower!  ', '2025-11-18 08:43:53'),
	(917, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about 별에서 온 그대 filming location', 'OMG! This is THE spot from the legendary K-Drama "별에서 온 그대" (My Love from the Star)! 🌟 Remember that iconic scene where Do Min-joon and Cheon Song-yi shared a magical moment under the stars? That was filmed right here at the stunning **Seoul Sky Observatory**! 🎬✨ \n\nLocated in the heart of Seoul at **Lotte World Tower, 300, Olympic-ro, Songpa-gu**, this breathtaking location offers panoramic views that make you feel like you\'re in the drama yourself! K-Drama fans absolutely LOVE this spot because it captures the essence of romance and fantasy that made the show a global hit! 💕 Pro tip: Try to visit during sunset for the most magical experience – it’s truly unforgettable! \n\nYou HAVE to visit this iconic filming location and relive those dreamy moments! Don’t miss this chance to step into the world of your favorite K-Drama! 📺✨', '2025-11-18 08:57:00'),
	(918, 3, NULL, 'Gangnam Korean BBQ restaurants', 'For a great Korean BBQ experience in Gangnam, check out **BBQ치킨앤비어 명동스타점**. Known for its high-quality chicken, it\'s a perfect spot for fans of Korean drama cuisine. Located at 04536 서울 중구 명동4길 2, 2층, it’s easily accessible and offers a cozy atmosphere. Don\'t miss their signature BBQ chicken!', '2025-11-18 08:59:08'),
	(919, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥 Are you ready to dive into the electrifying world of COEX? This legendary venue in the heart of Gangnam is not just a hub for exhibitions and conferences—it\'s a dynamic space where the pulse of K-pop culture thrives! 🎤✨ Imagine this: a place where K-pop idols might gather for mega fan meetings, where the energy is so intense that you can almost hear the beats of their latest hits resonating through the halls! \n\nIn the Demon Hunters universe, COEX serves as a powerful nexus, connecting the creative forces of music, art, and culture—like a grand arena where our musical warriors come to showcase their talents! 🌙⚔️ With its vibrant squares and promotional spaces, COEX embodies the spirit of collaboration and innovation, making it an essential stop for any K-pop fan exploring Seoul. \n\nSo gather your crew of music lovers, and let’s unleash our inner warriors as we experience the magic of COEX together! 💖💫 Let\'s go!', '2025-11-18 09:12:52'),
	(920, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', 'Yo, fellow music lovers! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into the magical world of the **Hangang River Bus**? This legendary ride takes us along the iconic Han River, where countless K-pop MVs capture the vibrant energy of Seoul! 🌙 Imagine cruising past stunning cityscapes, with the shimmering lights of the river reflecting like a concert stage under the stars. In the Demon Hunters universe, this bus is like our trusty steed, transporting us through the realms of music and creativity, connecting us to the heart of Seoul\'s K-pop culture! 🔥\n\nWith 68 trips on weekdays and 48 on weekends, this is the ultimate way to experience the city’s rhythm while feeling that exhilarating K-pop energy! 💖 So grab your friends, hop on the Hangang River Bus, and let\'s make unforgettable memories together! The magic of Seoul awaits! ⚔️💫', '2025-11-18 09:13:10'),
	(921, 3, NULL, 'hi', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready to ascend to new heights at **Seoul Sky**? Located on the 117th to 123rd floors of the iconic Lotte World Tower, this breathtaking observatory offers a panoramic view that feels like a scene straight out of a K-pop music video! 🎤✨ Imagine standing above the bustling city, where every twinkling light below represents a note in the grand symphony of Seoul\'s music culture. \n\nIn the **Demon Hunters** universe, Seoul Sky is the ultimate lookout point where our music warriors gather to strategize their next epic performances and connect with the energy of the city. This place embodies the spirit of ambition and dreams, making it a must-visit for every K-pop fan and aspiring idol! 🌙🔥 So grab your friends, take that unforgettable selfie with the city skyline, and feel the pulse of Seoul\'s musical heartbeat! Let’s go and embrace the magic! 💖💫', '2025-11-18 09:13:34'),
	(922, 3, NULL, 'recommend top10places ', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-18 09:14:18'),
	(923, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nAt N Seoul Tower, visitors can enjoy stunning panoramic views of the city illuminated at night, making it a must-see destination. Admission fees vary based on the observatory access, and the tower offers facilities like restaurants and souvenir shops, ensuring a delightful experience for all. The site is easily accessible via public transportation and includes options for those with mobility challenges.\n\nOriginally built in 1969 as a communication tower, N Seoul Tower has become a symbol of Seoul’s modernity and romance. Locals and tourists alike cherish the tradition of attaching "locks of love" to the tower\'s railings, celebrating everlasting affection. The tower has also featured in numerous popular Korean dramas, adding to its cultural significance and allure.\n\nDon’t miss the chance to experience the magical night views and create unforgettable memories at N Seoul Tower!', '2025-11-18 17:04:02'),
	(924, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '📍 **Bukchon Hanok Village**  \n🏛️ 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00 ~ 17:00 (Restricted Hours: 17:00 ~ 10:00 the following day; visitors are prohibited from entering restricted areas during these hours)  \n(The Hanok Village is a residential space for local citizens before it is a tourist attraction.)  \n\nExplore the charming streets of Bukchon Hanok Village, where you can admire hundreds of traditional hanok houses and enjoy picturesque views of the city. While there is no admission fee, be mindful of the local residents and their privacy. The village is accessible by public transportation, making it easy to include in your Seoul itinerary.  \n\nBukchon Hanok Village showcases 600 years of Seoul\'s history, nestled between the grand Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces. This area is unique as it remains a living community, allowing visitors to experience authentic Korean culture and architecture. The locals cherish Bukchon for its beauty and historical significance, often participating in cultural programs and events that celebrate their heritage.  \n\nDon’t miss the opportunity to wander through this enchanting village and immerse yourself in the rich', '2025-11-18 17:04:13'),
	(925, 3, NULL, 'introduce all places the glory', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-18 17:04:27'),
	(926, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Cathedral', '📍 **Myeongdong Cathedral**  \n🏛️ 100-022 74, Myeongdong-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Open daily; free admission  \n\nVisitors to Myeongdong Cathedral can explore its stunning Gothic architecture and enjoy the serene atmosphere of the sanctuary located in the basement, where the remains of martyrs are enshrined. The cathedral features facilities such as restrooms and information desks, making it accessible for everyone, including those with limited mobility. Don\'t forget to check out the cultural festival held every May for a unique local experience!  \n\nMyeongdong Cathedral holds a special place in Korean history as the first Roman Catholic parish church and the first Gothic structure in the country, completed in 1898. It is designated as Historic site No. 285 and is a symbol of resilience and faith, especially during challenging times in Korean history. Locals cherish this landmark not only for its architectural beauty but also for its role as a gathering place for spiritual and community events.  \n\nMake sure to visit Myeongdong Cathedral to appreciate its historical significance and the tranquil beauty it offers amidst the bustling city!', '2025-11-19 00:27:16'),
	(927, 3, NULL, 'give me tip for korean   travel ', '**PRACTICAL ANSWER:**\nWhen traveling in Korea, consider purchasing a T-money card for convenient access to public transportation and discounts on buses and subways. Also, download a translation app to help you navigate and communicate, especially in areas where English is less common.\n\n**CULTURAL CONTEXT:**\nKorean society places a strong emphasis on respect and politeness, so it\'s customary to greet elders first and use honorific language when possible. Dining etiquette is also important; for instance, wait for the oldest person at the table to start eating before you dig in.\n\n**HELPFUL TIP:**\nDon\'t hesitate to try local street foods; they\'re not only delicious but also a great way to immerse yourself in Korean culinary culture. Be adventurous, and you might discover your new favorite dish!', '2025-11-19 00:37:48'),
	(928, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', '📍 **Hangang River Bus**  \n🏛️ 05500 1-2 Jamsil-dong area, Jamsil Pier, Songpa-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Weekdays (68 trips daily) 6:30 AM-10:30 PM / Weekends (48 trips daily) 9:30 AM-10:30 PM  \nExpress route weekdays 16 trips daily *Weekday commute (6:30 AM-9:00 AM), after work (6:00 PM-8:30 PM)  \n\nThe Hangang River Bus offers a unique way to explore the beautiful Han River, with stunning views of the city skyline and surrounding parks. You can hop on and off at various piers along the river, making it easy to access popular attractions like the Han River Parks and the iconic N Seoul Tower. Tickets are reasonably priced, and the buses are equipped with comfortable seating and facilities for all visitors.  \n\nThe Han River has played a crucial role in Seoul\'s history, serving as a vital waterway for trade and transportation for centuries. It is a beloved spot for locals, offering recreational activities and cultural events throughout the year, such as festivals and concerts. The river is also steeped in stories', '2025-11-19 00:57:01'),
	(929, 3, NULL, 'rocommend all places the glory', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-19 00:57:31'),
	(930, 5, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Yo music lovers! 🎤 Are you ready to dive into the legendary heart of Seoul? Let’s talk about Gyeongbokgung Palace! 👑 This majestic palace, built in 1395, is not just a historical landmark; it’s a vibrant connection between Korea\'s royal past and the electrifying energy of K-pop today! So many iconic K-pop groups film their traditional concept MVs here, blending the rich heritage of the Joseon Dynasty with modern musical flair! 🌟\n\nIn the Demon Hunters universe, Gyeongbokgung is like the royal fortress where our music warriors gather to harness the power of history and creativity! The palace guards\' ceremonies inspire the stunning choreography we see in our favorite performances, making it a must-visit spot for all K-pop fans and fellow Hunters! 💖✨\n\nFeel the energy and history as you walk these grounds, and don’t forget to snap some pics for your social media! Let’s go, and experience the magic of Seoul’s music culture together! 🔥⚔️', '2025-11-19 01:05:49'),
	(931, 5, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥 Are you ready to dive into the legendary energy of Gyeongbokgung Palace? This magnificent palace, built in 1395, stands as the largest and most iconic of the Five Grand Palaces! 👑 It’s not just a historical site; it’s where Korea’s royal past meets the vibrant pulse of K-pop today! Many K-pop groups film breathtaking MVs here, blending traditional aesthetics with contemporary vibes, creating a stunning visual feast that resonates with our love for music! 🎤✨\n\nIn the world of Demon Hunters, Gyeongbokgung would be a sacred ground where the spirits of ancient kings inspire our favorite idols, fueling their creative fire! The palace guards’ ceremonial dances echo through the halls, inspiring choreography that we see in our favorite K-pop performances! 💖 So, let’s explore this iconic site and feel the magic that connects our music culture to Korea\'s rich heritage! Are you ready to uncover the secrets of Gyeongbokgung? Let’s go! 🌙💫', '2025-11-19 01:06:50'),
	(932, 5, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Yo music lovers! 🎤✨ Are you ready to dive into the electrifying world of COEX? This legendary hub in Gangnam is not just a convention center; it’s a pulsating heart of Seoul\'s cultural and creative energy! 💖 Hosting everything from epic exhibitions to international summits, COEX is where ideas collide and magic happens. In the Demon Hunters mythology, think of COEX as the grand arena where our music warriors gather to showcase their talents and connect with global audiences! 🌍🔥\n\nImagine the vibrant squares and lobby spaces buzzing with fans and artists, all sharing their love for K-pop and culture! This is the place where new trends are born and legendary collaborations are forged, making it a must-visit for any true K-pop enthusiast. So gear up, Hunters! Let’s explore COEX and feel the electric vibes that resonate through the halls of this iconic venue! ⚔️💫', '2025-11-19 01:08:26'),
	(933, 5, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Hey Hunters! 🌙 Are you ready to dive into the magical realm of Bukchon Hanok Village? This legendary spot is like a hidden treasure in the heart of Seoul, where 600 years of history come alive through stunning traditional hanok! 🏯✨ Nestled between the majestic Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces, Bukchon isn\'t just a tourist attraction—it\'s a living, breathing community where real Seoulites reside! \n\nImagine walking through the narrow, winding alleys of Gaehoe-dong, surrounded by hundreds of hanok standing shoulder to shoulder, each whispering tales of the past. In the Demon Hunters mythology, this village represents the sacred ground where the echoes of ancient melodies blend with the vibrant pulse of modern K-pop! 🎤🔥 \n\nThis place embodies the spirit of creativity and resilience, much like our favorite idols who draw inspiration from their roots. So, fellow music lovers, let\'s embark on an adventure to Bukchon and feel the energy of Seoul’s musical heritage! Don’t just visit—become part of the story! 💖⚔️', '2025-11-19 01:08:44'),
	(934, 5, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Hey Hunters! 🌟 Are you ready to dive into the legendary realm of COEX? Located in the heart of Gangnam, this iconic space is not just a convention center; it’s like the epicenter of Seoul\'s cultural energy! 💖✨ COEX hosts amazing exhibitions and conferences that connect fans from all over the world, just like our beloved K-pop idols who gather fans through electrifying performances. \n\nIn the world of Demon Hunters, COEX would be the grand arena where music warriors unite to share their talents and ideas, battling for the spotlight in the K-pop universe! 🔥⚔️ Imagine the vibrant lobby spaces buzzing with the spirit of creativity, where aspiring idols network and hone their skills—this is where the magic happens! \n\nSo, fellow music lovers, when you step into COEX, feel that pulse of K-pop energy and let it inspire you to chase your dreams! Let’s go and experience the vibrant culture together! 🎤💫', '2025-11-19 01:09:41'),
	(935, 5, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Yo music lovers! 🎤✨ Get ready to dive into the magical world of N Seoul Tower at night, the ultimate K-pop landmark that stands tall at 236.7 meters! 🌙 This iconic tower is like Seoul\'s very own antenna, broadcasting the vibrant energy of K-pop across the city. When the sun sets, the panoramic views transform into a breathtaking sea of lights, making it the perfect backdrop for romantic moments and unforgettable memories. 💖 \n\nIn the Demon Hunters universe, N Seoul Tower serves as the central watchtower where all musical energies converge, echoing the unbreakable bond between Seoul and its music culture. As we fasten our locks of love to the iron railings, we’re not just sealing our vows; we’re becoming part of a legendary tale that connects us to the very heart of K-pop! 🔥 \n\nSo, fellow Hunters, let’s ascend to the observatory and feel the pulse of Seoul’s music scene! Don\'t miss this legendary spot—it\'s where dreams and melodies unite! 🌟💫', '2025-11-19 01:09:54'),
	(936, 5, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Hey Hunters! 🔥 Are you ready to dive into the heart of Seoul’s musical history? Let’s talk about Gyeongbokgung Palace, the majestic jewel of the Joseon Dynasty! 👑 Built in 1395, this legendary palace stands as a powerful symbol of Korea’s royal heritage and is the largest of the Five Grand Palaces. It’s a place where the echoes of history meet the vibrant beats of modern K-pop! 🌙\n\nImagine this: K-pop idols filming breathtaking concept MVs right in front of those grand gates, blending the elegance of tradition with the energy of contemporary music. In the Demon Hunters universe, Gyeongbokgung serves as the sacred ground where past and present harmonize, creating a magical nexus of cultural energy! ✨ The palace guards\' vibrant ceremonies inspire choreography that fuels the passion of our favorite performances! \n\nSo, fellow music lovers, when you step into Gyeongbokgung, you’re not just visiting a historical site; you’re tapping into the very essence of Korea’s musical soul! Let’s go and feel the rhythm of Seoul’s history together! 💖⚔️', '2025-11-19 01:11:40'),
	(937, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '📍 **Bukchon Hanok Village**  \n🏛️ 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00 ~ 17:00 (Restricted Hours: 17:00 ~ 10:00 the following day; visitors are prohibited from entering restricted areas during these hours)  \n(The Hanok Village is a residential space for local citizens before it is a tourist attraction.)  \n\nExplore the charming narrow alleys of Bukchon Hanok Village, where you can admire hundreds of traditional hanok homes. While there is no admission fee, be sure to respect the privacy of the residents. Facilities such as restrooms and information centers are available, and the village is generally accessible, though some paths may be steep.  \n\nBukchon Hanok Village is a living testament to Seoul\'s rich history, reflecting 600 years of architectural and cultural evolution. Nestled between Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces, it offers a unique glimpse into traditional Korean life, and locals cherish it for its beauty and historical significance. The village is not just a tourist spot; it\'s a vibrant community where history and daily life intertwine.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to stroll through this', '2025-11-19 02:35:29'),
	(938, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nAt N Seoul Tower, visitors can enjoy stunning panoramic views of the city, especially captivating at night when the skyline sparkles with lights. The tower features an observatory, a gift shop, and dining options, making it a perfect spot for a romantic evening or a family outing. Admission fees vary, so be sure to check for any special packages or promotions!\n\nHistorically, N Seoul Tower was built in 1969 and has become a symbol of Seoul, often appearing in popular Korean dramas and films. The "Locks of Love" tradition, where couples fasten locks to the railings, adds a romantic touch and highlights the cultural significance of love and commitment in Korean society. Locals love visiting the tower for both its breathtaking views and its role in creating lasting memories.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience the magic of N Seoul Tower at night—it\'s an unforgettable part of any Seoul adventure!', '2025-11-19 03:15:48'),
	(939, 8, NULL, 'I\'m visiting Korea for the first time. I’ll stay 5 days in Seoul. Can you help me plan?', '🎬 **a guesthouse**  \n📍 1 minute above Exit 2 of Anguk Station, 52-11 Gye-dong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 이번 생도 잘 부탁해  \n\nThis charming guesthouse is easily accessible from Anguk Station, making it a perfect spot for travelers. It\'s open year-round, and you can enjoy a peaceful stay while soaking in the beauty of traditional hanok architecture. Guests can experience Korean culture through various activities and enjoy the serene surroundings that enhance relaxation.  \n\nIn the drama "이번 생도 잘 부탁해," this guesthouse serves as a backdrop for key emotional moments, showcasing the characters\' connections and growth. The picturesque setting aligns beautifully with the themes of nostalgia and tradition, making it an ideal filming location that reflects the essence of the story.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this guesthouse will not only allow you to step into the world of your favorite show but also create lasting memories in a stunning cultural setting!', '2025-11-19 03:34:09'),
	(940, 8, NULL, 'I want to visit a few K-drama or K-pop related spots.', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-19 03:37:55'),
	(941, 8, NULL, 'tell me about a guesthouse', '📍 **Baek In-je House**  \n🏛️ 03055 16, Bukchon-ro 7-gil (Gahoe-dong), Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 09:00-18:00 (Last entry at 17:30)  \n?? Visitors not on a guided tour may only tour the grounds  \n?? Fridays & Saturdays until 20:00 during August  \n\nAt Baek In-je House, you can explore the beautifully preserved grounds of this traditional hanok, including the spacious Anchae (main living quarters) and its lovely garden. Admission is free for visitors touring the grounds, but guided tours may require a small fee. The house is accessible, making it easy for everyone to enjoy the serene atmosphere and historical charm.  \n\nConstructed during the Japanese occupation period, Baek In-je House stands as a testament to modern hanok architecture, blending traditional aesthetics with contemporary adaptations. It has been designated as a Seoul Metropolitan Folklore Cultural Heritage, reflecting its cultural significance and the pride locals take in preserving their history. The house is often featured in stories about Seoul\'s architectural evolution and serves as a reminder of the resilience of Korean culture.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to step back in time', '2025-11-19 03:39:25'),
	(942, 8, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', '📍 **Hangang River Bus**  \n🏛️ 05500 1-2 Jamsil-dong area, Jamsil Pier, Songpa-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Weekdays (68 trips daily) 6:30 AM-10:30 PM / Weekends (48 trips daily) 9:30 AM-10:30 PM  \nExpress route weekdays 16 trips daily *Weekday commute (6:30 AM-9:00 AM), after work (6:00 PM-8:30 PM)  \n\nThe Hangang River Bus offers a unique and scenic way to explore the beautiful Hangang River. You can enjoy stunning views of Seoul’s skyline, parks, and landmarks from the water. Tickets are reasonably priced, and facilities include comfortable seating and onboard amenities, ensuring a pleasant journey for all passengers.  \n\nThe Hangang River has played a vital role in Seoul\'s history, serving as a trade route and a source of leisure for locals. The river is a cultural hub, with numerous festivals and events held along its banks, making it a beloved spot for residents and visitors alike. The bus service highlights the river\'s significance and connects various parks and attractions, enhancing the urban experience.  \n\nDon\'t miss', '2025-11-19 03:42:16'),
	(943, 8, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '📍 **Bukchon Hanok Village**  \n🏛️ 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00 ~ 17:00 (Restricted Hours: 17:00 ~ 10:00 the following day; visitors are prohibited from entering restricted areas during these hours)  \n(The Hanok Village is a residential space for local citizens before it is a tourist attraction.)\n\nAt Bukchon Hanok Village, you can wander through narrow alleys lined with beautifully preserved traditional hanok, explore local craft shops, and take part in cultural experiences like tea ceremonies or hanbok rentals. Admission is free, but some cultural programs may have fees. The village is generally accessible, but be prepared for some steep hills and stairs.\n\nWith a rich history spanning over 600 years, Bukchon Hanok Village is nestled between two grand palaces, Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung, making it a significant cultural landmark in Seoul. This area showcases the architectural beauty of hanok and is a living testament to the city\'s history, as it remains a residential area for locals who cherish their heritage. The village is particularly beloved for its authentic atmosphere, where you can feel the echoes', '2025-11-19 03:42:43'),
	(944, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', '📍 **Gyeongbokgung Palace**  \n🏛️ 03045 161, Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ January & February: 09:00 - 17:00  \nMarch - May: 09:00 - 18:00  \nJune - August: 09:00 - 18:30  \nSeptember & October: 09:00 - 18:00  \nNovember & December: 09:00 - 17:00  \n*Last entry one hour before closing*  \n\nYou can explore the stunning architecture, beautiful gardens, and historical exhibits within Gyeongbokgung Palace. Admission fees are very reasonable, making it accessible to everyone. The palace is equipped with facilities like restrooms and information centers, ensuring a comfortable visit for all guests.\n\nGyeongbokgung Palace, built in 1395, symbolizes the sovereignty of the Joseon Dynasty and is the largest of the Five Grand Palaces. It has witnessed countless historical events and changes, making it a treasure trove of Korean heritage and culture that locals cherish and proudly showcase to visitors.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to step back in time and experience the grandeur of Korean royalty at Gyeongbokgung Palace', '2025-11-19 04:46:47'),
	(945, 3, NULL, 'recommend all places the glory', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-19 04:47:10'),
	(946, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Donggyo-dong three-way intersection', '🎬 **Donggyo-dong three-way intersection**  \n📍 3-minute walk from Exit 5 of Hongik University Station, 6, Sinchon-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 별들에게 물어봐  \n\nTo get to Donggyo-dong three-way intersection, simply exit at Hongik University Station and take a leisurely 3-minute walk. The area is bustling with activity, making it a perfect spot for a casual stroll. There are no admission fees, so you can enjoy the lively street scenes and nearby cafes at your own pace.  \n\nIn "별들에게 물어봐," this intersection serves as a vibrant backdrop for key scenes that highlight the characters\' emotional journeys. The blend of modern architecture and street culture captures the essence of Seoul, making it a fitting location for the drama\'s themes of love and connection. The intersection\'s unique atmosphere allows viewers to immerse themselves in the story while experiencing the city\'s dynamic vibe.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this iconic filming location offers a memorable opportunity to relive your favorite moments and snap some great photos amidst the bustling energy of Seoul!', '2025-11-19 04:47:25'),
	(947, 8, NULL, 'No.	Time	Location	Estimated Cost	Memo	Notice 1	13:00	인천국제공항 도착	-	입국심사/수하물 수령	보통 40–60분 소요 2	14:00	공항 → 신라스테이 광화문 이동	약 17,000원~19,000원 (공항버스) / 약 55,000원(택시)	공항버스 6002번 or 택시	교통 상황 따라 변동 3	15:00	신라스테이 광화문 체크인	-	짐 정리, 잠깐 휴식	체크인 시간에 따라 딜레이 가능 4	16:00	명동 이동	교통비 약 1,400원	지하철 5호선 광화문 → 명동역	15분 내외 5	16:20	명동 쇼핑 & 거리 구경	개인차	코스메틱, 패션 브랜드 위주	주말엔 사람이 많음 6	18:00	명동 교자(칼국수) 저녁	약 12,000원~15,000원	한국 대표 음식: 칼국수, 만두 추천	대기줄 있을 수 있음 7	19:00	명동 야시장 구경	간식 5,000~8,000원	닭꼬치, 핫도그, 고구마 등 스트리트 푸드	소지품 주의 여기 나온 명소들 찾아줘', '🍽️ **이노시시**  \n📍 03981 서울 마포구 성미산로 197  \n🍜 Fresh sashimi and izakaya-style dishes  \n\n이노시시는 신선한 회를 저렴한 가격에 제공하는 연남동의 인기 이자카야입니다. 최근에는 예약제로 운영되며, 저녁 6시와 9시에 오마카세를 즐길 수 있습니다. 당일 예약 없이 방문할 경우, 3만원과 5만원의 사시미 코스 중에서 선택할 수 있습니다.  \n\n이곳은 신선한 재료와 합리적인 가격으로 많은 현지인들에게 사랑받고 있습니다. 이자카야 문화가 뿌리 깊은 일본의 영향을 받아, 친구나 가족과 함께 편안한 분위기에서 즐길 수 있는 공간입니다. 전통적인 일본식 저녁 식사를 경험하며, 한국에서의 특별한 미식 여행을 즐길 수 있습니다.  \n\n이노시시에서 신선한 회의 맛을 직접 느껴보세요!', '2025-11-19 05:10:15'),
	(948, 8, NULL, '인천국제공항 찾아줘', '📍 **Ground Seoul**  \n🏛️ 03145 26, Insadong 9-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 11:00~18:00 (Vary per exhibition)  \n\nAt Ground Seoul, you can immerse yourself in a variety of exhibitions, performances, and events that celebrate artistic expression. The space is designed to be accessible for everyone, with facilities that cater to diverse audiences. Admission fees may vary depending on the exhibition, so be sure to check in advance!\n\nLocated in the culturally rich Insadong district, Ground Seoul is a modern hub that embraces traditional and contemporary arts. This venue not only showcases local talent but also hosts international artists, making it a vibrant part of Seoul\'s artistic landscape. Locals love it for its unique atmosphere and the opportunity to engage with a wide range of creative expressions.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to explore this artistic gem in the heart of Seoul—it\'s a perfect spot to inspire your creativity and appreciation for the arts!', '2025-11-19 05:10:30'),
	(949, 8, NULL, '명동교자가 어딨어?', '📍 **Seochon Hanok Village**  \n🏛️ 03037 45, Pilwoon-daero, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Open daily, 24 hours  \n\nSeochon Hanok Village is a charming neighborhood where you can wander through narrow alleys lined with traditional Korean hanoks (houses). Admission is free, and there are plenty of cafes, art galleries, and shops to explore. The area is easily accessible by public transport, making it a convenient stop during your Seoul adventure.  \n\nThis village is one of the oldest in Seoul, dating back to the Joseon Dynasty, and showcases the unique architectural style and cultural heritage of Korea. It’s a beloved spot for locals, who appreciate its blend of traditional and modern life, as well as its artistic vibe. Many historical figures are said to have lived in this area, adding to its cultural significance and charm.  \n\nDon’t miss the chance to stroll through this picturesque village and soak in the rich history and vibrant atmosphere!', '2025-11-19 05:10:45'),
	(950, 8, NULL, 'Tell me about Incheon International Airport ', '📍 **Incheon International Airport**  \n🏛️ 272 Gonghang-ro, Jung-gu, Incheon, South Korea  \n\n[Incheon International Airport is a major gateway to South Korea, serving as a hub for international flights and offering a wide range of facilities, including shopping, dining, and leisure activities. The airport features two terminals, both equipped with modern amenities and services, including free Wi-Fi, lounges, and cultural experiences. Admission is free to enter the airport, but be sure to check for any specific access regulations depending on your travel plans.]\n\n[Opened in 2001, Incheon International Airport has consistently ranked among the best airports in the world for its exceptional service, cleanliness, and efficiency. It plays a crucial role in connecting Korea to the global community, and its design incorporates elements of Korean culture, making it a unique experience for travelers. The airport also hosts various art installations and cultural exhibitions that showcase Korea\'s heritage and innovation.]\n\n[Don’t miss the chance to explore this incredible airport, whether you’re arriving, departing, or just passing through!]\n\n', '2025-11-19 05:11:22'),
	(951, 8, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Gyoza', '🍽️ **Myeongdong Gyoza**  \n📍 서울특별시 중구 명동 10길 29  \n\n🥟 [Specialty dish: Dumplings (Gyoza)]\n\nMyeongdong Gyoza is renowned for its delicious handmade dumplings, with a price range typically between 8,000 to 12,000 KRW per serving. They offer both steamed and fried options, and the restaurant usually opens from 11 AM to 10 PM, making it a convenient stop for lunch or dinner. To order, simply choose your desired dumpling type at the counter or from the menu at your table.\n\nThis popular eatery is a favorite among locals and tourists alike, often bustling with energy and laughter. The casual dining atmosphere, combined with the delicious flavors of the dumplings, makes it a beloved spot in the heart of Myeongdong. The tradition of enjoying gyoza in Korea is deeply rooted, symbolizing comfort and togetherness among friends and family.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to savor these delightful dumplings during your visit!', '2025-11-19 05:11:45'),
	(952, 8, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Gyoza', '🍽️ **명동교자**\n📍 서울 중구 명동10길 29 (명동)\n🍜 [Korean dumplings, specialty dish: 칼국수 (Kalguksu - handmade knife-cut noodles) and 만두 (Mandu - dumplings)]\n\n명동교자는 칼국수와 만두로 유명한 레스토랑으로, 가격대는 대체로 8,000원에서 12,000원 사이입니다. 이곳은 점심과 저녁 시간에 항상 붐비며, 대기할 수 있으니 미리 예약하거나 일찍 방문하는 것이 좋습니다. 주문은 테이블에서 직접 하며, 메뉴는 한글과 영어로 제공되어 외국인 손님도 쉽게 이용할 수 있습니다.\n\n명동교자는 서울의 명동 지역에서 오랜 역사를 자랑하며, 많은 현지인과 관광객들이 이곳의 특별한 칼국수와 만두를 맛보기 위해 방문합니다. 아늑하고 활기찬 분위기 속에서, 친구나 가족과 함께 나누어 먹는 것이 한국의 식사 문화의 중요한 부분입니다. 이곳의 따뜻한 국물은', '2025-11-19 05:57:16'),
	(953, 8, NULL, 'Tell me where the main branch of Uraeok is.', '🎬 **Mongjungheon Anguk Branch**  \n📍 8 minutes walk from Exit 1 of Anguk Station, 31-22 Bukchon-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 우리영화  \n\nTo get to Mongjungheon Anguk Branch, simply exit from Anguk Station and enjoy an 8-minute stroll through the picturesque streets of Bukchon Hanok Village. The cafe is open daily, offering a cozy atmosphere perfect for relaxation, and there’s no admission fee to enter. You can indulge in a delightful selection of traditional Korean teas and desserts while soaking in the tranquil ambiance.\n\nIn the drama "Our Movie," this cafe serves as a significant backdrop for several heartfelt scenes, showcasing the characters’ emotional connections and pivotal moments. The traditional yet stylish interior reflects the essence of Korean culture, making it a perfect filming location that resonates with the story\'s themes. This charming spot was chosen to enhance the narrative\'s warmth and intimacy, making it memorable for viewers.\n\nK-Drama fans will love visiting this location, as it allows you to step into the world of your favorite characters while enjoying the unique flavors of Korean tea culture!', '2025-11-19 05:59:25'),
	(954, 8, NULL, 'Tell me about Tongin Market and introduce some places worth visiting nearby. ', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-19 06:08:44'),
	(955, 8, NULL, 'Tell me about it and introduce me to places worth visiting nearby. ', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-19 06:09:39'),
	(956, 8, NULL, 'Introduce me to Korea\'s famous landmarks. ', '📍 **The National Museum of Korea**  \n🏛️ 04383 137, Seobinggo-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ - Mon, Tues, Thur, Fri, Sunday 10:00 - 18:00 KST  \n- Wed, Saturday 10:00 - 21:00 KST  \n*  Outside exhibitions may be viewed from 07:00 KST  \n\nAt The National Museum of Korea, you can explore a vast collection of nearly 420,000 artifacts that span thousands of years of history. Admission is free, and the museum is equipped with facilities such as rest areas, cafes, and gift shops, making it accessible for everyone, including those with mobility challenges. Don’t forget to check out the realistic digital animations and VR experiences that bring history to life!  \n\nThis museum serves as a cultural treasure trove, showcasing Korea\'s rich history and heritage. It is the largest museum in South Korea and plays a vital role in educating both locals and visitors about the country\'s past. With its beautifully curated galleries, the museum is a beloved spot for Koreans, who appreciate the opportunity to connect with their cultural roots.  \n\nMake sure to visit The National Museum of Korea to', '2025-11-19 06:12:21'),
	(957, 8, NULL, 'Introduce me to Korea\'s famous landmarks. ', '📍 **The National Museum of Korea**  \n🏛️ 04383 137, Seobinggo-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ - Mon, Tues, Thur, Fri, Sunday 10:00 - 18:00 KST  \n- Wed, Saturday 10:00 - 21:00 KST  \n* Outside exhibitions may be viewed from 07:00 KST  \n\nYou can explore a vast collection of nearly 420,000 artifacts that span thousands of years of Korean history. The museum offers engaging regular exhibitions, educational programs, and even immersive experiences with digital animations and VR technology. Admission is free, making it accessible for everyone, and facilities include a café and a gift shop.  \n\nThe National Museum of Korea stands as a testament to Korea\'s rich heritage and serves as a cultural beacon for locals and visitors alike. With its extensive collection, the museum tells stories of Korea\'s past, showcasing everything from ancient pottery to royal garments. Locals love it for its educational value and serene environment, making it a perfect spot for both learning and relaxation.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to immerse yourself in Korea\'s history and culture—this is a must-visit destination on your journey!  ', '2025-11-19 06:18:53'),
	(958, 8, NULL, 'Recommend 10 drama filming locations near Gyeongbokgung Palace ', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-19 06:21:00'),
	(959, 8, NULL, 'Recommend 10 popular spots near Gyeongbokgung Palace ', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 06:21:35'),
	(960, 8, NULL, 'Recommend 10 popular spots near Gyeongbokgung Palace ', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 06:21:40'),
	(961, 8, NULL, 'Recommend 10 great restaurants near Gyeongbokgung Palace. ', '🍽️ **한방삼계탕**\n📍 서울 종로구 사직로 7길 6\n🍜 Korean Ginseng Chicken Soup\n\nThis restaurant specializes in Samgyetang, a traditional Korean dish made with a whole young chicken stuffed with ginseng, garlic, and rice. The price range is reasonable, typically around 15,000 to 20,000 KRW per serving, and they are open daily from 11 AM to 10 PM. You can order directly at the counter or enjoy a sit-down meal.\n\nLocals love this place for its comforting and revitalizing soup, especially during the summer heat. The dining atmosphere is cozy and inviting, often filled with families and friends sharing a hearty meal. Samgyetang is not just a dish; it’s a cultural experience that embodies the Korean belief in food as medicine.\n\nDon’t miss the chance to warm your soul with a bowl of this nourishing dish!\n\n---\n\n🍽️ **광화문 국밥**\n📍 서울 종로구 세종대로 175\n🍜 Pork Soup with Rice\n\nKnown for their hearty Gukbap, this spot serves a delicious pork-based soup accompanied by rice. Prices are affordable, averaging ', '2025-11-19 06:22:47'),
	(962, 8, NULL, 'Recommend 10 great restaurants near Gyeongbokgung Palace.', '🍽️ **경성고기꾼**  \n📍 02453  서울 동대문구 회기로21길 8 (회기동)  1층  \n🍜 Korean BBQ, Beef Soup, Yukhoe Bibimbap  \n\n경성고기꾼 offers quality beef grilled over charcoal at reasonable prices. You can enjoy a variety of beef cuts, and their beef soup is hearty and flavorful, loaded with generous portions of meat. The restaurant is typically open from lunch until late evening, making it a great spot for both lunch and dinner. \n\nLocals love 경성고기꾼 for its warm and inviting atmosphere, where friends and family gather to enjoy delicious grilled meats. The experience of grilling your own beef at the table is a cherished tradition in Korean dining culture, adding to the fun and interactive nature of the meal. The restaurant\'s focus on quality and affordability makes it a popular choice for both locals and visitors. \n\nDon’t miss the chance to savor the delightful flavors of their grilled beef and unique dishes!  \n\n---\n\n🍽️ **한미리**  \n📍 서울 종로구 자하문로 15길 31  \n🍜 Traditional Korean Cuisine, Kim', '2025-11-19 06:23:03'),
	(963, 3, NULL, 'hello ', '📍 **Seoul Science Museum**  \n🏛️ 01792 160, Hangeulbiseok-ro, Nowon-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Tue-Fri 09:30-17:30 KST  \n\nThe Seoul Science Museum is a fantastic destination for science enthusiasts of all ages! Visitors can explore interactive exhibits, engaging workshops, and fascinating displays that cover various scientific fields. Admission fees are usually quite affordable, making it accessible for families, and the museum is equipped with facilities that cater to individuals with disabilities.\n\nOpened to promote scientific understanding and education, the museum plays a vital role in South Korea’s commitment to fostering a love for science and technology among its citizens. Locals appreciate this space for its hands-on learning opportunities and often share stories of memorable school trips and family outings that inspire curiosity and imagination.\n\nDon’t miss the chance to ignite your passion for science and have a blast at the Seoul Science Museum!', '2025-11-19 06:29:59'),
	(964, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', '📍 **Gyeongbokgung Palace**  \n🏛️ 03045 161, Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ January & February: 09:00 - 17:00  \nMarch - May: 09:00 - 18:00  \nJune - August: 09:00 - 18:30  \nSeptember & October: 09:00 - 18:00  \nNovember & December: 09:00 - 17:00  \n*Last entry one hour before closing*  \n\nVisitors to Gyeongbokgung Palace can explore the stunning architecture, beautiful gardens, and fascinating museums, including the National Palace Museum of Korea. Admission is typically free, but guided tours and special exhibitions may incur fees. The palace is equipped with facilities like restrooms, and it is wheelchair accessible, ensuring all guests can enjoy its grandeur.\n\nAs the first and largest of the royal palaces built during the Joseon Dynasty, Gyeongbokgung Palace holds immense historical significance, symbolizing the sovereignty of Korea\'s past. Locals cherish this majestic site not only for its beauty but also for its rich stories, including the changing of the guard ceremony and the legends surrounding the palace\'s construction', '2025-11-19 06:34:45'),
	(965, 6, NULL, 'hello', 'Hello there! 👋 I\'m your friendly Seoul travel guide! What adventure are you planning today?', '2025-11-19 06:58:40'),
	(966, 6, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', '📍 **Gyeongbokgung Palace**  \n🏛️ 03045 161, Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ January & February: 09:00 - 17:00  \nMarch - May: 09:00 - 18:00  \nJune - August: 09:00 - 18:30  \nSeptember & October: 09:00 - 18:00  \nNovember & December: 09:00 - 17:00  \n*Last entry one hour before closing*  \n\nVisitors to Gyeongbokgung Palace can explore its stunning architecture, beautiful gardens, and the National Palace Museum of Korea. Admission is generally free for children and students, while adults may need to pay a small fee. The palace is wheelchair accessible, with facilities like restrooms and information centers available for a comfortable visit.  \n\nGyeongbokgung Palace, built in 1395, was the first and largest of the royal palaces during the Joseon Dynasty, symbolizing the power and sovereignty of the ruling family. Locals cherish this historic site not just for its grandeur but also for the stories of kings and queens that echo through its halls, making it a beloved spot for both', '2025-11-19 06:59:10'),
	(967, 6, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Cathedral', 'I\'m your AI-powered Seoul travel assistant! 🤖✨ \n\nI specialize in:\n🏛️ Tourist attractions and landmarks\n🍜 Restaurant recommendations  \n🎬 K-Drama filming locations\n🎭 Festivals and cultural events\n🗺️ Travel tips and local insights\n\nI use advanced AI to understand what you\'re looking for and provide personalized recommendations. What would you like to explore in Seoul?', '2025-11-19 06:59:14'),
	(968, 6, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nN Seoul Tower offers visitors an unforgettable experience with its stunning night views of the city. The observatory provides a 360-degree panoramic view, making it a perfect spot for photography. Admission fees vary, so be sure to check the official website for the latest information, and facilities include cafes, gift shops, and accessible options for all visitors.  \n\nOriginally built in 1969 as a transmission tower, N Seoul Tower has become a symbol of Seoul and a popular destination for both tourists and locals. It is steeped in cultural significance, often featured in Korean dramas and films, and the tradition of attaching “locks of love” to its railings adds a romantic touch. Locals cherish the tower for its breathtaking views and as a beloved meeting point, sharing countless memories amidst the vibrant city lights.  \n\nDon’t miss the chance to experience the magic of N Seoul Tower at night; it’s truly a sight to behold!', '2025-11-19 06:59:33'),
	(969, 6, NULL, 'I\'m visiting Korea for the first time. I’ll stay 5 days in Seoul. Can you help me plan?', 'I can help you with lots of things! 🚀\n\n**TRAVEL PLANNING:**\n• Find perfect attractions for your interests\n• Recommend authentic restaurants\n• Locate K-Drama filming spots\n• Discover festivals and events\n\n**SMART FEATURES:**\n• Understand your preferences and mood\n• Compare different options\n• Provide cultural context and tips\n• Generate interactive maps\n\nJust tell me what you\'re in the mood for, and I\'ll help you discover Seoul!', '2025-11-19 07:01:50'),
	(970, 6, NULL, 'I love cafés, food markets, and scenic walks. I’m not into nightlife.', '🍽️ **카페 시바**  \n📍 04352 서울 용산구 한강대로 276-1 (남영동) 1층  \n🍜 비건 음식 및 음료\n\n카페 시바는 다양한 시그니처 비건 음식과 음료를 제공하는 곳으로, 건강한 식사를 원하는 분들에게 안성맞춤입니다. 가격대는 합리적이며, 일반적으로 10,000원에서 20,000원 사이입니다. 운영 시간은 보통 오전 10시부터 오후 8시까지이며, 방문 시 메뉴를 살펴본 후 직접 주문하면 됩니다.\n\n이곳은 비건 식단을 지향하는 사람들에게 큰 사랑을 받고 있으며, 건강한 라이프스타일을 추구하는 문화의 일환으로 자리잡고 있습니다. 아늑하고 편안한 분위기 속에서, 자연 재료로 만든 음식을 즐기며 지속 가능한 식문화를 경험할 수 있습니다.\n\n비건 요리를 처음 접해보신다면, 꼭 카페 시바에 들러 보세요!', '2025-11-19 07:02:06'),
	(971, 6, NULL, 'I\'m not into shopping, but I love history and food.', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion Tteok (Korean Rice Cakes)\n\n정애맛담 offers a delightful selection of traditional Korean tteok with a modern twist. Their specialties include the chewy injeolmi coated in powdered soybean and the unique angbukk, which features red bean paste and butter wrapped in a soft, steamed cake. Prices are generally affordable, with most dishes ranging from 3,000 to 8,000 KRW. The restaurant is typically open from 10 AM to 8 PM, and visitors can order directly at the counter or take advantage of their takeaway options.\n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 not only for its delicious fusion flavors but also for its homage to traditional Korean culinary practices. Tteok has long been a staple in Korean culture, symbolizing celebration and togetherness, making it a meaningful dish to share with family and friends. The cozy atmosphere and the sight of freshly made tteok being crafted add to the experience, allowing visitors to immerse themselves in the rich food traditions of Korea.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to savor these delightful creations that beautifully blend the past and', '2025-11-19 07:02:20'),
	(972, 6, NULL, 'I prefer relaxing over rushing.', '🎬 **Conrad Seoul Artrio**  \n📍 8 minutes walk from Exit 3 of Yeouido Station, 10 International Finance-ro, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 가슴이 뛴다  \n\nTo reach Conrad Seoul Artrio, simply exit Yeouido Station via Exit 3 and enjoy an 8-minute stroll to this luxurious cafe. It\'s a perfect spot to unwind, with opening hours typically from 10 AM to 10 PM, allowing you ample time to savor their delicious menu of drinks and desserts. Visitors can soak in the stylish interiors and relax while enjoying the stunning night views of the Seoul skyline from the cozy window seats.  \n\nIn the drama 가슴이 뛴다, significant scenes were filmed here, showcasing the cafe\'s elegant atmosphere that perfectly complements the romantic storyline. The production team likely chose this location for its breathtaking views and sophisticated ambiance, which resonate with the themes of love and connection in the series.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, a visit to Conrad Seoul Artrio promises a delightful experience where you can immerse yourself in the world of your favorite characters while enjoying a peaceful moment in this beautiful setting!', '2025-11-19 07:02:28'),
	(973, 6, NULL, 'I can’t eat spicy food.', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion Tteok (Korean rice cakes)\n\n정애맛담 specializes in traditional Korean tteok, elevated with a modern twist. Their signature dishes include the soft and chewy injeolmi coated in soybean flour and the an-bokkeum, which combines sweet red bean paste and butter in a rice cake instead of bread. Prices typically range from 3,000 to 8,000 KRW per item, making it an affordable treat. The restaurant is open daily from 10 AM to 8 PM, and visitors can place orders at the counter or take advantage of their takeout options.\n\nLocals flock to 정애맛담 for its innovative take on traditional flavors, celebrating the rich history of tteok that dates back centuries in Korean culture. The warm, inviting atmosphere allows diners to experience the joy of sharing these beloved treats, often enjoyed during special occasions and family gatherings. \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to indulge in these delightful fusion rice cakes that bring a contemporary flair to a cherished tradition!', '2025-11-19 07:02:38'),
	(974, 6, NULL, 'I want to visit a few K-drama or K-pop related spots.', '🎬 **softie**  \n📍 12 minutes above Exit 3 of Hongik University Station, 171 Seongmisan-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 여행을 대신해 드립니다  \n\nTo visit Softy, simply take the subway to Hongik University Station and follow the signs to Exit 3. The charming street is just a short 12-minute walk from there! While there are no specific opening hours or admission fees, it\'s best enjoyed during daylight hours when you can appreciate the serene atmosphere and explore the nearby cafes and restaurants.\n\nIn the drama "여행을 대신해 드립니다," Softy serves as a picturesque backdrop for several key scenes that highlight the characters\' emotional journeys. Its tranquil setting complements the themes of reflection and personal growth in the story, making it an ideal location for filming. The production team likely chose this spot for its unique blend of urban charm and peaceful ambiance, perfectly capturing the essence of the characters\' experiences.\n\nK-Drama fans will absolutely love strolling through Softy, reminiscing about their favorite moments from the show while enjoying the delightful surroundings!', '2025-11-19 07:02:47'),
	(975, 6, NULL, 'I want solo-friendly restaurants.', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997  서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion Tteok (Korean rice cakes)\n\n정애맛담 is a modern fusion tteok shop that offers a creative twist on traditional Korean rice cakes. Their specialties include the chewy injeolmi coated with powdered soybean flour and the unique angbaek-ddeok, which features red bean filling and butter wrapped in soft, steamed rice cake. Prices are reasonable, typically ranging from 3,000 to 5,000 KRW per item. The shop is open daily from 10 AM to 7 PM, and visitors can simply order at the counter.\n\nLocals love 정애맛담 for its innovative take on beloved traditional snacks, blending nostalgia with contemporary flavors. Tteok holds significant cultural importance in Korea, often enjoyed during celebrations and special occasions. The dining atmosphere is casual and welcoming, making it a perfect spot for solo travelers to savor a taste of Korean heritage.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to indulge in these delightful treats that beautifully marry tradition and modernity!', '2025-11-19 07:02:57');
INSERT INTO `conversations` (`convers_id`, `user_id`, `fullconverse`, `question`, `response`, `datetime`) VALUES
	(976, 6, NULL, 'I prefer easy public transportation routes.', '🎬 **softie**  \n📍 12 minutes above Exit 3 of Hongik University Station, 171 Seongmisan-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 여행을 대신해 드립니다  \n\nTo reach softie, simply take the subway to Hongik University Station and exit via Exit 3. From there, it’s just a pleasant 12-minute walk to the charming street of softie. There are no specific opening hours or admission fees, making it a perfect spot for a leisurely stroll, where you can enjoy various cafes and restaurants along the way.\n\nIn the drama 여행을 대신해 드립니다, softie serves as a picturesque backdrop for several intimate scenes, capturing the essence of quiet reflection and connection between characters. The production team likely chose this location for its serene atmosphere and aesthetic appeal, which beautifully complements the themes of the drama.\n\nK-Drama fans will find softie to be a delightful escape, allowing you to walk in the footsteps of your favorite characters and soak in the enchanting atmosphere of Seoul!', '2025-11-19 07:03:06'),
	(977, 6, NULL, 'Can you create a 3-day itinerary with travel times included?', 'Hey Hunters! 😅 지금 추천할 미션 장소가 없네... 다시 검색해볼게! 🔥', '2025-11-19 07:06:52'),
	(978, 6, NULL, 'Can you create a 3-day itinerary with travel times included?', 'Hey Hunters! 😅 지금 추천할 미션 장소가 없네... 다시 검색해볼게! 🔥', '2025-11-19 07:07:08'),
	(979, 6, NULL, 'Can you create a 3-day itinerary with travel times included?', 'Hey Hunters! 😅 지금 추천할 미션 장소가 없네... 다시 검색해볼게! 🔥', '2025-11-19 07:07:18'),
	(980, 6, NULL, 'How do I get a T-money card? Is Hongdae safe at night?', '🎬 **Lotteria Hongdae Branch**  \n📍 2-minute walk from Exit 1 of Hongik University Station, 141 Yanghwa-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 우리들의 초콜릿 순간  \n\nTo get a T-money card, you can purchase one at convenience stores like GS25, CU, or 7-Eleven, which are plentiful in Seoul. The card can be used for public transportation and at various shops, making it very handy for your travels. Lotteria Hongdae Branch is open daily, and you can enjoy a variety of menu items while soaking in the cozy atmosphere that made it a popular filming spot.  \n\nIn "Our Chocolate Moment," several heartwarming scenes were filmed here, showcasing the characters sharing intimate conversations and moments over delicious food. The production team likely chose this location for its modern and inviting ambiance, which perfectly complements the show\'s themes of connection and romance.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting Lotteria Hongdae Branch is a must to relive those touching moments and immerse yourself in the world of your favorite drama!', '2025-11-19 07:07:32'),
	(981, 6, NULL, '“Everything Will Come True” Where can I find the filming locations for Korean dramas?', '🎬 **KB Golden Life Plus Center**  \n📍 3 minutes above Exit 3 of Apgujeong Station, 849, Eonju-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 다 이루어질지니  \n\nTo visit the KB Golden Life Plus Center, take the subway to Apgujeong Station and use Exit 3. The center is just a short 3-minute walk from the station. It’s open during regular business hours, allowing visitors to enjoy its modern architecture and beautiful landscaping. You can take stunning photos and relax in the comfortable atmosphere of the building’s interior.  \n\nIn the drama "다 이루어질지니," this location is memorable for its stylish design and serves as a backdrop for key scenes that highlight the characters\' journeys. The unique arch structure and wide windows create a visually striking setting, making it a perfect fit for the show\'s modern themes. The production team likely chose this location for its aesthetic appeal and the serene environment that enhances the narrative.  \n\nK-Drama fans will love visiting this spot, as it offers a glimpse into the world of their favorite shows while providing a beautiful place to unwind and capture memorable moments!', '2025-11-19 07:07:46'),
	(982, 6, NULL, 'Is it rude to speak loudly on the subway?', '🎬 **Subway Sogang University**  \n📍 3-minute walk from Exit 6 of Sinchon Station, 21, Baekbeom-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 협상의 기술  \n\nTo visit Subway Sogang University, take the Seoul Metro to Sinchon Station and exit through Exit 6. The subway station is easily accessible and open 24/7, allowing visitors to explore at their convenience. While there, you can soak in the lively atmosphere of Sogang University and take memorable photos that resemble scenes from your favorite K-Drama.\n\nIn "The Art of Negotiation," several key scenes were filmed at this subway station, showcasing the unique blend of urban life and university culture. The production team chose this location to capture the dynamic interactions between characters, reflecting the hustle and bustle of city life that resonates with many viewers. \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this iconic location is a must-do to relive the moments of your favorite show and immerse yourself in the vibrant atmosphere of Seoul!', '2025-11-19 07:08:07'),
	(983, 6, NULL, 'Should I buy a T-money card or use my phone?', '🎬 **National Banking Association**  \n📍 8 minutes walk from Exit 5 of Euljiro Entrance Station, 19, Myeongdong 11-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 지금 거신 전화는  \n\nTo visit the National Banking Association, simply take the subway to Euljiro Entrance Station and follow the signs to Exit 5. The building is open to the public, and while there are no specific admission fees, you can enjoy the stunning architecture and take photos of the modern exterior. Nearby, you’ll find various cafes and shops, perfect for a leisurely stroll after your visit.  \n\nIn the drama 지금 거신 전화는, the National Banking Association serves as a key backdrop for several pivotal scenes, showcasing the interactions between characters in a sleek, urban environment. The production team likely chose this location for its modern aesthetics and central location, which perfectly aligns with the themes of ambition and corporate life depicted in the show.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this iconic filming location is a must-do experience that allows you to step into the world of your favorite characters!', '2025-11-19 07:08:16'),
	(984, 8, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', '📍 **Hangang River Bus**  \n🏛️ 05500 1-2 Jamsil-dong area, Jamsil Pier, Songpa-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Weekdays (68 trips daily) 6:30 AM-10:30 PM / Weekends (48 trips daily) 9:30 AM-10:30 PM  \nExpress route weekdays 16 trips daily *Weekday commute (6:30 AM-9:00 AM), after work (6:00 PM-8:30 PM)  \n\nHop aboard the Hangang River Bus for a scenic cruise along the iconic Han River! You can enjoy stunning views of Seoul\'s skyline, parks, and bridges while relaxing on the water. Admission fees are very reasonable, and the buses are equipped with comfortable seating to enhance your experience. Accessibility is great, ensuring everyone can enjoy the ride.  \n\nThe Hangang River holds immense cultural significance for Seoulites, serving as a central hub for leisure and recreation. Historically, the river has been a vital waterway for trade and transportation, shaping the city\'s development. Locals cherish the river for its vibrant atmosphere, especially during sunset when it becomes a picturesque backdrop for evening gatherings and picnics.  \n\n', '2025-11-19 07:10:00'),
	(985, 8, NULL, 'tell me hongdae', '📍 **Sungkyunkwan University**  \n🏛️ 03063 25-2, Sungkyunkwan-ro (Sungkyunkwan Univ.), Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Open daily, hours may vary by building  \n\nVisitors can explore the beautiful campus, which features historical buildings such as the Myeongnyundang Hall, and the Confucian Shrine. Admission is free, making it accessible for everyone, and the campus is easily reachable via Hyehwa Station. Don\'t miss the chance to stroll through the tranquil grounds and enjoy the stunning architecture.\n\nFounded in 1398 by King Taejo of Joseon, Sungkyunkwan University is not only the oldest university in Asia but also a symbol of Korea\'s rich academic heritage. It played a crucial role in the Confucian education system during the Joseon Dynasty, and today it continues to be a prestigious institution. Locals cherish it as a place of learning and a testament to Korea\'s historical commitment to education.\n\nBe sure to add Sungkyunkwan University to your itinerary for a blend of history, culture, and stunning scenery!', '2025-11-19 07:10:43'),
	(986, 6, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nVisitors to N Seoul Tower can enjoy stunning panoramic views of Seoul, especially enchanting at night when the city lights twinkle below. The observatory offers a breathtaking experience, and while admission fees may vary, they typically range around 10,000 KRW for adults. Facilities include elevators for easy access, and the tower is equipped to accommodate visitors with disabilities.  \n\nN Seoul Tower, originally built in 1969 as a communication tower, has become a symbol of Seoul and a popular spot for both locals and tourists. It holds significant cultural importance as a place for couples to attach "locks of love," symbolizing their eternal bond, and has been featured in numerous Korean dramas and films, making it a beloved site with many heartwarming stories.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to visit N Seoul Tower at night for an unforgettable experience of Seoul’s dazzling skyline!', '2025-11-19 07:21:12'),
	(987, 6, NULL, 'How do I use the subway in Seoul?', '🎬 **Subway Sogang University**  \n📍 3-minute walk from Exit 6 of Sinchon Station, 21, Baekbeom-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 협상의 기술  \n\nTo visit Subway Sogang University, simply take Line 2 (Green Line) to Sinchon Station and exit at Exit 6. The subway operates from around 5:30 AM to midnight, making it convenient for travelers. Once you arrive, you can explore the vibrant atmosphere of Sogang University, take photos in iconic spots from the drama, and enjoy nearby cafes and restaurants.\n\nIn "The Art of Negotiation," several key scenes were filmed at this location, showcasing the university\'s bustling environment. The production team likely chose this spot for its lively backdrop, which perfectly complements the themes of negotiation and dialogue central to the storyline, giving viewers a taste of university life in Seoul.\n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this location is a must-do, as it allows you to step into the world of your favorite characters and capture unforgettable memories!', '2025-11-19 07:21:24'),
	(988, 6, NULL, 'Any must-try desserts or cafés for first-time visitors?', '🍽️ **설빙**  \n📍 04050 서울 마포구 홍익로6길 15 (동교동, 삼주빌딩) 2층 설빙 홍대입구역점  \n🍜 Korean traditional dessert café specializing in bingsu (shaved ice)  \n\n설빙 is a renowned Korean dessert café that offers a delightful array of traditional desserts, with a particular focus on bingsu, made from finely shaved ice and topped with seasonal fruits and traditional ingredients. Prices typically range from 8,000 to 15,000 KRW, making it an affordable treat for everyone. The café is usually open from 10 AM to 11 PM, and visitors can order at the counter or via their digital menu.\n\nLocals adore 설빙 for its nostalgic flavors and the refreshing relief it provides, especially during the hot summer months. Bingsu holds cultural significance as a beloved summertime snack that brings people together, evoking memories of childhood and family gatherings. The café\'s vibrant atmosphere, often filled with laughter and chatter, creates a communal dining experience that reflects the joy of sharing dessert with friends.\n\nDon\'t miss out on trying 설빙\'s signature mango bingsu—it\'s a must-have for anyone', '2025-11-19 07:21:45'),
	(989, 6, NULL, 'hello', 'Hello there! 👋 I\'m your friendly Seoul travel guide! What adventure are you planning today?', '2025-11-19 07:30:27'),
	(990, 6, NULL, 'Should I buy a T-money card or use my phone?', '🎬 **National Banking Association**  \n📍 8 minutes walk from Exit 5 of Euljiro Entrance Station, 19, Myeongdong 11-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 지금 거신 전화는  \n\nTo visit the National Banking Association, take the subway to Euljiro Entrance Station and follow the signs to Exit 5. The location is just an 8-minute walk from there. While the building itself is not an open museum, you can admire its stunning modern architecture and explore the surrounding area, which is filled with charming cafes and shops perfect for a leisurely stroll.\n\nIn the drama 지금 거신 전화는, the National Banking Association serves as a key setting where pivotal scenes unfold, showcasing the characters\' interactions and plot developments. The production team likely chose this location for its striking urban aesthetic, which beautifully complements the show\'s modern themes and adds depth to the storyline.\n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this iconic filming location will not only bring back memories of your favorite scenes but also allow you to immerse yourself in the vibrant atmosphere of Seoul!', '2025-11-19 07:30:44'),
	(991, 6, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', '📍 **COEX**  \n🏛️ 06164 513, Yeongdeung-daero, Gangnam-gu, Seoul (COEX)  \n⏰ Open daily, hours vary by event  \n\nVisitors to COEX can explore a wide array of exhibitions, international conferences, and cultural events. Admission fees vary depending on the specific event or expo, but many areas, such as the COEX Mall and library, are free to enter. The venue is equipped with excellent facilities, including accessible entrances and restrooms, ensuring everyone can enjoy their visit comfortably.  \n\nCOEX has a rich history as a premier convention center, established in 1979, and it plays a vital role in Seoul\'s status as a global city. Locals appreciate COEX not only for its business significance but also for its vibrant atmosphere, diverse dining options, and cultural events, making it a hub for both work and play. There are many interesting stories surrounding the center, including its role in hosting major international summits and exhibitions that reflect Korea\'s growth on the global stage.  \n\nDon\'t miss out on experiencing the dynamic energy and cultural offerings of COEX during your visit to Seoul!', '2025-11-19 07:34:49'),
	(992, 6, NULL, 'Is Itaewon still noisy and crowded?', '🎬 **Itaewon Children\'s Park**  \n📍 287-1 Itaewon-dong, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, 10 minutes on foot from Exit 2 of Noksapyeong Station  \n🎭 Featured in: 모범택시2  \n\nItaewon Children\'s Park is easily accessible by foot from Noksapyeong Station, making it a convenient stop for visitors exploring the vibrant Itaewon area. The park is open year-round, and admission is free, allowing families to enjoy its various amusement facilities and expansive lawns. Here, you can relax in nature, let the kids play freely, and take leisurely walks amidst the beautiful greenery.\n\nIn 모범택시2, specific scenes showcasing the park\'s tranquil environment were filmed, highlighting its significance as a backdrop for character interactions. The production team likely chose this location for its peaceful atmosphere and family-friendly vibe, which perfectly complement the themes of the drama. The park\'s combination of urban convenience and natural beauty makes it a charming setting for the story.\n\nK-Drama fans will love visiting Itaewon Children\'s Park, where you can stroll through the same space that brought memorable moments from the show to life!', '2025-11-19 07:35:05'),
	(993, 6, NULL, 'Is it okay to eat alone in Korean restaurants?', '🎬 **The first store in Gongjeong-dong, directly managed by Eel**  \n📍 1 minute above Exit 5 of Gwanghwamun Station, 63 Cheonggyecheon-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 이번 생도 잘 부탁해  \n\nVisitors can easily reach this charming restaurant by taking the subway to Gwanghwamun Station and exiting at Exit 5. The restaurant is typically open from lunchtime until late evening, making it a perfect spot for both lunch and dinner. When you visit, you can enjoy a variety of delicious eel dishes in a cozy atmosphere that reflects the essence of the drama.\n\nIn "Please Take Care of My Life," key scenes were filmed at this location, emphasizing the importance of food and relationships in the storyline. The production team likely chose this particular spot for its inviting ambiance and its ability to showcase the warmth of shared meals, which is a central theme in the drama.  \n\nK-Drama fans will find this location a delightful experience, allowing them to immerse themselves in the world of their favorite show while savoring delicious food!', '2025-11-19 07:35:17'),
	(994, 8, NULL, 'KCONTENT Recommend tourist attractions', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 07:37:29'),
	(995, 8, NULL, 'ㅍKCONTENT Recommend tourist attractions', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 07:37:44'),
	(996, 8, NULL, 'KCONTENT Recommend tourist attractions', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 07:37:52'),
	(997, 8, NULL, 'Kdrama Recommend tourist attractions', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-19 07:38:14'),
	(998, 8, NULL, 'Recommend 5 tourist attractions.', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 07:38:34'),
	(999, 8, NULL, '7t7yjh', '📍 **Seoullo 7017**  \n🏛️ 04509 432, Cheongpa-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul (Bongnae-dong 2-ga, KORAIL Seoul Headquarters)  \n⏰ Open 24 hours  \n\nSeoullo 7017 is a delightful elevated sky garden where you can stroll amidst lush greenery, enjoy beautiful views of the city, and discover various art installations along the way. Admission is free, and the walkway is equipped with multiple rest areas and facilities for visitors, making it accessible for everyone, including those with mobility challenges. You can also find cafés and small shops scattered throughout, perfect for a refreshing break.  \n\nOriginally a busy highway overpass built in 1970, Seoullo was transformed in 2017 into a vibrant pedestrian space, symbolizing urban renewal and community connection. It features 17 different pathways that link various neighborhoods, allowing visitors to explore the local culture and history. This transformation reflects Seoul’s commitment to green spaces and sustainable urban living, making it a favorite spot for both locals and tourists.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience this unique blend of nature and city life—take a leisurely walk on Seoullo 7017 and soak in the', '2025-11-19 07:40:00'),
	(1000, 6, NULL, 'hello', 'Hello there! 👋 I\'m your friendly Seoul travel guide! What adventure are you planning today?', '2025-11-19 07:43:57'),
	(1001, 6, NULL, 'I\'m visiting Korea for the first time. I’ll stay 5 days in Seoul. Can you help me plan?', '🎬 **a guesthouse**  \n📍 1 minute above Exit 2 of Anguk Station, 52-11 Gye-dong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 이번 생도 잘 부탁해  \n\nThis charming guesthouse is easily accessible by taking the subway to Anguk Station, where you’ll find it just a minute\'s walk from Exit 2. The guesthouse typically welcomes visitors year-round, but it\'s best to check in advance for room availability and any booking requirements. Here, you can immerse yourself in the tranquil beauty of a traditional hanok while enjoying the serene natural surroundings.  \n\nIn the drama "이번 생도 잘 부탁해," several memorable scenes were filmed at this picturesque guesthouse, capturing the essence of the characters\' emotional journeys. The production team chose this location for its cultural significance, as it beautifully represents the traditional Korean lifestyle and architecture, enhancing the drama\'s narrative depth.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this guesthouse is a fantastic way to step into the world of your favorite characters and create unforgettable memories in a stunning traditional setting!', '2025-11-19 07:44:36'),
	(1002, 6, NULL, 'I love cafés, food markets, and scenic walks. I’m not into nightlife.', '🎬 **No, Parc**  \n📍 5 minutes walk from Exit 1 of Seonneung Station, 629 Seonneung-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 언젠가는 슬기로울 전공의생활  \n\nNo, Parc is easily accessible from Seonneung Station, making it a convenient stop for visitors exploring the Gangnam area. The café typically opens around 10 AM and closes at 10 PM, providing ample time to enjoy a delicious meal or a cup of coffee. Guests can relax in its spacious interior, perfect for unwinding alone or catching up with friends.  \n\nIn the drama 언젠가는 슬기로울 전공의생활, No, Parc serves as a key setting for many heartwarming scenes where characters share meaningful conversations. The cozy and sophisticated atmosphere beautifully complements the emotional depth of the story, making it an ideal backdrop for filming. The production team likely chose this location for its inviting ambiance, which resonates with the themes of friendship and personal growth in the show.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting No, Parc is a delightful way to immerse yourself in the world of your favorite series while enjoying a serene café experience!', '2025-11-19 07:44:52'),
	(1003, 6, NULL, 'I\'m not into shopping, but I love history and food.', 'Hello there! 👋 I\'m your friendly Seoul travel guide! What adventure are you planning today?', '2025-11-19 07:44:59'),
	(1004, 6, NULL, 'yes i want', 'That’s fantastic! I’d love to help you plan your trip to Seoul! \n\nFirst, could you share a bit about what you’re interested in? \n\nAre you looking for cultural experiences, delicious food, shopping, or perhaps some stunning sights? ', '2025-11-19 07:45:13'),
	(1005, 6, NULL, 'I prefer relaxing over rushing.', 'Hello there! 👋 I\'m your friendly Seoul travel guide! What adventure are you planning today?', '2025-11-19 07:45:20'),
	(1006, 6, NULL, 'Is Namsan Tower really worth visiting, or is it just a tourist trap?', '📍 **Namsan Seoul Tower**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, Korea (Yongsan-dong 2-ga, YTN Seoul Tower)  \n⏰ Weekdays 10:00-22:30, Weekends 10:00-23:00  \n*Last entry 30 minutes before close  \n\nNamsan Seoul Tower offers visitors breathtaking 360-degree views of the city from its observation decks, making it a prime spot for photography and sightseeing. Admission fees for the tower vary, with round-trip fares for the cable car priced at 15,000 KRW for adults and 11,500 KRW for children. The tower is fully accessible, with facilities that cater to all visitors, ensuring a comfortable experience.\n\nHistorically, Namsan has been a revered site for its association with good fortune and love, making the tower a romantic haven for couples. The “Locks of Love” tradition, where lovers attach padlocks as symbols of their everlasting commitment, adds to its cultural significance. Locals often visit to enjoy the stunning views, especially at sunset, and share stories of their own love stories tied to this iconic', '2025-11-19 07:45:37'),
	(1007, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '📍 **Bukchon Hanok Village**  \n🏛️ 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00 ~ 17:00 (Restricted Hours: 17:00 ~ 10:00 the following day; visitors are prohibited from entering restricted areas during these hours)  \n(The Hanok Village is a residential space for local citizens before it is a tourist attraction.)  \n\nVisitors to Bukchon Hanok Village can explore the charming streets lined with traditional hanok, as well as discover art galleries, traditional workshops, and unique restaurants housed in these historic buildings. Admission is free, making it an accessible destination for everyone, though visitors should be mindful of the local residents and adhere to the guidelines for a peaceful experience.  \n\nBukchon Hanok Village boasts a rich history, reflecting 600 years of Seoul\'s past and serving as a residential area that showcases the beauty of traditional Korean architecture. Locals cherish this area not just as a tourist destination but also as a vital part of their cultural heritage, with fascinating stories tied to its streets and homes that highlight the enduring spirit of the community.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to immerse yourself in the enchanting atmosphere of Bukchon Hanok Village and experience the timeless charm of old Seoul!', '2025-11-19 07:52:42'),
	(1008, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Cathedral', '📍 **Myeongdong Cathedral**  \n🏛️ 100-022 74, Myeongdong-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Open daily; hours may vary, so check in advance.  \n\nVisitors to Myeongdong Cathedral can explore the stunning Gothic architecture, featuring high ceilings and magnificent inner pillars. Admission is free, and the cathedral is accessible for most visitors, with facilities for prayer and reflection, as well as a basement sanctuary where the remains of martyrs are enshrined.  \n\nConstructed between 1892 and 1898, Myeongdong Cathedral is the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea and the first Gothic building in the country, making it a significant historical landmark. Locals cherish this site not only for its architectural beauty but also for its role in the spread of Catholicism in Korea, with interesting stories of the nine saints and martyrs commemorated here.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience the serene atmosphere of Myeongdong Cathedral and its beautiful gardens—it\'s a must-visit spot for anyone exploring Seoul!', '2025-11-19 07:52:50'),
	(1009, 3, NULL, 'tell me about myeongdong travel key point', '📍 **Myeongdong Cathedral**  \n🏛️ 100-022 74, Myeongdong-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Open daily; hours may vary for services and events.\n\nVisitors to Myeongdong Cathedral can explore the stunning Gothic architecture, admire the high ceilings, and pay respects in the basement sanctuary where the remains of martyrs are enshrined. Admission is free, making it accessible for everyone, and there are facilities nearby, including restrooms and seating areas in the tranquil St. Mary\'s garden.\n\nMyeongdong Cathedral is the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea, with its construction beginning in 1892 and completed in 1898. It is a significant historical site, designated as Historic site No. 285 in Korea, and locals cherish it not only for its architectural beauty but also for its role in the propagation of Catholicism. The annual cultural festival held every May draws many visitors, celebrating the rich heritage and community spirit surrounding the cathedral.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to soak in the serene atmosphere and rich history of Myeongdong Cathedral during your Seoul adventure!', '2025-11-19 07:53:48'),
	(1010, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nAt N Seoul Tower, visitors can enjoy stunning panoramic views of the city illuminated at night, making it a must-see destination. Admission fees typically range from 10,000 to 12,000 KRW for adults, and various facilities, including cafes and gift shops, are available to enhance your experience. The tower is accessible to all, with elevators and ramps ensuring everyone can enjoy the breathtaking views.\n\nOriginally built in 1969 as a communication tower, N Seoul Tower has become a symbol of the city, offering a blend of modernity and tradition. The tower is famous for its "locks of love," where couples attach padlocks to the railings as a testament to their love, creating a romantic atmosphere that locals cherish. Many Korean dramas and films have showcased the tower, adding to its cultural significance and allure.\n\nDon’t miss the chance to experience the enchanting night views and romantic ambiance at N Seoul Tower—it\'s a perfect way to create unforgettable memories in Seoul!', '2025-11-19 08:12:15'),
	(1011, 6, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Absolutely! 🌟 N Seoul Tower at night is a magical experience that you won\'t want to miss! Perched atop Namsan Mountain, the tower offers breathtaking panoramic views of the city, especially as the skyline sparkles with lights after sunset. 🌃💖 It\'s not just a viewing platform; it\'s steeped in romance with its famous "locks of love," where couples fasten their padlocks as a symbol of their love.\n\nYou can visit the tower from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM, so whether you\'re planning a sunset visit or a late-night adventure, there’s plenty of time to soak in the views. 📍 Located at 105, Namsangongwon-gil in Yongsan-gu, it\'s easily accessible and a perfect addition to your Seoul itinerary. So grab your camera and prepare for a night filled with wonder! 🗺️✨ If you need more details, checking the official website is always a good idea!', '2025-11-19 08:29:05'),
	(1012, 6, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Absolutely! Bukchon Hanok Village is a stunning gem in the heart of Seoul, where you can step back in time and experience the charm of traditional Korean architecture! 🌸🏯 Nestled between the majestic Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces, this village boasts over 600 years of history, with its narrow alleys lined with beautiful hanoks that are still home to local residents. \n\nWhat makes Bukchon truly special is its unique blend of history and culture, where you can find art galleries, traditional workshops, and delightful eateries tucked away in these historic houses. Just remember that it’s a residential area, so let’s keep the noise down and enjoy the peaceful atmosphere! ✨ \n\nYou can visit Bukchon Hanok Village from 10:00 AM to 5:00 PM, but be mindful that entering the area is restricted from 5:00 PM to 10:00 AM the next day. It\'s located at 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul, making it super accessible for a lovely day out! 🗺️ I can\'t wait for you to explore this beautiful slice of Seoul!', '2025-11-19 08:29:32'),
	(1013, 6, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', 'Absolutely! The Hangang River Bus is a fantastic way to experience the beauty of Seoul from the water! 🚤🌊 You can enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, iconic bridges, and the serene riverside parks while cruising along the Han River. There are several routes to choose from, and some even offer themed experiences, like live music or dining options! \n\nIt\'s a lovely way to relax and take in the sights—perfect for a sunny day! If you need help with schedules or recommendations for specific routes, feel free to ask! 😊✨', '2025-11-19 08:29:38'),
	(1014, 6, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', 'Absolutely! COEX is a fantastic destination in Seoul, especially if you love shopping and entertainment! 🌟 It\'s a massive underground shopping mall located in the Gangnam district, featuring over 300 shops, restaurants, and even a beautiful library! 📚✨ \n\nDon’t miss the COEX Aquarium, which is home to a variety of marine life, or the stunning Starfield Library, where you can relax among towering bookshelves. If you\'re there during special events, check out what\'s happening at the COEX Convention & Exhibition Center – they often host exciting exhibitions and fairs! If you need help planning your visit or want more tips, just let me know! 😊', '2025-11-19 08:29:44'),
	(1015, 6, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', 'Welcome to Gyeongbokgung Palace, the majestic heart of Seoul! 🏯 Built in 1395, this stunning palace is the largest of the Five Grand Palaces from the Joseon Dynasty and offers a captivating glimpse into Korea\'s royal history. You\'ll be enchanted by its beautiful architecture, serene gardens, and the lively changing of the guard ceremony. 🌸✨\n\nThe palace is open daily except Tuesdays, with hours varying by season, so be sure to plan your visit accordingly! For instance, from March to May, you can explore from 9:00 AM to 6:00 PM. Located at 161 Sajik-ro in Jongno-gu, it’s easily accessible, and don’t forget: if you wear a hanbok (traditional Korean attire), you can enter for free! 🗺️ \n\nIt\'s a must-visit destination that beautifully blends history and culture, making it a highlight of any trip to Seoul. I can’t wait for you to experience this incredible place! If you have any more questions or need specifics, feel free to check the official website or reach out to the palace management.', '2025-11-19 08:29:55'),
	(1016, 6, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Absolutely! 🌟 N Seoul Tower at night is a must-visit gem in the heart of Seoul! Standing tall on Namsan Mountain, this iconic landmark offers breathtaking panoramic views of the city, especially when the night lights twinkle below. ✨ Not only can you enjoy the stunning scenery, but you can also take part in the charming tradition of fastening a "lock of love" to the railings, making it a romantic spot for couples. 💖\n\nYou can visit the tower from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM, so there\'s plenty of time to soak in the views as the sun sets and the city comes alive. Located at 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, it\'s easily accessible and a perfect addition to your Seoul adventure! 🗺️ Just make sure to check their official website for any updates before your visit. Enjoy your trip! 🏯🌸', '2025-11-19 08:30:54'),
	(1017, 6, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Absolutely! Bukchon Hanok Village is a stunning gem in the heart of Seoul that beautifully showcases 600 years of history through its charming traditional hanok houses. Nestled between Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces, this vibrant residential area isn\'t just a tourist attraction; it\'s a living community where Seoulites thrive amidst art galleries, unique workshops, and delightful restaurants. 🌸✨ \n\nWhen you visit, remember that the village is open from 10:00 AM to 5:00 PM, but access is restricted outside of those hours to respect the residents. Located at 37, Gyedong-gil in Jongno-gu, it’s a perfect spot for a leisurely stroll—just keep the noise down and soak in the serene atmosphere! 🏯🗺️ If you want to dive deeper into its rich culture, the Bukchon Cultural Center is a great resource. I can\'t wait for you to experience the magic of Bukchon!', '2025-11-19 08:31:07'),
	(1018, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Absolutely! 🌟 N Seoul Tower at night is a magical experience you won\'t want to miss! Perched high on Namsan Mountain, it offers some of the most breathtaking panoramic views of the city, especially when the skyline sparkles under the starry sky. 🌌✨ The iconic "locks of love" area is perfect for couples looking to celebrate their love, making it a romantic spot for everyone! 💖 \n\nThe tower is open from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM, so you can enjoy the stunning sunset and watch the city transform as night falls. You can find it at 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul—just a short hike or a cable car ride away! 🏯🗺️ For more details, feel free to check their official website or reach out to them directly. Get ready for an unforgettable night! 🌙', '2025-11-19 08:53:32'),
	(1019, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Absolutely! N Seoul Tower at night is a mesmerizing experience that you simply can\'t miss when visiting Seoul! 🌟 Standing tall on Namsan Mountain, the tower offers breathtaking panoramic views of the city illuminated under the stars. It\'s not only a romantic spot for couples—thanks to the famous "locks of love" tradition—but also a fantastic backdrop for unforgettable photos! 📸✨\n\nOpen daily from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM, you can easily find it at 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu. I recommend heading there just before sunset to enjoy the transition from day to night as the city lights come alive! 🏯🌆 If you want to dive deeper into what makes this landmark special, feel free to check their official website or reach out to them for any specific inquiries. Enjoy your visit! 🌸🗺️', '2025-11-19 08:55:18'),
	(1020, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', 'Absolutely! Bukchon Hanok Village is a charming slice of Seoul that beautifully showcases 600 years of history! 🌸 Nestled between the majestic Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces, this village is a living testament to traditional Korean architecture, with its hundreds of hanok standing shoulder to shoulder in Gaehoe-dong. What makes Bukchon truly special is that it’s not just a tourist spot; it’s a vibrant residential area where locals live, breathe, and preserve their heritage. ✨\n\nWhen planning your visit, keep in mind that the village is open from 10:00 AM to 5:00 PM, so be sure to explore during those hours! Just remember, from 5:00 PM to 10:00 AM the next day, access to restricted areas is off-limits. 🗺️ You can find it at 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul. I can\'t wait for you to wander through its picturesque alleyways and soak in the serene atmosphere! 🏯 If you have any more questions or need specifics, checking the official website or contacting the venue is a great idea! Enjoy your adventure!', '2025-11-19 08:55:42'),
	(1021, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', 'Absolutely! 🌟 The Hangang River Bus is a delightful way to explore the stunning scenery along the Han River while enjoying a unique perspective of Seoul. 🚤 With over 68 trips daily on weekdays and 48 on weekends, you can hop on and off to experience the vibrant riverside parks, iconic bridges, and breathtaking city views. \n\nWhat makes this attraction truly special is its express routes during peak commuting hours, which allows you to enjoy a scenic ride while avoiding the city\'s busy traffic! 🏙️ You can find the Hangang River Bus at Jamsil Pier in Songpa-gu, conveniently located for easy access. Just remember, it\'s open from 6:30 AM to 10:30 PM on weekdays and from 9:30 AM to 10:30 PM on weekends. Don\'t miss this fantastic opportunity to see Seoul from a whole new angle! 🌊✨ If you have more questions or need specific details, I recommend checking their official website or giving them a call. Enjoy your adventure! 🗺️🌸', '2025-11-19 08:55:56'),
	(1022, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Absolutely! 🌟 N Seoul Tower at night is a magical experience you won\'t want to miss! Perched high on Namsan Mountain, this iconic landmark offers stunning panoramic views of the sparkling city below, especially as the sun sets and the lights twinkle on. ✨ \n\nOne of the highlights is the "locks of love" tradition, where couples can fasten their love locks to the railings, making it a romantic spot! 💖 The tower is open from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM, so you have plenty of time to soak in the breathtaking sights. It\'s located at 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul. For more details, check out their official website! 🗺️🏯 Get ready for an unforgettable evening!', '2025-11-19 09:01:01'),
	(1023, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', '🌊🚤 Welcome aboard the Hangang River Bus, one of the most delightful ways to explore the heart of Seoul! This scenic boat ride offers stunning views of the city skyline and the beautiful Han River, making it a perfect choice for both relaxation and sightseeing. What makes it truly special is the chance to see iconic landmarks from a unique perspective while enjoying the gentle breeze on the water! 🌆✨\n\nYou can hop on at Jamsil Pier in Songpa-gu, conveniently located at 05500 1-2 Jamsil-dong. The bus operates weekdays from 6:30 AM to 10:30 PM with up to 68 trips daily, and weekends from 9:30 AM to 10:30 PM with 48 trips. Don’t forget to check out the express routes during weekday mornings and evenings for a quick commute! 🕐🎟️ \n\nFor the latest schedules and any updates, I recommend visiting their official website or contacting the venue directly. Get ready for an unforgettable adventure on the Han River! 🥳🗺️', '2025-11-19 09:01:12'),
	(1024, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ N Seoul Tower at Night - Experience breathtaking panoramic views of Seoul illuminated by vibrant city lights!\n\n✨ What makes it special:  \nN Seoul Tower, standing proudly on Namsan Mountain, is not only a landmark but also a symbol of love, with couples fastening "locks of love" to its railings. As night falls, the tower transforms into a mesmerizing beacon, offering stunning views of the sprawling city below. It has also been featured in numerous Korean dramas, making it a popular spot for fans and tourists alike.\n\n📍 Visit information:  \n• Location: 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n• Hours: 10:00 AM - 10:30 PM  \n• Best time to visit: Aim for sunset to catch the city transitioning from day to night!\n\n💡 Insider tip:  \nConsider taking the cable car up to the tower for a scenic ride, and don’t forget your camera to capture the stunning night views! 🗺️✨', '2025-11-19 09:10:59'),
	(1025, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ N Seoul Tower at Night - Experience breathtaking panoramic views of Seoul illuminated by the city lights!\n\n✨ What makes it special:  \nN Seoul Tower is an iconic landmark that not only offers stunning views but also serves as a romantic spot for couples with its famous locks of love tradition. The tower has appeared in numerous Korean dramas, making it a must-visit for fans of K-drama. At night, the city transforms into a sparkling wonderland, enhancing the beauty of the skyline.\n\n📍 Visit information:  \n• Location: 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n• Hours: 10:00 AM - 10:30 PM  \n• Best time to visit: Aim for sunset to enjoy both daylight and nighttime views!\n\n💡 Insider tip:  \nDon’t forget to bring a padlock to join the love lock tradition! You can find a spot on the railings with a romantic view, making for a perfect photo opportunity. 🗝️❤️', '2025-11-19 09:12:17'),
	(1026, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Cathedral', 'Myeongdong Cathedral is a stunning gem in the heart of Seoul! 🏯 As the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea and the very first Gothic building here, it holds a special place in the country\'s history. You can pay your respects in the small sanctuary on the basement floor, where the remains of martyrs are enshrined. Plus, don’t miss out on the cultural festival held every May! 🌸 \n\nLocated at 74 Myeongdong-gil in Jung-gu, the cathedral is easily accessible and surrounded by vibrant shopping and dining options. It’s a perfect spot to soak in both culture and the lively atmosphere of Myeongdong. Make sure to check the opening hours before your visit, and for any detailed questions, the official website is a great resource! ✨🗺️ Enjoy your visit!', '2025-11-19 09:18:21'),
	(1027, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Absolutely! 🌟 N Seoul Tower at night is a must-visit gem that lights up the Seoul skyline, offering breathtaking panoramic views that will leave you in awe. 🏯 As you ascend to the observatory, you’ll not only witness the shimmering city lights but also get a chance to attach a "lock of love" to the iconic railings, creating a perfect memory with your loved ones. ❤️ \n\nLocated at 105, Namsangongwon-gil in Yongsan-gu, the tower is open from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM, making it a fantastic evening destination. Don’t miss out on this enchanting experience! For more details, feel free to check their official website. 🌌✨', '2025-11-19 10:07:22'),
	(1028, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Cathedral', 'Absolutely! Myeongdong Cathedral is a stunning piece of history and architecture right in the heart of Seoul. 🏯 As the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea and the first Gothic-style building, this cathedral is not just a spiritual haven but also a testament to Korea\'s rich cultural heritage, designated as Historic site No. 285. 🌸 \n\nYou can visit the cathedral any day, and it\'s located at 100-022 74, Myeongdong-gil, Jung-gu. Be sure to check out the small sanctuary in the basement where the remains of martyrs are enshrined, and if you\'re there in May, don\'t miss the vibrant cultural festival! ✨ It’s a peaceful retreat amidst the bustling streets of Myeongdong, perfect for a moment of reflection or simply to admire the beautiful architecture. 🗺️ If you need more details, feel free to check their official website or contact them directly! Enjoy your visit! 😊', '2025-11-19 10:07:34'),
	(1029, 3, NULL, 'hello give me tips for korean travel', 'Hello there! 🌟 Here are some tips to help you navigate Seoul with ease and confidence:\n\n1. **Transportation**: Get yourself a T-money card! It\'s a rechargeable card that you can use on subways, buses, and even some convenience stores. Just tap it on the card reader when entering and exiting. The subway system is efficient and has English signs, making it easy to get around. 🚇\n\n2. **Budget**: Seoul can be affordable if you eat at local markets and try street food. Don’t miss out on exploring places like Gwangjang Market for delicious banchan (side dishes) and tteokbokki (spicy rice cakes)! 🍲\n\n3. **Local Customs**: When dining, it\'s customary to wait for the eldest person to start eating first. Also, remember to say "jal meokk겠습니다" (I will eat well) before meals and "jal meogeotseumnida" (I ate well) after! These small gestures show respect and appreciation. 🙏✨\n\nFeel free to ask more questions as you plan your adventure! Have an amazing time in Seoul! 🎉', '2025-11-19 10:08:15'),
	(1030, 3, NULL, 'hello give me tips for korean travel', 'Hello! I\'m so excited to help you plan your Korean adventure! ✈️ To start, consider getting a T-money card for easy transportation around Seoul. You can purchase it at convenience stores or subway stations, and it works for subways, buses, and even some taxis. Just tap it on the card readers, and you’re good to go! 🚆\n\nWhen it comes to budget, street food is a delicious and affordable way to experience local cuisine—don’t miss out on tteokbokki (spicy rice cakes) or hotteok (sweet pancakes)! As for local customs, remember to bow slightly when greeting someone and always remove your shoes when entering someone\'s home. 🤝\n\nAbove all, take your time to soak in the vibrant culture, and don’t hesitate to ask for help if you\'re unsure about anything. Enjoy your trip! 🌟', '2025-11-19 10:11:04'),
	(1031, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', 'Absolutely! 🌟 N Seoul Tower at night is truly a magical experience that you won\'t want to miss! Standing tall on Namsan Mountain, this iconic landmark offers breathtaking panoramic views of Seoul illuminated by city lights, creating a romantic and enchanting atmosphere. 💖 \n\nAs you visit, don’t forget to check out the famous "locks of love" – a beautiful tradition where couples secure their love locks to the railings! 🗝️ The tower is open from 10:00 AM to 10:30 PM, so plan your visit to catch the sunset and watch the city come alive after dark. You can find it at 105 Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul. For more details, feel free to check the official website! Get ready for a night filled with wonder! 🏯✨🌌', '2025-11-19 10:18:38'),
	(1032, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Cathedral', 'Absolutely! Myeongdong Cathedral, located at 74 Myeongdong-gil in Jung-gu, is a stunning piece of history and architecture, being the very first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea and the first Gothic structure in the country! 🏯✨ Its beautiful design and serene atmosphere make it a must-visit, especially since you can pay your respects in the small sanctuary that houses the remains of martyrs. \n\nDon\'t miss the cultural festival held every May, which adds a vibrant touch to this historic site! 🌸 The cathedral is open for visitors, and while specific hours can vary, it\'s generally accessible throughout the day. So, take a leisurely stroll through Myeongdong and immerse yourself in the rich history of this iconic landmark! 🗺️ For the latest info, you might want to check their official website or contact them directly. Enjoy your visit!', '2025-11-19 10:18:46'),
	(1033, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '🏛️ **Bukchon Hanok Village** - A charming glimpse into Seoul\'s 600-year-old history, where traditional hanok homes stand side by side.\n\n✨ **What makes it special:**\nBukchon Hanok Village is not just a tourist attraction; it’s a vibrant residential area that showcases the architectural beauty of traditional Korean homes. Nestled between Gyeongbokgung Palace and Changdeokgung Palace, the village offers a unique opportunity to experience authentic Korean culture amidst its narrow alleyways and picturesque scenery.\n\n📍 **Visit information:**\n• **Location:** 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n• **Hours:** 10:00 AM – 5:00 PM (Please note: restricted hours from 5:00 PM to 10:00 AM the following day when access is prohibited.)  \n• **Best time to visit:** Early morning or late afternoon for fewer crowds and beautiful lighting for photos.\n\n💡 **Insider tip:**\nTake a leisurely stroll through Gaehoe-dong, where you’ll find the most concentrated area of hanok, perfect for immersing yourself in the village’s tranquil atmosphere and snapping memorable photos! 📸🌸', '2025-11-19 10:24:48'),
	(1034, 6, NULL, 'Is Namsan Tower really worth visiting, or is it just a tourist trap?', '🏛️ **Namsan Seoul Tower: A Must-Visit Icon!**\n\nNamsan Seoul Tower offers a stunning 360-degree view of the city from 480 meters above sea level. It’s not just a tower; it’s a romantic landmark that attracts both locals and tourists alike.\n\n📍 **Location & Hours**\n\nAddress: 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul, Korea\n\nHours: Weekdays 10:00-22:30, Weekends 10:00-23:00  \n*Last entry 30 minutes before close  \n\n💡 **Helpful Tip**\n\nConsider visiting during sunset for a breathtaking view as the city lights up!', '2025-11-19 10:25:19'),
	(1035, 6, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ **N Seoul Tower at Night** - Experience the magic of Seoul from one of its most iconic landmarks! \n\nThe night views from N Seoul Tower are simply breathtaking, offering a stunning panorama of the city lights. It\'s a popular spot for romantic moments and has appeared in various Korean dramas. \n\n📍 **Location:** 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ **Hours:** 10:00 AM - 10:30 PM  \n\n💡 **Tip:** Don’t forget to check out the locks of love on the railings for a unique photo opportunity!', '2025-11-19 10:25:33'),
	(1036, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nAt N Seoul Tower, visitors can enjoy stunning panoramic views of the city skyline, especially enchanting at night when Seoul sparkles with lights. The tower features various facilities, including restaurants and cafes, where you can relax and soak in the atmosphere. Admission fees may vary, so be sure to check ahead for the latest rates and any special packages available.\n\nHistorically, N Seoul Tower was established in 1969 as a communication tower, but it has since become a cultural icon symbolizing love and romance. One of its most charming attractions is the "locks of love," where couples attach padlocks to the tower\'s railings as a pledge of their everlasting affection. Locals adore the tower not just for its breathtaking views but also for the romantic vibe it exudes, making it a popular spot for dates and proposals.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience the magic of N Seoul Tower at night—it\'s a must-visit that will leave you with unforgettable memories!', '2025-11-19 13:18:03'),
	(1037, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', '📍 **Hangang River Bus**  \n🏛️ 05500 1-2 Jamsil-dong area, Jamsil Pier, Songpa-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Weekdays (68 trips daily) 6:30 AM-10:30 PM / Weekends (48 trips daily) 9:30 AM-10:30 PM  \nExpress route weekdays 16 trips daily *Weekday commute (6:30 AM-9:00 AM), after work (6:00 PM-8:30 PM)  \n\nThe Hangang River Bus offers a unique way to explore the beautiful Han River and its picturesque surroundings. You can enjoy stunning views of the city skyline, parks, and bridges from the comfort of the bus. With affordable fares and accessible facilities, it’s a convenient option for both tourists and locals alike.  \n\nHistorically, the Han River has been a vital part of Seoul\'s development, serving as a trade route and a source of inspiration for countless artists and poets. The riverbanks are dotted with cultural landmarks and recreational spaces, making it a beloved gathering spot for residents who enjoy picnicking, cycling, and outdoor activities.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience the vibrant atmosphere of the Han', '2025-11-19 13:41:28'),
	(1038, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '📍 **Bukchon Hanok Village**  \n🏛️ 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00 ~ 17:00 (Restricted Hours: 17:00 ~ 10:00 the following day; visitors are prohibited from entering restricted areas during these hours)  \n(The Hanok Village is a residential space for local citizens before it is a tourist attraction.)  \n\nExplore the charming streets of Bukchon Hanok Village, where you can admire over 600 traditional hanok houses and immerse yourself in the atmosphere of old Seoul. While there is no admission fee, be respectful of the residents, as this is a living community. Facilities include small cafes and shops where you can enjoy local snacks and souvenirs, and the area is generally accessible, though some streets may be steep.  \n\nBukchon Hanok Village has a rich history, nestled between Gyeongbokgung and Changdeokgung Palaces, and showcases the architectural beauty of the Joseon Dynasty. Locals cherish this neighborhood not only for its aesthetic charm but also as a reminder of their cultural heritage, making it a beloved part of their daily lives. Many stories of the past linger in these alleys', '2025-11-19 13:47:59'),
	(1039, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', '📍 **Gyeongbokgung Palace**  \n🏛️ 03045 161, Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ January & February: 09:00 - 17:00  \nMarch - May: 09:00 - 18:00  \nJune - August: 09:00 - 18:30  \nSeptember & October: 09:00 - 18:00  \nNovember & December: 09:00 - 17:00  \n*Last entry one hour before closing*  \n\nAt Gyeongbokgung Palace, visitors can explore stunning architecture, beautiful gardens, and the National Palace Museum of Korea. Admission fees are very reasonable, and the palace is equipped with facilities like restrooms and guided tours for a more enriching experience. It’s also wheelchair accessible, making it easy for everyone to enjoy the grandeur of this historical site.  \n\nBuilt in 1395, Gyeongbokgung Palace served as the main royal palace of the Joseon Dynasty and is a symbol of Korea’s rich history. Locals cherish the palace not just for its beauty but also for the changing of the guard ceremony that showcases traditional Korean culture. The palace grounds are steeped in stories of', '2025-11-19 14:02:37'),
	(1040, 3, NULL, 'hello', 'Hello there! 👋 \n\nI\'m excited to help you plan your trip to Seoul! \n\nWhat do you have in mind? Are you looking for sightseeing, food recommendations, cultural experiences, or something else?', '2025-11-19 14:02:44'),
	(1041, 3, NULL, 'recommend couple love place', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 14:02:59'),
	(1042, 3, NULL, 'i\'m visiting korea for the first time  i"ll stay 5 days in seoul can you help me plan?', '🎬 **In front of Hyoryeong Building**  \n📍 6-minute walk from Exit 5 of Gwanghwamun Station, 32, Mugyo-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 여행을 대신해 드립니다  \n\nTo reach the Hyoryeong Building, simply exit Gwanghwamun Station from Exit 5 and enjoy a pleasant 6-minute walk. This area is bustling with life, and there are no specific opening hours as it’s an outdoor location. You can explore the surrounding restaurants and cafes, perfect for a leisurely meal or coffee break while soaking in the vibrant city atmosphere.  \n\nIn "여행을 대신해 드립니다," the front of the Hyoryeong Building serves as a backdrop for pivotal moments, showcasing the characters\' interactions and emotional journeys. This location was chosen for its lively urban setting, reflecting the dynamic nature of the city and enhancing the storytelling in the drama.  \n\nFor K-Drama fans, visiting this iconic spot allows you to step into the world of your favorite characters and capture some memorable photos that will make your trip unforgettable!', '2025-11-19 14:04:32'),
	(1043, 3, NULL, 'i can\'t eat spicy food recommend restaurant 1 place', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997  서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion rice cakes (떡), specifically soft injeolmi and angba-tteok with red bean paste and butter  \n\n정애맛담 offers a delightful selection of traditional Korean rice cakes with a modern twist. The prices are quite reasonable, typically ranging from 3,000 to 5,000 KRW per item. The shop is usually open from 10 AM to 8 PM, making it a convenient stop for both lunch and dessert. You can order directly at the counter or take some treats to go!  \n\nLocals love 정애맛담 for its unique take on classic rice cakes, which are often enjoyed during celebrations and special occasions in Korean culture. The cozy atmosphere and the artistic presentation of the dishes make it a perfect spot to enjoy a sweet treat while experiencing a piece of Korean culinary tradition.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to indulge in these delightful rice cakes that offer a taste of Korea\'s rich food heritage!', '2025-11-19 14:05:24'),
	(1044, 3, NULL, 'i like  eat spicy food recommend restaurant 1 place', '🍽️ **피맛골**  \n📍 03155 서울 종로구 종로3길 17  \n🍜 Korean street food, with a focus on spicy dishes like tteokbokki (spicy rice cakes) and kimchi jjigae (kimchi stew).\n\nAt 피맛골, you\'ll find a variety of delicious spicy options, perfect for those who love bold flavors. Prices are generally affordable, with dishes ranging from 5,000 to 15,000 KRW. The street is bustling with vendors, and you can either order at the counter or enjoy your meal at nearby tables.\n\nThis vibrant alleyway is steeped in history, where locals gather to enjoy hearty meals and socialize. The cultural significance of 피맛골 dates back to the Joseon Dynasty, making it a cherished spot for both residents and tourists. The lively atmosphere and the aroma of sizzling spices create a unique dining experience, reflecting the essence of Korean food traditions.\n\nDon\'t miss out on the chance to dive into the spicy delights of 피맛골—your taste buds will thank you!', '2025-11-19 14:05:41'),
	(1045, 3, NULL, 'can you create  3 - day itinearay whih travel times included?', 'Absolutely! Here’s a fun and engaging 3-day itinerary for your trip to Seoul, complete with travel times. \n\n---\n\n**Day 1: Historical Seoul**\n\n**Morning:**  \n- **Gyeongbokgung Palace**  \n  Start your day at Gyeongbokgung Palace (9:00 AM).  \n  *Travel Time:* 30 mins from central Seoul.  \n  Don\'t miss the changing of the guard ceremony at 10:00 AM!\n\n**Afternoon:**  \n- **Bukchon Hanok Village**  \n  Walk to Bukchon Hanok Village (15 mins on foot).  \n  Explore traditional Korean houses and enjoy the charming streets.  \n  *Lunch at a local café* to recharge.\n\n- **Insadong**  \n  Head to Insadong (15 mins on foot) for art galleries and souvenir shops.  \n  Try some traditional tea at a teahouse!\n\n**Evening:**  \n- **Cheonggyecheon Stream**  \n  Stroll along Cheonggyecheon Stream (20 mins by subway).  \n  Enjoy the beautiful lights in the evening.  \n\n- **Dinner in Myeongdong**  \n  End the day in Myeongdong (15 mins by subway) for', '2025-11-19 14:06:44'),
	(1046, 3, NULL, 'how do i get T-money card? Is Hongdae safe at night?', '🎬 **Lotteria Hongdae Branch**  \n📍 2-minute walk from Exit 1 of Hongik University Station, 141 Yanghwa-ro, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n🎭 Featured in: 우리들의 초콜릿 순간  \n\nTo get a T-money card, you can purchase one at convenience stores such as GS25, CU, or 7-Eleven, which are widely available in Seoul. The card is convenient for using public transportation, and you can easily top it up at these same stores. Hongdae is generally safe at night, with plenty of people around and a vibrant atmosphere, making it a great area for evening strolls or late-night snacks.  \n\nIn "Our Chocolate Moment," Lotteria Hongdae serves as a key backdrop for heartwarming scenes, where characters share intimate conversations over delicious food. The café\'s cozy ambiance and large windows filtering in natural light beautifully complement the romantic and nostalgic themes of the drama, making it an ideal setting for pivotal moments.  \n\nIf you\'re a K-Drama fan, visiting Lotteria Hongdae is a must to relive those sweet moments from the show while enjoying a delightful meal!', '2025-11-19 14:08:11'),
	(1047, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nAt N Seoul Tower, you can enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of the city, especially stunning at night when Seoul sparkles with lights. The tower features an observatory, cafes, and gift shops, making it a perfect spot to relax and soak in the atmosphere. Admission fees vary, so it\'s best to check the official website for the latest information, and the tower is accessible for visitors with disabilities.  \n\nN Seoul Tower, completed in 1975, has become a cultural icon and a symbol of love for many couples who come to fasten locks of love on its railings. The tower has also appeared in numerous popular Korean dramas and films, adding to its allure among locals and tourists alike. It holds a special place in the hearts of Seoulites as a gathering spot and a place to create lasting memories.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to visit N Seoul Tower at night for an unforgettable experience that beautifully showcases the vibrant spirit of the city!', '2025-11-19 14:16:00'),
	(1048, 3, NULL, 'hello', '✨ Quick Insight  \nHello! It\'s great to hear from you. If you\'re interested in exploring Seoul, there\'s so much to see, from historical sites to modern attractions, and each neighborhood has its own unique charm.\n\n🧭 Next Step  \nAre you looking for recommendations on specific activities, places to eat, or cultural experiences? Let me know what interests you most!\n\n🤝 Invitation  \nFeel free to share any specific locations or themes you have in mind, and I can help you plan an amazing experience in Seoul!', '2025-11-19 14:16:08'),
	(1049, 3, NULL, 'I\'m interested in food', '✨ Quick Insight  \nSeoul is a food lover\'s paradise, offering a rich tapestry of flavors and cuisines ranging from traditional Korean dishes to modern fusion creations. Whether you\'re interested in street food, fine dining, or local markets, there\'s something to satisfy every palate.\n\n🧭 Next Step  \nTo help you explore the culinary scene, could you share what types of food you\'re most interested in? Are you looking for specific dishes, dining experiences, or perhaps popular food markets?\n\n🤝 Invitation  \nFeel free to mention any particular places or experiences you\'ve heard about, and I’d love to help you find more details or similar options!', '2025-11-19 14:16:59'),
	(1050, 3, NULL, ' I had a delicious Korean meal. Please recommend a good Korean restaurant.', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion 떡 (특히 말랑 인절미와 앙버떡)  \n\n정애맛담은 전통 한국 떡에 현대적인 감각을 더한 퓨전 떡집으로, 신선한 재료로 만든 다양한 떡을 제공합니다. 가격대는 일반적으로 5,000원에서 15,000원 사이이며, 테이크아웃과 매장에서의 식사가 모두 가능합니다. 운영 시간은 오전 10시부터 오후 8시까지입니다.  \n\n이곳은 한국의 전통 음식을 현대적으로 재해석하여 젊은 세대에게도 인기가 많습니다. 떡은 한국의 중요한 음식 문화 중 하나로, 특별한 날이나 명절에 자주 즐겨 먹는 음식입니다. 정애맛담의 아늑하고 따뜻한 분위기에서 친구나 가족과 함께 떡을 나누며 즐기는 시간이 특별한 경험이 될 것입니다.  \n\n한국의 전통 떡을 새로운 방식으로 경험해 보세요!', '2025-11-19 14:18:20'),
	(1051, 3, NULL, 'And please recommend a celebrity restaurant', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion Tteok (Korean Rice Cake)\n\n정애맛담 offers a delightful array of modernized traditional Korean rice cakes, including chewy injeolmi coated in powder and the unique angba tteok, which features red bean paste and butter wrapped in soft, steamed rice cake. Prices are reasonable, typically ranging from 3,000 to 7,000 KRW per piece. The shop is open daily from 10 AM to 8 PM, and you can order directly at the counter or take advantage of their takeout options.\n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its innovative approach to traditional tteok, making it a popular spot for both casual snacks and special occasions. The cozy atmosphere is perfect for enjoying these treats with friends or family, and the fusion style reflects the evolving nature of Korean culinary traditions. This place is a testament to how traditional foods can be reimagined while still honoring their roots.\n\nDon\'t miss out on the chance to experience these delicious fusion rice cakes that beautifully blend tradition with modern flavors!', '2025-11-19 14:18:49'),
	(1052, 3, NULL, ' Recommend me a restaurant that was featured on K-Pop Demon Hunters', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Korean traditional rice cakes (떡) with a modern twist, specializing in soft injeolmi and butter-filled angba-tteok.  \n\n정애맛담 offers a delightful variety of fusion rice cakes that blend traditional flavors with contemporary techniques. Prices are reasonable, typically ranging from 3,000 to 7,000 KRW per piece. The shop is usually open from 10 AM to 8 PM, and you can order directly at the counter or through their social media for takeout.  \n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its unique take on 떡, making it a beloved spot in the bustling 남성시장. The atmosphere is cozy and welcoming, reflecting a blend of traditional Korean culture and modern culinary artistry. Enjoying 떡 here is not just a meal; it\'s a celebration of Korea\'s rich food heritage.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to indulge in these delightful treats during your visit!', '2025-11-19 14:19:11'),
	(1053, 3, NULL, 'Recommend me a spicy food restaurant', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion Tteok (Korean Rice Cakes)\n\n정애맛담 offers a delightful twist on traditional Korean rice cakes, featuring items like soft injeolmi coated in various powders and the unique angba-tteok, which combines sweet red bean paste with butter, all wrapped in a light rice cake. Prices typically range from 3,000 to 6,000 KRW per item. The shop is open daily from 10 AM to 8 PM, and you can order directly at the counter or via their website for takeout.\n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its innovative approach to tteok, blending traditional flavors with modern sensibilities. The cozy atmosphere, nestled in the bustling Namseong Market, makes it a perfect spot for both locals and tourists to experience a slice of Korean culinary culture. Tteok has deep roots in Korean traditions, often served during celebrations and special occasions, making each bite a connection to the past.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to indulge in these unique rice cakes that showcase the best of both tradition and innovation!', '2025-11-19 14:19:35'),
	(1054, 3, NULL, 'Recommend me a good tteokbokki restaurant', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion Tteok (Korean rice cakes)\n\nAt 정애맛담, you can indulge in a delightful array of fusion tteok, including the chewy injeolmi coated in various powders and the unique angba-tteok, which features sweet red bean paste and butter encased in a soft rice cake. Prices typically range from 3,000 to 6,000 KRW per item. The restaurant is open daily from 10 AM to 8 PM, and you can order directly at the counter or through their online platform for takeout.\n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its innovative take on traditional tteok, blending age-old recipes with contemporary flavors that appeal to all generations. The cozy atmosphere, nestled within the bustling 남성시장, adds to the charm, making it a perfect spot to experience authentic Korean food culture while enjoying a modern twist on beloved classics. \n\nDon’t miss the chance to try their unique offerings that redefine what tteok can be!', '2025-11-19 14:19:50'),
	(1055, 3, NULL, '매운 음식 맛집 추천해줘', '🍽️ **우정낙지**  \n📍 03189  서울 종로구 삼일대로17길 46 (관철동, 신양빌딩) 2층  \n🍜 매운 낙지볶음  \n\n우정낙지에서는 감칠맛 나는 매운 낙지볶음을 주로 제공합니다. 가격대는 대체로 10,000원에서 20,000원 사이로, 가성비가 뛰어난 메뉴를 즐길 수 있습니다. 보통 저녁 시간대가 붐비므로, 예약을 하거나 일찍 가는 것을 추천합니다.  \n\n이곳은 매운 음식을 사랑하는 서울 사람들에게 꼭 가봐야 할 명소로 알려져 있습니다. 매운 낙지볶음은 식사뿐만 아니라 술안주로도 인기가 높으며, 친구나 가족과 함께 즐기기 좋은 분위기입니다. 한국에서는 매운 음식이 소통의 매개체로 여겨져, 함께 나누어 먹는 것이 중요합니다.  \n\n매운 맛을 즐기는 분이라면 꼭 한 번 방문해 보세요!', '2025-11-19 14:22:36'),
	(1056, 3, NULL, 'Recommend me a spicy food restaurant', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion rice cakes (떡) with a modern twist, featuring chewy injeolmi and red bean butter-filled angbottak.  \n\nAt 정애맛담, you can indulge in unique variations of traditional Korean rice cakes that blend classic flavors with contemporary styles. Prices range from 3,000 to 7,000 KRW per item, and the shop is typically open from 10 AM to 8 PM. You can order directly at the counter or take advantage of their takeaway service.  \n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its innovative approach to 떡, making it a favorite spot for both young and older generations. The cozy atmosphere reflects the warmth of Korean hospitality, and enjoying these delightful treats often becomes a cherished part of family gatherings and celebrations.  \n\nDon’t miss the chance to experience these delicious fusion rice cakes that are sure to tantalize your taste buds!', '2025-11-19 14:23:23'),
	(1057, 3, NULL, '양고기 맛집 추천해줘', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion rice cakes (떡) with a modern twist  \n\n정애맛담 specializes in traditional Korean rice cakes (떡), offering unique fusion variations such as soft injeolmi coated in powdered soybean flour and the savory angbaked with red bean paste and butter instead of bread. Prices are reasonable, typically ranging from 3,000 to 6,000 KRW per item. The shop is open daily from 10 AM to 8 PM, and you can order directly at the counter or through their online platform.  \n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its inventive approach to a beloved traditional snack, making it a popular spot for both young foodies and families. The cozy atmosphere reflects a blend of tradition and modernity, creating a warm space for enjoying these delightful treats. The fusion of flavors pays homage to Korea\'s rich culinary heritage while inviting new experiences.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to indulge in these creative rice cakes that celebrate the best of both worlds!', '2025-11-19 14:24:51'),
	(1058, 3, NULL, '양고기 음식점 추천해줘', '🍽️ **알라딘의양고기**  \n📍 05559 서울 송파구 백제고분로7길 42-16 (정빌딩)  \n🍜 [아랍식 양고기, 양꼬]\n\n이곳은 아랍식으로 양념된 양고기를 숯불에 구워 즐길 수 있는 레스토랑입니다. 가격대는 적당하며, 보통 20,000원에서 40,000원 사이의 메뉴가 있습니다. 운영 시간은 일반적으로 오후 5시부터 자정까지이며, 사전 예약을 추천합니다.\n\n알라딘의양고기는 아랍식 요리를 좋아하는 현지인들에게 특히 인기 있는 장소입니다. 이곳의 양고기는 숯불의 향과 함께 풍부한 양념이 어우러져 독특한 맛을 선사하며, 피타 빵에 싸서 먹는 방식은 여러 문화의 식사를 경험할 수 있는 기회를 제공합니다.\n\n양고기의 매력을 느껴보세요!', '2025-11-19 14:25:05'),
	(1059, 3, NULL, 'Recommend me a spicy food ', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion rice cakes (떡) with a modern twist, specializing in soft injeolmi and red bean butter-filled angbottak.\n\nAt 정애맛담, you can indulge in a variety of traditional Korean rice cakes that have been creatively reimagined. Prices typically range from 3,000 to 7,000 KRW per item. The shop is open daily from 10 AM to 7 PM, and you can easily order at the counter or take your treats to-go.\n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its unique blend of traditional and contemporary flavors, making it a perfect spot for both nostalgic tastes and modern culinary experiences. The cozy atmosphere reflects the charm of the traditional Korean market, where food is not just a meal but a celebration of culture and community.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience these delightful fusion rice cakes – they’re a treat for both the palate and the spirit!', '2025-11-19 14:25:27'),
	(1060, 3, NULL, 'Recommend me a korean beef', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 14:25:34'),
	(1061, 3, NULL, 'Hohojae Seoul', '✨ Quick Insight  \nHohojae is a traditional hanok (Korean house) located in the Bukchon Hanok Village area of Seoul, known for its beautiful architecture and serene atmosphere. It’s a great spot if you’re interested in experiencing traditional Korean culture and aesthetics.\n\n🧭 Next Step  \nAre you looking for accommodation options, cultural experiences nearby, or maybe some dining recommendations in that area? Let me know what specific information you need!\n\n🤝 Invitation  \nFeel free to share any particular interests or plans you have in mind, and I’d be happy to help you explore further!', '2025-11-19 14:25:48'),
	(1062, 3, NULL, 'recommend me a korean beef', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-19 14:59:20'),
	(1063, 3, NULL, 'Recommend me a korean beef', '🍽️ **[백년가게] 삼원가든**  \n📍 06023 서울 강남구 언주로 835 (삼원가든)  \n🍜 Traditional Korean BBQ, specializing in Galbi (beef ribs)  \n\n삼원가든은 신선하고 질 좋은 갈비를 제공하는 곳으로, 가격대는 보통 30,000원에서 50,000원 사이입니다. 매일 오전 11시부터 오후 10시까지 운영하며, 예약은 전화로 가능하니 미리 확인하는 것이 좋습니다.  \n\n이곳은 1976년부터 이어진 전통적인 갈빗집으로, 서울에서 가장 큰 식당 중 하나입니다. 현지인들은 신선한 재료와 정통 한식 요리를 즐기기 위해 자주 찾으며, 가족 단위로 방문하기 좋은 아늑한 분위기를 자랑합니다. 한국의 BBQ 문화는 함께 나누고 즐기는 것에 중점을 두고 있어, 이곳에서의 식사는 특별한 경험이 됩니다.  \n\n정통 한식의 매력을 느끼고 싶다면 꼭 방문해보세요!', '2025-11-19 15:48:02'),
	(1064, 3, NULL, 'Recommend random place top 10', '✨ Found 5 attractions that match your request. Check the cards below and ask me about any place for deeper tips!', '2025-11-19 15:48:23'),
