	(1066, 3, NULL, 'Recommend random attaraction top 10', '🍽️ **정애맛담**  \n📍 06997 서울 동작구 동작대로29나길 10  \n🍜 Fusion Tteok (Korean rice cakes)  \n\n정애맛담 specializes in innovative takes on traditional Korean tteok, offering delightful treats like soft injeolmi coated with powdered soybean and the unique angba-tteok, which combines sweet red bean paste and butter in a light rice cake. Prices typically range from 3,000 to 6,000 KRW per item. The shop usually opens from 10 AM to 8 PM, and ordering is simple—just walk in and choose from the beautifully displayed treats!\n\nLocals adore 정애맛담 for its creative fusion of traditional flavors with a modern twist, making it a popular spot for both young people and families. The atmosphere is warm and inviting, often filled with the enticing aroma of freshly made tteok, which plays a significant role in Korean celebrations and traditions. Enjoying these treats here not only satisfies your taste buds but also connects you to the rich heritage of Korean cuisine.\n\nDon\'t miss the chance to indulge in these delightful fusion rice cakes during your visit!', '2025-11-19 15:48:55'),
	(1067, 3, NULL, 'Recommend random attaraction top 10 places', '✨ Found 10 attractions that match your request. Check the cards below and ask me about any place for deeper tips!', '2025-11-19 15:49:05'),
	(1068, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '📍 **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n🏛️ 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00-22:30  \n\nAt N Seoul Tower, you can enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of Seoul illuminated at night, making it a perfect spot for photography and romantic outings. The observatory offers various facilities, including a café and gift shop, and is accessible for visitors with disabilities. Admission fees may vary, so it\'s a good idea to check ahead for any special promotions or packages.  \n\nN Seoul Tower has a rich history, originally built in 1969 as a communication tower, and it has become a beloved symbol of the city. The tradition of attaching "locks of love" to the railings is a popular activity among couples, symbolizing their everlasting bond. Locals adore the tower not only for its stunning views but also for the vibrant atmosphere and the cultural events often held in the surrounding Namsan Park.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience the magic of Seoul from the heights of N Seoul Tower at night—it\'s an unforgettable adventure!', '2025-11-19 15:53:46'),
	(1069, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '📍 **Bukchon Hanok Village**  \n🏛️ 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ 10:00 ~ 17:00 (Restricted Hours: 17:00 ~ 10:00 the following day; visitors are prohibited from entering restricted areas during these hours)  \n(The Hanok Village is a residential space for local citizens before it is a tourist attraction.)  \n\nExplore the charming streets of Bukchon, where you can admire hundreds of traditional hanok and experience the serene atmosphere of this historic village. While there is no admission fee, be mindful of the local residents and enjoy the various cultural workshops and galleries that allow you to dive deeper into traditional Korean arts. The village is accessible by public transportation, making it easy to visit.\n\nBukchon Hanok Village is a testament to Seoul\'s rich history, showcasing over 600 years of architectural heritage nestled between two grand palaces. Unlike other tourist-centric villages, Bukchon is a living community, where locals cherish their heritage and share their stories, creating a unique blend of history and daily life. The picturesque Gaehoe-dong area, in particular, offers a glimpse into the past, making it a favorite among', '2025-11-19 15:53:57'),
	(1070, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Hangang River Bus', '📍 **Hangang River Bus**  \n🏛️ 05500 1-2 Jamsil-dong area, Jamsil Pier, Songpa-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Weekdays (68 trips daily) 6:30 AM-10:30 PM / Weekends (48 trips daily) 9:30 AM-10:30 PM  \nExpress route weekdays 16 trips daily *Weekday commute (6:30 AM-9:00 AM), after work (6:00 PM-8:30 PM)  \n\nThe Hangang River Bus offers a unique way to explore the stunning Han River, providing picturesque views of Seoul\'s skyline and parks along the banks. Whether you’re commuting or enjoying a leisurely ride, this bus service is both convenient and affordable, with no admission fees required. Facilities on board ensure a comfortable journey, and the service is accessible for everyone.  \n\nHistorically, the Han River has been a vital part of Seoul\'s development, serving as a trade route and a recreational area for locals. Today, it\'s a cultural hub, with many festivals and events taking place along its shores. The Hangang River Bus allows visitors to connect with this vibrant history while enjoying the natural beauty that the river', '2025-11-19 15:54:06'),
	(1071, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about COEX', '📍 **COEX**  \n🏛️ 06164 513, Yeongdeung-daero, Gangnam-gu, Seoul (COEX)  \n⏰ Open year-round with varying hours depending on events and exhibitions.  \n\nAt COEX, you can explore a vast array of exhibitions and conferences that focus on food, culture, arts, and various global issues. Admission fees may vary depending on specific events, but many exhibitions are free to enter. The center is equipped with excellent facilities, including restaurants, cafes, and shops, making it easily accessible for everyone.  \n\nCOEX has a rich cultural significance as it serves as a hub for international conferences and summits, helping to position Seoul as a global city. The venue is also home to the famous COEX Mall and Starfield Library, making it a beloved spot for locals and tourists alike. Its modern architecture and vibrant atmosphere create a unique blend of business and leisure, reflecting Seoul\'s dynamic spirit.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to immerse yourself in the exciting energy of COEX during your visit to Seoul!', '2025-11-19 15:54:18'),
	(1072, 3, NULL, 'Introduce Gyeongbokgung Palace', '📍 **Gyeongbokgung Palace**  \n🏛️ 03045 161, Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ January & February: 09:00 - 17:00  \nMarch - May: 09:00 - 18:00  \nJune - August: 09:00 - 18:30  \nSeptember & October: 09:00 - 18:00  \nNovember & December: 09:00 - 17:00  \n*Last entry one hour before closing*  \n\nAt Gyeongbokgung Palace, you can explore the stunning architecture and beautiful gardens, as well as witness the ceremonial changing of the guard. Admission fees are very reasonable, and you can enjoy various facilities, including guided tours and visitor centers. The palace is accessible for all visitors, making it easy to navigate and appreciate its grandeur.\n\nAs the first and largest of the royal palaces built during the Joseon Dynasty in 1395, Gyeongbokgung symbolizes the heart of Korea\'s history and culture. Locals cherish this landmark not only for its breathtaking beauty but also for the rich stories and traditions that it embodies, including tales of past kings and their legacies. \n\nDon\'t', '2025-11-19 15:54:31'),
	(1073, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Myeongdong Cathedral', '📍 **Myeongdong Cathedral**  \n🏛️ 100-022 74, Myeongdong-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Open daily; free admission  \n\nAt Myeongdong Cathedral, visitors can explore the stunning Gothic architecture and enjoy the serene atmosphere. The basement sanctuary houses the remains of martyrs, allowing for a moment of reflection. Facilities include restrooms and a small gift shop, making it accessible for everyone.  \n\nAs the first Roman Catholic parish church in Korea, Myeongdong Cathedral holds great historical significance, having been constructed between 1892 and 1898. It is designated as Historic Site No. 285 and serves as a cultural hub, hosting a vibrant festival every May. Locals love it not only for its architectural beauty but also for its role in the spiritual and social life of the community.  \n\nDon\'t miss the chance to experience the peaceful ambiance and rich history of this iconic landmark!', '2025-11-19 15:54:39'),
