	(1079, 3, NULL, 'compare  Jeongdong-gil vs  Samcheongdong', '**PRACTICAL COMPARISON:**  \nJeongdong-gil is located near Deoksugung Palace, making it easily accessible by subway and bus, with various cultural sites nearby. It generally offers a peaceful walking experience with no entrance fees, while Samcheongdong is a vibrant neighborhood near Gyeongbokgung Palace, featuring a mix of art galleries, cafes, and shops, but it can be more crowded, especially on weekends. Both areas are free to explore, making them budget-friendly options for travelers.\n\n**EXPERIENCE COMPARISON:**  \nJeongdong-gil boasts a serene atmosphere lined with beautiful trees and historical buildings, perfect for a leisurely stroll and appreciating traditional architecture. In contrast, Samcheongdong is known for its eclectic blend of modern and traditional aesthetics, vibrant street life, and cultural experiences, offering a more dynamic vibe that attracts art enthusiasts and foodies alike. Each location has its unique charm, with Jeongdong-gil emphasizing tranquility and history, while Samcheongdong buzzes with creativity and energy.\n\n**RECOMMENDATION:**  \nIf you’re seeking a calm and reflective experience, I recommend starting your journey at Jeongdong-gil for its picturesque surroundings and historical significance. However, if you’re in the mood for a lively atmosphere filled with art, cafes, and shops, then Samcheongdong is the place to be. Both areas offer unique insights into Seoul’s culture, but your choice will depend on whether you', '2025-11-19 16:54:43'),
	(1080, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ **Discover N Seoul Tower at Night!**\n\nN Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s iconic landmarks, offering stunning panoramic views of the city. The night vistas are particularly enchanting, making it a must-visit spot for both locals and tourists. \n\n📍 **Location:** 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** 10:00 AM - 10:30 PM  \n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Don\'t forget to check out the locks of love on the iron railings for a romantic touch to your visit!', '2025-11-20 00:44:50'),
	(1081, 3, NULL, 'Tell me about Bukchon', '🏛️ Discover the Charm of Bukchon Hanok Village!  \n\nBukchon Hanok Village is a captivating glimpse into 600 years of Seoul\'s history. This unique village is a blend of traditional architecture and local life, making it a true gem for visitors.  \n\n📍 Address: 03059 37, Gyedong-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ Hours: 10:00 AM - 5:00 PM (Restricted hours from 5:00 PM to 10:00 AM; no entry allowed during this time)  \n\n💡 Helpful Tip: For the best experience, visit Gaehoe-dong where you can fully immerse yourself in the authentic hanok atmosphere!', '2025-11-20 00:44:58'),
	(1082, 3, NULL, 'hello', '🏛️ Welcome to the Seoul Science Museum! \n\nThis museum is a treasure trove of interactive exhibits that spark curiosity and ignite a passion for science. It\'s a perfect destination for families and anyone fascinated by the wonders of the natural world. \n\n📍 Address: 01792 160, Hangeulbiseok-ro, Nowon-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ Hours: Tue-Fri 09:30-17:30 KST  \n\n💡 Tip: Arrive early to enjoy the hands-on activities without the crowds!', '2025-11-20 00:45:42'),
	(1083, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ **N Seoul Tower at Night**  \n\nN Seoul Tower is a must-visit landmark in Seoul, especially when the city lights up after dark. The panoramic night views from the observatory are truly breathtaking, making it a romantic spot for couples.  \n\n📍 **Location**: 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours**: 10:00 AM - 10:30 PM  \n\n💡 **Tip**: Don’t forget to check out the locks of love on the iron railings for a memorable photo opportunity!  ', '2025-11-20 00:45:54'),
	(1084, 3, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ **Discover the Magic of N Seoul Tower at Night!** \n\nN Seoul Tower is a must-visit landmark that offers breathtaking night views of the city. Its panoramic observatory provides a unique perspective of Seoul\'s sparkling skyline.\n\n📍 **Location:** 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** 10:00 AM - 10:30 PM\n\n💡 **Tip:** Don\'t forget to check out the locks of love along the iron railings for a romantic touch!', '2025-11-20 00:46:08'),
