	(1088, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Austria-Eden', '🌟 Welcome to Austria-Eden!\n\nAustria-Eden is a unique and enchanting destination that combines the beauty of nature with vibrant cultural experiences. It offers visitors a chance to immerse themselves in lush landscapes, artistic expressions, and a deep connection to the local community.\n\n🗓️ Dates and Location\n\nWhile specific dates may vary, Austria-Eden is typically celebrated throughout various seasons, showcasing the best of Austria’s natural beauty. Located in the heart of Austria, it’s easily accessible and perfect for both locals and tourists alike.\n\n🌼 Don\'t miss out on the chance to explore this magical place and experience the warmth of its culture!', '2025-11-20 00:47:34'),
	(1089, 3, NULL, 'tell me about KB Woojun Tower', '🏛️ **KB Woojun Tower - A Hidden Gem in the City!**\n\nThis tower stands out for its unique architectural design and stunning views, making it a perfect spot for both locals and tourists. It offers a serene escape while still being close to the vibrant city life.\n\n📍 **Location:** The tower is located at [insert address here].\n\n⏰ **Hours:** Open daily from 10:00 AM to 10:00 PM.\n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Visit during sunset for a breathtaking view of the city transitioning from day to night!', '2025-11-20 00:47:44'),
	(1090, 3, NULL, 'reccommend all place be completely taken in', '**폭싹 속았수다 - A Must-Visit for K-Drama Fans! 🎬💜**\n\nThis charming location on the east side of Hanyang Apartment E features stunning backdrops seen in "I Got Tricked." It\'s the perfect spot to relive iconic scenes and immerse yourself in the drama\'s atmosphere! \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 4-2 Yeouido-dong, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 9-minute walk from Exit 2 of Saetgang Station. \n\nFor the best photos, visit early in the morning or during golden hour for that dreamy light! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:50:59'),
	(1091, 3, NULL, 'reccommend all place be completely taken in', '**폭싹 속았수다 - A Must-Visit for K-Drama Lovers! 🎬💜** \n\nThis filming location of "I Got Tricked" is a hidden gem in the heart of Yeouido. With its beautiful greenery, it\'s the perfect backdrop for capturing your favorite drama moments!\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 4-2 Yeouido-dong, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 9-minute walk from Exit 2 of Saetgang Station!  \n\n \n\nFor the best photos, visit during golden hour for stunning lighting. Don\'t forget to capture those K-drama vibes! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:51:10'),
	(1092, 3, NULL, 'reccommend all places be completely taken in', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 00:51:14'),
	(1093, 3, NULL, 'tell me about All that jazz', '🌟 Let\'s Go to the Moon - a K-drama gem! \n\nAll That Jazz serves as the main filming location for this heartwarming series, bringing the emotional moments to life. The cozy atmosphere and live jazz performances make it a must-visit for fans. \n\nHow to get there:  \n\n• Address: 216, Itaewon-ro, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 6-minute walk from Exit 3 of Itaewon Station!  \n\n📸 For the best photos, visit during the evening when the lighting enhances the interior design. Capture those magical moments with friends or loved ones!  \n\nEnjoy your visit! 🎬💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:51:26'),
	(1094, 3, NULL, 'tell me about The east side of Hanyang Apartment E', '🎬 "폭싹 속았수다" is a must-visit for K-drama fans! \n\nThis charming location features iconic scenes that capture the essence of the drama, making it a perfect backdrop for your own photos. \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 4-2 Yeouido-dong, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 9-minute walk from Exit 2 of Saetgang Station! \n\n📺 For the best photos, visit during the golden hour when the light beautifully highlights the greenery! 💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:51:35'),
	(1095, 8, NULL, ' reccommend all places Let\'s carry Sunjae and run', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 00:51:37'),
	(1096, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Yeouido-dong-ro (Yeouido Middle School, High School)', '**폭싹 속았수다 - A K-drama lover\'s paradise! 🎬💜**\n\nThis location features iconic scenes from the drama, showcasing the unique charm of Yeouido-dong-ro. Fans can relive memorable moments while strolling past Yeouido Middle and High Schools.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 8-1 Yeouido-dong, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Easily reachable via public transportation, just hop on the subway to Yeouido Station!\n\nFor the best photos, visit early in the morning or late afternoon for that perfect lighting! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:51:45'),
	(1097, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Samil-daero 32nd-gil', '[Samil-daero 32nd-gil - A Hidden Gem in Seoul! 🌟]\n\nSamil-daero 32nd-gil offers a unique blend of history and tranquility, making it a peaceful escape from the city\'s hustle and bustle. Visitors can enjoy charming streets lined with beautiful architecture and a serene atmosphere.\n\n📍 Location: Samil-daero 32nd-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Hours: Open all day for leisurely strolls\n\n💡 Helpful Tip: Bring a camera to capture the stunning architecture and relaxing ambiance!', '2025-11-20 00:51:52'),
	(1098, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Changdeokgung 1-gil', '🏛️ Discover the Beauty of Changdeokgung Palace!\n\nChangdeokgung Palace is a UNESCO World Heritage Site, renowned for its stunning architecture and harmonious relationship with nature. Built in 1405, it embodies the essence of East Asian palace design.\n\n📍 Location:  \nChangdeokgung Palace, 03072 2-71, Waryong-dong, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ Hours:  \n• February - May: 09:00 - 18:00 (Last entry at 17:00)  \n• June - August: 09:00 - 18:30 (Last entry at 17:30)  \n• September - October: 09:00 - 18:00 (Last entry at 17:00)  \n• November - January: 09:00 - 17:30 (Last entry at 16:30)  \n\n💡 Helpful Tip:  \nDon\'t miss the Secret Garden tour, which offers a unique glimpse into the palace\'s serene landscapes!', '2025-11-20 00:51:55'),
	(1099, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Miwon Building', '🎬 Welcome to "대행사" (The Agency)! 📺💜 \n\nThe Miwon Building is a stunning backdrop for many memorable scenes in the drama. Visitors can stand where the characters did and soak in the breathtaking views of Seoul\'s skyline.  \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 70 International Financial Road, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 13-minute walk from Exit 5 of Yeouido Station!  \n\nFor the best photos, visit during golden hour when the city lights start to twinkle! ✨', '2025-11-20 00:52:04'),
	(1100, 3, NULL, 'tell me about In front of Hyoryeong Building', '**여행을 대신해 드립니다 - A Must-Visit for K-Drama Fans! 🎬💜**\n\nThis vibrant location in front of Hyoryeong Building is where some memorable scenes from the drama were filmed. You\'ll feel the energy and emotions of the characters as you walk through this lively city center.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 32, Mugyo-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 6-minute walk from Exit 5 of Gwanghwamun Station!  \n\n  \nFor the best photo opportunities, visit during the evening when the nightscape lights up the surroundings. Capture the magic of the drama and make unforgettable memories! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:52:13'),
	(1101, 3, NULL, 'tell me about In front of the main road tower building', '🎬✨ "이번 생도 잘 부탁해" is a must-visit spot for K-drama enthusiasts!\n\nThe front of the main road tower building features some iconic scenes from the drama. It\'s a vibrant spot where you can truly soak in the lively atmosphere of Seoul\'s city center. \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 223, Teheran-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n• Access: Just a 5-minute walk from Exit 8 of Yeoksam Station  \n\nFor the best photo opportunities, visit during the golden hour for that perfect lighting! 📺💜', '2025-11-20 00:52:40'),
	(1102, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Miwon Building', '🎬 Get ready, K-drama fans! "대행사" (The Agency) has some incredible scenes filmed at the Miwon Building! \n\nThis stunning location showcases the beautiful skyline of Seoul where the characters brought the drama to life. You can walk in their footsteps and feel the city\'s charm envelop you. \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 70 International Financial Road, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 13-minute walk from Exit 5 of Yeouido Station! \n\nFor the best photos, visit during sunset when the skyline is lit up beautifully. 📺💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:52:54'),
	(1103, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Bongwon Overpass', '🏛️ Discover the Bongwon Overpass!\n\nThe Bongwon Overpass is a unique structure that connects various parts of the city while providing stunning views of the surrounding area. It\'s a popular spot for both locals and tourists looking to experience Seoul from a different perspective.\n\n📍 Location: The Bongwon Overpass is situated near Bongwonsa Temple, in Seodaemun-gu, Seoul.\n\n⏰ Hours: The overpass is accessible at all times, making it convenient for visitors any day of the week.\n\n💡 Tip: Bring your camera to capture the beautiful skyline and enjoy a leisurely stroll for a refreshing city experience!', '2025-11-20 00:53:07'),
	(1104, 3, NULL, 'tell me about The State Room', '🏛️ Discover The State Room!\n\nThe State Room is a stunning space within the National Museum of Art at Deoksugung Palace. It showcases the unique blend of Korean and Western architectural styles, offering a glimpse into Korea\'s artistic heritage.\n\n📍 Location: 04519 99, Sejong-daero, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ Hours:  \n• Tuesdays, Thursdays, Fridays & Sundays: 10:00 - 19:00  \n• Wednesdays & Saturdays: 10:00 - 21:00  \n* Last entry is 1 hour before closing.  \n\n💡 Helpful Tip: Combine your visit to The State Room with a stroll through the palace gardens for a complete experience!', '2025-11-20 00:53:20'),
	(1105, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Seongsu Nak Nak Nak', '**Unknown Seoul - A Must-Visit Spot for K-Drama Fans! 🎬💜**\n\nSeongsu Nak Nak Nak is a chic and stylish location that captures the essence of modern Seoul. It’s not just a cafe; it’s a vibrant space where fans can relive their favorite moments from the drama!\n\nMany memorable scenes from "미지의 서울" were filmed here, making it a special pilgrimage for fans. The atmosphere is cozy and sophisticated, perfect for enjoying a relaxing time.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 48 Achasan-ro 17-gil, Seongdong-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 2-minute walk above Exit 4 of Seongsu Station!  \n\n \n\nFor the best photos, visit during golden hour for that perfect lighting! 📷✨', '2025-11-20 00:53:21'),
	(1106, 3, NULL, 'tell me about the bankruptcy of the brushstrokeser', '**Lies for No Use - A Must-Visit Spot! 🎬💜**\n\nThis charming cafe, known as the bankruptcy of the brushstrokeser, is a key filming location in the drama "Lies for No Use." It\'s perfect for fans who want to relive their favorite moments in a cozy and stylish setting. \n\nHow to get there: \n\n• Address: 837, Eonju-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 9-minute walk from Exit 3 of Apgujeong Station. \n\nFor the best experience, visit in the evening when the lights create a romantic ambiance—perfect for capturing those Instagram-worthy moments! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:53:34'),
	(1107, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Seongsan-ro 22-gil', '[Discover Seongsan-ro 22-gil! 🌟]\n\nSeongsan-ro 22-gil is a charming street that captures the essence of Seoul\'s vibrant culture. It offers a unique blend of local shops, cafes, and artistic vibes that make it perfect for leisurely exploration. \n\n📍 Address: Seongsan-ro 22-gil, Seoul  \n⏰ Hours: Varies by establishment \n\n💡 A helpful tip: Visit during the afternoon for a quieter experience and to enjoy the local atmosphere!', '2025-11-20 00:53:34'),
	(1108, 3, NULL, 'tell me about It\'s down', '🏛️ Discover Ground Seoul!\n\nGround Seoul is a versatile cultural space that spans 4958 square meters, featuring a unique underground layout that allows for stunning natural lighting. It seamlessly blends exhibitions, performances, events, and parties, positioning itself as a hub for artistic expression.\n\n📍 Address: 03145 26, Insadong 9-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ Hours: 11:00~18:00 (Vary per exhibition)  \n\n💡 Tip: Check their website for current exhibitions and events to make the most of your visit!', '2025-11-20 00:53:45'),
	(1109, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Sogang Bridge', '🏛️ **Discover Sogang Bridge!**\n\nSogang Bridge is a modern marvel that offers stunning views of the Han River. It connects the bustling areas of Mapo and Yeongdeungpo, making it a vital passage for both pedestrians and vehicles.\n\n📍 **Location:** Sogang Bridge, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** Open 24 hours\n\n💡 **Tip:** Visit during sunset for breathtaking views and great photo opportunities!', '2025-11-20 00:53:57'),
	(1110, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Umiok (Korean traditional song)', '🎬 Let\'s dive into "달까지 가자" (Let\'s Go to the Moon)! \n\nThis charming drama has some iconic scenes filmed at Umiok, where the atmosphere perfectly captures the essence of the story. Fans will love the cozy setting that adds to the drama\'s warmth and appeal. \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 230-27, Yulgok-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 10-minute walk from Exit 3 of Jongno 3-ga Station!\n\n  \n\n📸 Pro tip: Visit during off-peak hours to avoid long waits and capture the perfect shots of this beautiful location! Make unforgettable memories as you enjoy the delicious food while reminiscing about your favorite scenes! 💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:54:13'),
	(1111, 8, NULL, 'reccommend all places a one-stroke scandal', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 00:54:21'),
	(1112, 3, NULL, 'tell me about softie', '🏛️ **Comfort Women Memorial: A Touching Tribute**\n\nThe Comfort Women Memorial is a poignant space dedicated to the victims of wartime sexual slavery, emphasizing themes of human rights and peace. Opened in 2016, it centers around survivor testimonies and documentation of historical injustices.\n\n📍 **Location:** 04628 6, Toegye-ro 26ga-gil, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** Check local listings for current visiting hours.\n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Take time to read the testimonies displayed; they offer deep insights into the experiences of the survivors.', '2025-11-20 00:54:31'),
	(1113, 8, NULL, 'reccommend all places model texi 2', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 00:54:44'),
	(1114, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Parnas Tower', '🏛️ Parnas Tower: A Modern Marvel in Seoul!  \n\nParnas Tower is a striking skyscraper that offers a blend of business and leisure activities in the heart of the city. With its modern architecture and stunning views, it stands as a symbol of Seoul\'s rapid development.  \n\n📍 Location: 108, Teheran-ro 7-gil, Gangnam-gu, Seoul, Korea  \n\n⏰ Hours: Typically open 9:00 AM - 6:00 PM, but hours may vary by business.  \n\n💡 Helpful Tip: Don\'t miss the observation deck for breathtaking views of the city skyline!', '2025-11-20 00:54:47'),
	(1115, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Seho-Taylor', '🌟 **Discover Seho-Taylor!**\n\nSeho-Taylor is a vibrant art space that showcases a rich blend of contemporary and classic artistry. Its unique approach fosters creativity and supports both emerging and established artists.\n\n📍 **Location:** 06648 94, Banpo-daero, Seocho-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ **Hours:** 10:00 - 17:00 (KST)  \n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Check their schedule for special exhibitions and artist talks to enhance your visit!', '2025-11-20 00:54:57'),
	(1116, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Samseong-ri', '🏛️ Discover Samseyoung! \n\nThis charming spot offers a unique blend of culture and relaxation in the heart of Seoul. Its inviting atmosphere makes it perfect for both locals and tourists looking to unwind.\n\n📍 Location: 03003 2 Pyeongchang 44-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Hours: 11:00-18:00  \n\n💡 Helpful Tip: Consider visiting during the weekdays to enjoy a more peaceful experience!', '2025-11-20 00:55:04'),
	(1117, 3, NULL, ' reccommend all places One day, the life of a major', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 00:55:05'),
	(1118, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Bolt 1932', '🏛️ **Discover Bolt 1932!**\n\nThis unique spot combines history and innovation, showcasing the evolution of design and engineering over the decades. Its name pays homage to the year when groundbreaking advancements were made in various fields.\n\n📍 **Location:** 03087 86, Daehak-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** Please refer to the website for more details.\n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Check for any special exhibitions or events that might enhance your visit!', '2025-11-20 00:55:15'),
	(1119, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Seosun-ra-gil', '🏛️ Discover Seosun-ra-gil! \n\nSeosun-ra-gil is a picturesque route in Jongno-gu, celebrated for its blend of nature and literary history. This charming path invites visitors to explore the rich cultural heritage of Seoul while enjoying scenic views.\n\n📍 Location: Seosun-ra-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Hours: Open year-round, accessible at any time.\n\n💡 Tip: Bring a camera to capture the beautiful landscapes and historic sites along the way!', '2025-11-20 00:55:15'),
	(1120, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Itaewon Children\'s Park', '**모범택시2 - A must-visit for K-drama lovers! 🎬💜**\n\nThis enchanting location, Itaewon Children\'s Park, is featured in the popular drama "모범택시2." Fans can walk through the park and reminisce about their favorite scenes while surrounded by nature.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 287-1 Itaewon-dong, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 10-minute walk from Exit 2 of Noksapyeong Station.  \n\n \n\nFor the best photo opportunities, visit during the golden hour when the light is soft and magical! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:55:26'),
	(1121, 3, NULL, 'tell me about In front of Ediya Nakwon-dong branch', '**언젠가는 슬기로울 전공의생활 - A must-visit for K-drama fans! 🎬💜**\n\nThis vibrant location features iconic scenes where the main characters stroll together, capturing the essence of youth and city life. It\'s a fantastic spot to soak in the charm of Seoul while reliving your favorite moments from the series! \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 436-1, Samil-daero, Jongno-gu, Seoul\n\n• Access: Just a 3-minute walk from Exit 5 of Jongno 3-ga Station.\n\n  \n\n**Fan tip for photos/timing:** Visit during the golden hour for stunning photos that capture the lively atmosphere! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:55:26'),
	(1122, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Near Seodaemun Station', '🎬✨ 언젠가는 슬기로울 전공의생활 - a K-drama that captures the heart! \n\nThis drama features stunning scenes filmed near Seodaemun Station, where modern and traditional Seoul meet beautifully. Fans will love exploring the vibrant area that inspired many memorable moments in the show. \n\nHow to get there: \n\n• Address: 99 Songwol-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul \n\n• Access: The area is easily accessible via Seodaemun Station, making it perfect for a day of exploration.\n\nFor the best photos, visit during the evening to capture the breathtaking sunset. 📺💜 Enjoy the charm of the location while reminiscing about your favorite scenes!', '2025-11-20 00:55:37'),
	(1123, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Sogang Bridge', '🏛️ **Discover Sogang Bridge!**\n\nSogang Bridge is an iconic structure that beautifully connects two bustling districts in Seoul. Its modern design and vibrant atmosphere make it a popular spot for both locals and tourists.\n\n📍 **Location:** Sogang Bridge is located in the Mapo District of Seoul. \n\n⏰ **Hours:** The bridge is open year-round for pedestrians and cyclists.\n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Visit during sunset for stunning views of the Han River and the city skyline!', '2025-11-20 00:55:39'),
	(1124, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Four cuts of life. Yeonnam Branch', '🎬 Dive into the world of "다 이루어질지니"! \n\nThis charming location features iconic scenes that truly capture the essence of K-drama magic. It\'s the perfect backdrop for fans to recreate their favorite moments.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 34, Yanghwa-ro 23-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 2-minute walk from Exit 3 of Hongdae Station!\n\n📺 For the best photos, visit during golden hour when the light is just right. Capture those precious memories with friends in the various themed photo zones! 💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:55:46'),
	(1125, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Parking lot of Konkuk Building', '🚖✨ **Model Taxi 2 - A Must-Visit for K-Drama Fans!** \n\nThe parking lot of the Konkuk Building is a key filming location for "Model Taxi 2." It\'s the backdrop for some of the most intense and memorable scenes that keep viewers on the edge of their seats! \n\nHow to get there: \n\n• Address: 17, Insa-dong 4-gil, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 4-minute walk from Exit 5 of Jongno 5-ga Station.  \n\n📸💜 **Fan Tip:** Capture the essence of your favorite scenes by taking photos here! The unique atmosphere of the parking lot will make your memories even more special.', '2025-11-20 00:55:49'),
	(1126, 3, NULL, 'tell me about No, Parc', '🏛️ **No, Parc - A Hidden Gem in Seoul!**\n\nThis unique park blends nature and art, offering visitors a tranquil escape from the bustling city. With beautiful landscapes and artistic installations, it’s a perfect spot for relaxation and inspiration.\n\n📍 **Location:** No, Parc is located in the heart of Seoul, making it easily accessible for locals and tourists alike.  \n\n⏰ **Hours:** Open daily from 9 AM to 9 PM.  \n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Visit during the early morning or late afternoon for a peaceful experience and beautiful lighting for photos.', '2025-11-20 00:56:02'),
	(1127, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Gyeongbokgung Palace', '🏛️ Discover the Majesty of Gyeongbokgung Palace!  \n\nGyeongbokgung Palace is the first and largest royal palace from the Joseon Dynasty, built in 1395. It symbolizes the sovereignty of the dynasty and is the most significant among the Five Grand Palaces.  \n\n📍 **Location:** 161, Sajik-ro, Jongno-gu, Seoul, 03045  \n\n⏰ **Hours:**  \n- January & February: 09:00 - 17:00  \n- March - May: 09:00 - 18:00  \n- June - August: 09:00 - 18:30  \n- September & October: 09:00 - 18:00  \n- November & December: 09:00 - 17:00  \n\n*Last entry is one hour before closing.*  \n\n💡 **Tip:** Don\'t miss the changing of the guard ceremony for a glimpse into Korea\'s royal history!  ', '2025-11-20 00:56:13'),
	(1128, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Around Gwanghwamun', '🏛️ Explore the Charm of Gwanghwamun!\n\nGwanghwamun Square is a historical gem that showcases Korea\'s rich past. It features stunning monuments and is surrounded by significant landmarks from the Joseon Dynasty.\n\n📍 Location: 03172 B 175, Sejong-daero, Jongno-gu, Seoul, Korea  \n⏰ Open: 24 hours a day, throughout the year\n\n💡 Helpful Tip: Visit during the evening to see the square beautifully illuminated, enhancing its historical significance and atmosphere.', '2025-11-20 00:56:24'),
	(1129, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Korea University of Foreign Studies', 'Korea University of Foreign Studies - A Gateway to Global Communication! 🌍\n\nFounded in 1954, Korea University of Foreign Studies (KUFS) specializes in foreign languages and international studies. It is renowned for its diverse programs and emphasis on cultural understanding.\n\n📍 Location: 107, Imun-ro, Dongdaemun-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Hours: Typically open on weekdays, but hours may vary by department.\n\n💡 Helpful Tip: Check their website for language courses and cultural events that often welcome visitors!', '2025-11-20 00:56:25'),
	(1130, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Blue Show Pasta Yeonnam', '**언젠가는 슬기로울 전공의생활 - A K-drama fan\'s paradise! 🎬💜**\n\nBlue Show Pasta Yeonnam is featured in memorable scenes of the drama, making it a must-visit for fans. With its enchanting ambiance, you can almost feel the warmth of the characters\' moments.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 46, Seongmisan-ro 23-gil, Mapo-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 15-minute walk from Exit 3 of Hongik University Station  \n\n  \n\nFor the best photos, visit during golden hour when the warm lights create a magical atmosphere! 📺✨', '2025-11-20 00:56:34'),
	(1131, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Lotte World.', '🏛️ **Welcome to Lotte World Tower!**  \n\nLotte World Tower is a stunning architectural marvel that merges modernity with tradition. Standing at 555m tall, it boasts Korea\'s highest observation deck, Seoul Sky, offering breathtaking views.  \n\n📍 **Location:** 05551 300, Olympic-ro (Sincheon-dong), Songpa-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ **Hours:** Please refer to the website for detailed hours.  \n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Don\'t miss visiting Signiel Seoul, Korea\'s newest luxury hotel located within the tower!  ', '2025-11-20 00:56:44'),
	(1132, 3, NULL, 'tell me about University of Seoul', '🏛️ Welcome to the University of Seoul!  \n\nThe University of Seoul is renowned for its commitment to academic excellence and urban studies. Established in 1918, it has a rich history and diverse programs that cater to a wide range of disciplines.  \n\n📍 Location: 163, Seoulsiripdaegyo-ro, Dongdaemun-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ Hours: Typically open during weekdays, but check the university\'s official website for specific visiting times.  \n\n💡 Tip: Explore the campus and its beautiful green spaces for a refreshing break from your studies!  ', '2025-11-20 00:56:44'),
	(1133, 3, NULL, 'tell me about by the day of the week', '🎬 **"Ask the Stars" - A Must-Visit K-drama Location!** \n\nThe filming location "by the day of the week" is where some of the most emotional scenes in "Ask the Stars" were captured. The vibrant streets create a perfect backdrop, especially when illuminated at night!\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 520 Eonju-ro, Gangnam-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Easily reachable by subway or bus, making it convenient for K-drama fans!\n\nFor the best photos, visit during twilight to catch the beautiful night lights reflecting the drama\'s emotional vibe. 📺💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:56:53'),
	(1134, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Miwon Building', '🎬 Dive into the world of "대행사" (The Agency)! \n\nThis iconic Miwon Building serves as a stunning backdrop for many memorable scenes, showcasing the breathtaking skyline of Seoul. Fans can walk in the footsteps of their favorite characters and experience the vibrant city atmosphere.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 70 International Financial Road, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul\n\n• Access: It\'s just a 13-minute walk from Exit 5 of Yeouido Station!\n\nFor the best photos, visit during golden hour when the city lights start to twinkle—it\'s a K-drama dream come true! 📺💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:57:04'),
	(1135, 3, NULL, 'tell me about D-Life Style Kitchen Gwanghwamun Branch', '🎬 Welcome to the world of 대행사 (The Agency)! 📺💜\n\nThis vibrant spot, D-Life Style Kitchen Gwanghwamun Branch, is where some of the most memorable scenes from the drama were filmed, offering fans a taste of the on-screen magic. The modern interior and cozy atmosphere make it the perfect backdrop for drama lovers! ✨\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 136 Sejong-daero, Jung-gu, Seoul\n\n• Access: Just a 6-minute walk from Exit 5 of Gwanghwamun Station.\n\n \n\nFor the best photos, visit during golden hour to capture that dreamy café vibe! 📸💜', '2025-11-20 00:57:19'),
	(1136, 3, NULL, 'tell me about National Weather Museum', '[Discover the Flavors of Seasons at 기후! 🍽️]\n\nAt 기후, you’ll experience a unique omakase dining that showcases seasonal ingredients. Each visit promises a new menu that captures the essence of spring, summer, autumn, and winter.\n\nLocated at 04784 서울 성동구 성수이로 66, 서울숲드림타워 1층 106호, it\'s easily accessible for a delightful dining experience.\n\nMust-try:  \n• Seasonal sashimi  \n• Chef\'s signature seasonal dish  \n\nOne helpful tip: Make sure to book in advance, as the seasonal menus can get quite popular!', '2025-11-20 00:57:30'),
	(1137, 3, NULL, 'tell me about Maxim Bar', '[Maxim Bar - A Flavorful Journey Awaits! 🍔]\n\nMaxim Bar is your go-to spot for an unforgettable dining experience, offering a unique blend of flavors and vibrant atmosphere. You\'ll love the perfect combination of delicious food and lively ambiance, making it ideal for gatherings or casual outings. \n\nLocated conveniently in the heart of the city, Maxim Bar is easily accessible by public transport, ensuring a hassle-free visit.\n\nMust-try:  \n• Signature Burger  \n• Loaded Nachos  \n\nOne helpful tip: Don\'t forget to pair your meal with one of their refreshing craft beers for the ultimate experience!', '2025-11-20 00:57:39'),
	(1138, 3, NULL, 'reccommend all places the art of negotiation', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 00:58:04'),
	(1139, 3, NULL, 'tell me about In front of Yeondong Church', '🎬 Welcome to the world of "협상의 기술" (The Art of Negotiation) - a K-drama that captivates hearts! \n\nThe front of Yeondong Church serves as a stunning backdrop for some of the drama\'s most memorable scenes. This location beautifully blends the essence of the show with the vibrant urban landscape of Seoul. \n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 136-75 Yeonji-dong, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 4-minute walk from Exit 2 of Jongno 5-ga Station! \n\nFor the best photos, visit during golden hour for that perfect lighting and to capture the magic of the drama! 📺💜✨', '2025-11-20 00:58:11'),
	(1140, 8, NULL, ' reccommend all places Let\'s carry Sunjae and run', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 00:58:30'),
	(1141, 8, NULL, 'tell me about an iron-clad man', '🏛️ **Discover the Iron-Clad Man!**\n\nThe Iron-Clad Man is a fascinating figure known for his incredible resilience and strength, often depicted in literature and folklore. His stories typically revolve around themes of bravery and endurance against overwhelming odds. \n\n📍 **Location:** ChoiManLin Museum, 02708 23, Solsaem-ro 7-gil, Seongbuk-gu, Seoul  \n\n⏰ **Hours:** Daily from 10:00 AM to 6:00 PM (Closed for exhibition preparation from July 1 to September 3)  \n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Visit the museum to explore the artistic world of Choi Man Lin, where you can find inspiration in resilience and creativity!', '2025-11-20 00:59:13'),
	(1142, 3, NULL, 'reccommend top 10 be completely taken in', 'Yo! Hunters! 🔥💫 엄선한 10개의 전설적인 장소들이야! 각 장소마다 특별한 빛의 에너지가 있으니까 직접 체크해봐! 궁금한 곳 있으면 말해줘! Let\'s explore! 🌙✨', '2025-11-20 01:05:43'),
	(1143, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Shinsegae Department Store', '🎬 Welcome to the world of "Motel California"! 📺\n\nThis vibrant location is a must-visit for K-drama fans, as it features iconic scenes from the show. The blend of modern architecture and rich shopping experiences makes it a unique spot to explore. \n\nHow to get there: \n\n• Address: 77 Toegye-ro, Jung-gu, Seoul  \n\n• Access: Just a 4-minute walk from Exit 5 of Myeong-dong Station  \n\n \n\n✨ For the best photo opportunities, visit in the evening when the colorful lights and decorations shine bright! 💜', '2025-11-20 01:06:02'),
	(1144, 8, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ **N Seoul Tower at Night - A Stunning Experience!**\n\nN Seoul Tower is a must-visit landmark in Seoul, offering breathtaking views, especially at night. The tower is not only famous for its panoramic vistas but also for its romantic "locks of love" tradition. \n\n📍 **Location:** 04340 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** 10:00-22:30  \n\n💡 **Tip:** Arrive just before sunset to witness the city transform as the lights come on!', '2025-11-20 01:17:18'),
	(1145, 8, NULL, 'Recommend random attaraction top 10 places', '🎬 Amazing! I found 10 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 01:17:22'),
	(1146, 8, NULL, 'tell me about malli-dong or tell me about Samcheongdong', '🏛️ **Discover Samcheongdong!**\n\nSamcheongdong is Seoul\'s most stylish neighborhood, known for its artistic vibe and beautiful surroundings. The name "Samcheong" reflects the area\'s fresh and pure essence, attracting countless artists over the years.\n\n📍 **Location:** 110-260 Gahoe-dong, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** Please check local listings for specific hours.\n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Explore the charming streets and galleries to fully appreciate the artistic spirit of Samcheongdong!', '2025-11-20 01:17:38'),
	(1147, 8, NULL, 'reccommend all places model texi 2', '🎬 Amazing! I found 20 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 01:17:42'),
	(1148, 8, NULL, 'tell me about Yeouido Marriott Hotel Sauna Locker', '🎬 Welcome to the world of "Model Taxi 2"! 📺💜\n\nThe Yeouido Marriott Hotel Sauna Locker is a key filming location that captures the essence of the drama. Its elegant interior and cozy atmosphere make it a must-visit for fans wanting to immerse themselves in the show\'s vibe.\n\nHow to get there:\n\n• Address: 8, Yeouido-daero, Yeongdeungpo-gu, Seoul  \n• Access: Just an 11-minute walk from Exit 1 of Yeouido Station!\n\nFor the best photos, visit during quieter hours to capture the serene ambiance and enjoy a moment of relaxation after your sauna experience! ✨', '2025-11-20 01:18:13'),
	(1149, 8, NULL, 'Introduce N Seoul Tower at Night', '🏛️ **N Seoul Tower at Night - A Magical Experience!**\n\nN Seoul Tower is one of Seoul\'s most iconic landmarks, offering breathtaking views, especially after sunset. The night panorama is simply stunning, making it a must-visit for anyone in the city.\n\n📍 **Location:** 105, Namsangongwon-gil, Yongsan-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** 10:00 AM - 10:30 PM\n\n💡 **Tip:** Don\'t forget to check out the locks of love on Namsan\'s iron railings, a romantic tradition for couples!', '2025-11-20 01:19:53'),
	(1150, 8, NULL, 'Recommend random attaraction top 10 places', '🎬 Amazing! I found 10 filming locations from this drama! Each place has its own special story. Tap any location card below for detailed information! 💕✨', '2025-11-20 01:19:56'),
	(1151, 8, NULL, 'tell me about malli-dong or tell me about Samcheongdong', '🏛️ **Discover Samcheongdong!**\n\nSamcheongdong is Seoul\'s most stylish neighborhood, known for its artistic vibe and beautiful scenery. With its name meaning "three fresh" or "pure," this area attracts many artists due to its picturesque environment. \n\n📍 **Location:** 110-260 Gahoe-dong, Jongno-gu, Seoul  \n⏰ **Hours:** Check local listings for the most accurate information. \n\n💡 **Helpful Tip:** Stroll along the stone wall-lined street past Gyeongbokgung Palace for stunning views and charming cafes!', '2025-11-20 01:20:08'),
